{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 sh -c 'sed -n \\\"222,285p\\\" contract/scripts/README.md; rg -n \\\"\"'^def |add_argument|REQUIRED|VERDICT|check_research_work\" contract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py contract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"## Submission\n\nSave the independent report and primary receipts before cross-reading. Receipts can be\nplain text: command/URL, repository, full object SHA/version, capture time, exit/HTTP\nresult and raw output. Preserve failed probes. Hash the receipts and keep original\noutputs immutable; corrections are new attempts linked to their originals.\n\nWrite report text and structured records with file patches or a script that serializes\ndata from files. Do not interpolate source quotations or whole JSON documents into\nnested shell command strings. After a quoting/write failure, inspect the actual files\nand diagnostics before continuing; a later successful check does not erase that failure.\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict <case.json>\npython3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict --repo <clone-dir> <case.json>\n```\n\nUse the frozen gate code and retain both outputs. The first checks structure; the second\nchecks commit quotes and parent links without fetching. Neither proves causal truth,\natomicity, absent AI use or web disclosure scope. Retain a failed local check with its\nalternative primary evidence or explicit research gap; never invent a value for `ok`.\nPrefer local Git and patch/raw/PR sources; avoid API calls while rate-limited.\n\nReject duplicate JSON keys and unfinished drafts. A crash, timeout, rate limit or empty\nresponse belongs in execution errors; resume within the assigned limits. Do not turn\nit into a researched gap or completed independent audit. An actual EVIDENCE_GAP names\nthe evidence sought, bounded probes/results and the next decisive question.\nSubmission, research acceptance and publication are separate states in the batch index.\n\nFor new batches adopting the research-work sidecar introduced in `2026-09-25.1`, bind the schema's\n[research-work contract](../docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md#research-work-contract) and invoke the\nreduction gate with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`. Its `research_work.worklist`\nincludes unfinished qualified conclusions as well as unresolved ones. Review\n`unassessed_cases` and the actual findings before treating an empty list as a handoff.\nBefore sealing an auditor sidecar, validate it with the frozen `check_research_work`\nand verify its receipt hashes. The leader checks each supplied sidecar before relying\non its work states; an invalid sidecar remains unassessed. Keep the independent\nsidecars with their sealed reports; the reduction gate validates the adjudicator's\nrecorded work, not the completeness of source discovery. Frozen old\nbatches continue using their pinned commands and contracts.\n\nComparison/reduction lane and accepted arguments accept exact record files or\nrecords-only directories. Use the original `record.json` for a one-case task; for a\nbatch, bind a complete view whose record bytes match the sealed originals. The directory\nloader recursively parses JSON, so source-response arrays, receipts and scratch checkouts\nbelong outside that view. Keep every manifest case and assigned lane, and retain the\noriginal reports and evidence for research and decision pins. A packaging retry preserves\nthe failed invocation and is not a fresh independent research attempt.\n\nA pass that changes accepted records after their decision digest exists is diagnostic until\nit ships a fresh `audit_reduction_gate.py` receipt for the changed bytes; the\nearlier digest and the earlier pin set are historical from that moment.\n\nHandoffs identify the case/task/attempt, owned report and record paths, decisive receipts,\nexact check commands/results (including failures or checks not run), and any unresolved\nquestion with its next owner. Auditors give the leader sealed independent outputs for\nrouting; adjudicators also supply final decisions and the reduction-gate receipt for\nall assigned lanes. Put gate output and decision-file hashes outside the frozen files.\nDo not narrow the manifest or omit missing/failed lanes to obtain PASS. A worker's\ncompleted command, sealed submission or accepted research grants no claim-release,\nledger or publication authority; the leader continues only to the authorized endpoint.\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:15:from audit_record_gates import AI_VERDICTS, check_record, check_record_strict, load_record, review_signals\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:25:def text(value) -> bool:\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:29:def check_research_work(research, label, receipt):\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:113:def digest(path: Path) -> str:\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:117:def manifest_ids(path: Path) -> set[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:131:def check_delivery(manifest: Path, accepted: Path, decisions: Path,\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:217:            errors, dimension_counts, pending, limited = check_research_work(\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:262:        if any(text(r.get('verdict')) and r['verdict'] in AI_VERDICTS for r in all_records):\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:322:def main() -> int:\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:325:        parser.add_argument('--' + name, required=True, type=Path)\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:326:    parser.add_argument('--lane', action='append', help='NAME=PATH; repeat for all assigned auditors')\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:327:    parser.add_argument('--a', type=Path, help='legacy input named a')\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:328:    parser.add_argument('--b', type=Path, help='legacy input named b')\ncontract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py:329:    parser.add_argument('--research-contract', choices=[RESEARCH_CONTRACT],\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:34:AI_VERDICTS = {\"AI_ROOT_CAUSE\", \"AI_CODE_FLAWED\", \"AI_CAUSAL_CONTRIBUTOR\"}\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:35:CLOSED = {\"NOT_AI\", \"FALSE_POSITIVE\"} | AI_VERDICTS\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:129:def judgment_text(record: dict) -> str:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:140:def denied_around(text: str, start: int, end: int) -> bool:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:148:def claimed_disclosure(text: str) -> str:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:157:def residual_denied(record: dict) -> bool:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:180:def official_ids(record: dict) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:189:def sha_list(value) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:201:def check_record(record: dict) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:270:def check_jsonl(path: Path) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:274:def check_record_strict(record: dict) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:406:    if state == \"PRESENT\" and verdict not in AI_VERDICTS and not need(\"ai_admissibility\"):\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:423:    if verdict in AI_VERDICTS and ai_on_bic is not True and bic_marker != \"PRESENT\":\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:541:    if verdict not in AI_VERDICTS and not need(\"ai_admissibility\"):\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:552:def review_signals(record: dict) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:569:        and verdict not in AI_VERDICTS\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:592:def load_record(text: str) -> dict:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:608:def check_git_evidence(record: dict, repo: Path) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:688:def check_text(text: str, strict: bool = False, repo: Path | None = None) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:701:def check_path(path: Path, strict: bool = False, repo: Path | None = None) -> list[str]:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:717:def main() -> int:\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:719:    parser.add_argument(\"paths\", nargs=\"*\", type=Path)\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:720:    parser.add_argument(\"--stdin\", action=\"store_true\")\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:721:    parser.add_argument(\"--repo\", type=Path, help=\"verify commit marker quotes and parent links in this local clone (no fetch)\")\ncontract/scripts/audit_record_gates.py:722:    parser.add_argument(\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
