arameter rules as its JSON equivalent. Set\n`general_settings.allow_client_side_credentials`, or the deployment's\n`configurable_clientside_auth_params`, to keep passing these. PARENTS ['fc4be70a3714d442c1e30353336f2f9cdb6df662']\ne5effcb8619a22c4e739a20a453d674ee1b35edb fix(health)!: let configured deployment parameters win over request overrides\n\nWhen a connection test names a model that resolves to a configured deployment,\nthat deployment's routing and credential parameters are authoritative. A request\nsupplying a complete connection of its own is unaffected.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: /health/test_connection no longer lets a request replace the\nrouting or credential parameters of a configured model it names. Supply the full\nconnection parameters instead of naming a configured model. PARENTS ['5b2c92d7491fd9a9867db20d45a7fd08e5fb4b25']\nb468acb31c68b63584736f57a6f07f4fde2f8d6f fix(health): stop inheriting configured credentials when a connection test sets its own\n\nA request that supplies its own connection fields describes a connection of its\nown, so the configured deployment's credentials are no longer merged underneath\nit. Anything the request leaves unset still comes from the configuration, so\nnaming a configured model and testing it as configured is unchanged, and adding\na second deployment for an already-configured name works as before.\n\nReplaces the earlier outright rejection, which also refused requests that\nsupplied a complete connection of their own. PARENTS ['e5effcb8619a22c4e739a20a453d674ee1b35edb']\n59173c3a203daeeefe1b2b40d420166a38369d90 feat(health): let allow_client_side_credentials re-enable configured-credential reuse\n\nThe proxy-wide opt-in that already governs callers supplying their own\nconnection parameters now also governs whether a connection test may pair a\nrequest-supplied endpoint with the configured deployment's credentials. Off by\ndefault, which keeps configured credentials scoped to the endpoint the\nconfiguration names; on, the previous merge behaviour is available unchanged. PARENTS ['b468acb31c68b63584736f57a6f07f4fde2f8d6f']\n298fb8ce56099774f310594c9970cc24a9b8f900 fix(health): drop a stored-credential reference along with the credentials it names\n\nA connection test that redirects the destination already leaves the configured\ncredentials behind. It kept litellm_credential_name, which names the same stored\nsecrets and is resolved further down the call, so the reference is now dropped\nwith them. A request that sets no connection fields of its own is unaffected,\nwhich is how the Admin UI tests a configured model. PARENTS ['59173c3a203daeeefe1b2b40d420166a38369d90']\nDEFAULT main\nv1.96.2 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:09:16Z False\nv1.95.1 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:08:54Z False\nv1.91.5 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:07:47Z False\nv1.96.0 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-10T22:25:02Z False\nv1.94.3 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:08:39Z False\nv1.93.2 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:08:25Z False\nv1.92.2 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:08:11Z False\nv1.90.7 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:07:29Z False\nv1.89.7 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:07:11Z False\nv1.88.6 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-11T22:06:08Z False\nv1.96.0-rc.1 litellm_internal_staging 2026-08-03T19:18:02Z True\nv1.96.0-dev.2 litellm_internal_staging 2026-07-31T06:46:18Z True\nv1.96.0-dev.1 litellm_internal_staging 2026-07-31T00:30:50Z True\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
