alled health checking but did not contain that deployment inheritance logic. Receipts: `health-origin.json`, `health-origin-parent.py`, `health-origin-child.py`, `health-root.json`.\n+4. AI-marked `0d4875dec978e7b458336e943b89c31efa92a4a2`, parent `934ecdca78daf7ec9514efd47df77bf7495c822d`, adds nested embedding-config validation but also repairs unrelated upstream polling URL checks and carries generated UI files. Follow-up `90fd791e0d4c794bd009ca0d84c558d9ff3d604a` replaces recursive validation with fixed single-level descent and changes hostname-error disclosure. These are multi-change objects. Their marker cannot be mechanically assigned to one omitted sibling or treated as proof of first introduction. The raw auth parent/child and both patches establish the inspected scope, while PR #26996'\"'s member table and bounded ref fetch did not expose a finer member for each logical change.\n+\n+The chain must still distinguish earlier origin, later exposure and incomplete remediation per actual consuming operation. There is no justified single atomic introducer covering all of these surfaces. Thus introducer_sha/bic_granularity are explicitly unknown in the record, while the observed objects remain in evidence.\n+\n+## AI participation\n+\n+The exact commit-local marker on both 0d4875d and 90fd791 is:\n+\n+> Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n+\n+It supports AI participation in those objects. It does not distinguish validation logic, polling repair, ancillary generated content, or review activity within the bundles. The current evidence has not bound an atomic flawed/exposing contribution to that marker. The later PR #36011 body identifies Cursor Bugbot review of head \"'`298fb8ce56099774f310594c9970cc24a9b8f900`; that is review-side evidence, not proof that an AI authored the defect or the repair.\n+\n+The local carrier scan enumerated **67,350 commit objects**, including objects not reachable from a ref, and compared exact auth_utils.py blobs for four candidates. It retained 1,426 matches and their full commit metadata. A follow-up transition scan distinguishes unchanged descendants from content-changing commits. Many unrelated later AI-authored commits carry an unchanged auth blob; those markers are not causally attributed to that earlier code. The selected transitions show the marker-free 32d/472/065/5818 objects and a backport, but this bounded exact-blob scan is not complete hunk coverage of every historical validator, every source path, or the 0d/90fd bundles. It cannot support a broad absence-of-AI conclusion. No NOT_AI verdict is made.\n+\n+## Repair members, integration and shipment\n+\n+PR #36011'\"'s actual six-member table separates path validation (\"'`fc4be70a3714d442c1e30353336f2f9cdb6df662`), bracket-form reconstruction (`5b2c92d7491fd9a9867db20d45a7fd08e5fb4b25`), an intermediate configured-parameter precedence policy (`e5effcb8619a22c4e739a20a453d674ee1b35edb`), credential filtering (`b468acb31c68b63584736f57a6f07f4fde2f8d6f`), explicit opt-in restoration (`59173c3a203daeeefe1b2b40d420166a38369d90`) and stored-reference removal (`298fb8ce56099774f310594c9970cc24a9b8f900`). These sequential prerequisites are not interchangeable landings of a single repair.\n+\n+`c898d341c02299cf2506d0d8e84cc67953043593` is the two-parent staging merge of that batch, with mainline parent aa1180c0 and head 298fb8ce. `473f72e63a9777d793fbbf57194d8ec4fb97bc1b` and `820f247a6abba55cd87d130bef7bba7be3b29d37` identify backports. Their messages do not establish atomicity. Repository metadata identifies **main**, not internal staging, as the default branch. Its first-parent log places the relevant integration at `714fff696aa7141e104a314d7f872757bdecf9c5`, parent `ead62528e607b9d8e61273def638799c9c3a69ba`. Raw parent/integration auth and health files exhibit the missing/present repair logic. This establishes an integration boundary for those inspected changes, not proof that this merge closes all reported mechanisms and residual modes. Accordingly no universal fix_sha is asserted in the structured record.\n+\n+Official release metadata identifies v1.88.6, v1.89.7, v1.90.7, v1.91.5, v1.92.2, v1.93.2, v1.94.3, v1.95.1 and v1.96.2 as non-prereleases published on August 11. It separately lists v1.96.0 and prereleases. Forty-five retained source files cover the five changed runtime paths across these nine tags. AST parsing and call-site indexing show the shared destination guard wired in common processing and image endpoints, bracket reconstruction in auth, and health credential filtering used by the endpoint in every inspected tag. v1.96.0 lacks the bracket reconstruction and health filtering. The AST receipt is an index to source comparisons, not a behavioral test or proof of arbitrary bypass resistance. The global/environment-key residual analysis is specifically bound to v1.96.2.\n+\n+## Limits, failures and next decisive work\n+\n+Unresolved primary questions are (a) a contribution-level source that separates and attributes the relevant flawed validator or exposure from the AI-marked multi-change objects, and (b) whether the health direct SDK path has an effective intervening policy preventing global/environment keys from following a caller-selected destination. The next owner is the leader/adjudicator. A full mocked non-network call-chain regression, with all product checks intact, can distinguish the competing residual explanations; no live target is needed. Further history at the actual body/form/path consumers is needed before extending the health-origin finding to the whole advisory. These are unfinished routes, not a claim that public evidence has been exhausted.\n+\n+Failures preserved: one initial fetch invocation failed in zsh before execution because an unquoted `?per_page=100` glob did not match; the quoted retry succeeded. A Git combined show failed on missing member 5818eb; a bounded PR-ref fetch recovered the member and the carrier scan read its metadata/tree. A later combined no-patch show returned partial metadata then failed on missing promisor object `140f1155e3a7ed9325e40930b92749c1e07cb60a`; public raw source/API snapshots supply the comparisons, but this is not silently called a successful local-object read. Tool-output truncations were handled by smaller targeted reads; underlying fetched bodies were retained in full. No source access denial or safety stop was bypassed.\n+\n+Strict record, local-object and research-sidecar checks and their exact outputs are retained under `checks/` and the evidence receipt directory. A local gate on unknown/null causal fields cannot validate unclaimed candidate parent links or prove research truth. Final hashes are in SEAL.json, which excludes itself. Runtime scratch and runner-final are outside the sealed payload. Delivery of these files is not research acceptance.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA output/alias-3389297662643f29363dbb4b/REPORT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
