## 7. Residual, flip condition and limits

`remaining_gap`: no known residual on the default branch for the three closed mechanisms; the
caller-visible behavior stays default-closed while the two documented admin opt-ins
(`allow_client_side_credentials`, `configurable_clientside_auth_params`) intentionally re-open
clientside override, which is by design and not a defect. The only qualified surface is
binary/tag containment on the 1.95.x/1.96.x lines, which I did not re-derive locally.

`flip_condition`: the verdict would change if (a) the introducing `_NESTED_METADATA_KEYS` change were
shown to be human-authored rather than carrying the Claude trailer (=> downgrade of `ai_on_bic`), or
(b) the advisory were shown to target only the human health-check credential-merge surface without the
denylist/nested bypass (=> NOT_AI with the AI change as unrelated hardening), or (c) a further open
bypass of these controls were demonstrated on a released line (=> residual / BLOCKED).

Limits/failures: `git log -S` pickaxe over the blobless clone was abandoned (lazy-fetch blow-up); I
used tree-only path history plus binary-searched blob reads and the GitHub API instead. Local Git
