{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc 'numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 cat sealed-auditors/auditor2/REPORT.md'","aggregated_output":"# Auditor report - alias-28f8ceffd7fbb625211260b2\n\nTask: incremental-causal-20261004-case-043 / auditor2, independent attempt 1.\nLeader/handoff recipient: incremental-causal-20261004T081300Z-lead. Endpoint: research handoff.\nProtocol 2026-09-27.3, causal-work-v1. Source coverage cutoff 2026-10-04T08:13:00Z.\nRepository lead (advisory-designated): jelmer/dulwich. Class: alias-28f8ceffd7fbb625211260b2.\n\n## Advisory status (step 0)\nKeyed advisory GHSA-8W8G-WQ8H-FQ33, `type: reviewed`, `withdrawn_at: null`,\n`published_at: 2026-10-02T18:53:35Z`, no CVE alias. Disposition ACTIVE (advances to\nmechanism work). Vulnerable range `>= 0.24.0, <= 1.2.7`; `first_patched_version 1.2.8`.\nMechanism (CWE-59/CWE-61): symlink write-through in `porcelain.checkout(paths=[...])`.\nAdvisory credits `manus-use` (reporter) and `jelmer` (remediation_developer); prose says\n\"Reported by zx (Jace)\". The NEWS credit was later corrected to \"zx (Jace) and Houlton\nMcGuinn\" (commit f06d6b89, PR #2269). Evidence: inputs/00-github.json (retained).\n\n## Mechanism (step 1) - confirmed at the affected revision\n`porcelain.checkout` gained a `paths=` branch in commit a83ac1e7. That branch resolved a\ntree path, then wrote the blob with\n`os.fdopen(os.open(file_path, os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREAT|os.O_TRUNC, mode), \"wb\")`.\n`os.open` without `O_NOFOLLOW` follows a symlink already present at the target, so a\nrepository whose work tree leaves e.g. `trigger` as a symlink to `../../.git/hooks/post-checkout`\ngets attacker content written to that destination when checkout restores a regular file at\n`trigger` from a tag. It also left the file mode to the tree entry. Preconditions: victim\nruns `porcelain.checkout(repo, target=<ref>, paths=[...])` in a work tree that already\ncontains the attacker symlink. Counterevidence/limits: the sibling `reset_file` path already\nused `build_file_from_blob`; only this branch did not. Evidence: 01-bic-and-fix.txt.\n\n## BIC / landing (step 2)\n`introducer_sha` = a83ac1e7e3258c0a663f229ddb9fb9007642b60e\n(\"Add LFS support to porcelain layer\"), parent 1711d50fa57580741ab9239cbd31688bb034148e,\nauthor Jelmer Vernooĳ <jelmer@jelmer.uk>, 2025-07-11. The immediate parent has no `paths`\nbranch in `checkout`; a83ac1e7 adds the `paths` parameter and the raw-write hunk\n(`@@ -3097,6 +3096,77 @@ def checkout`). `bic_granularity` ATOMIC: the causal hunk is the\nlogically atomic addition; the surrounding LFS porcelain additions are the carrier commit.\na83ac1e7 is directly on the default branch (single parent on `main`), so\n`landing_basis` = INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT and `landing_commit` = null. First release carrying\nit: dulwich-0.24.0 (tag 2025-08-01), matching the advisory's `>= 0.24.0`. A PR-twin\n2fd4b52d carries the same content (different parent); it is a carrier, not a member.\nEvidence: 01-bic-and-fix.txt, 02-repair-and-versions.txt.\n\n## Repair / release (step 3)\n`fix_sha` = 9389fcb5cb9113adfc7f207d8be86a56904db3e8 (Jelmer Vernooĳ, 2026-07-02),\n\"checkout: write blobs via build_file_from_blob for path-restricted checkout\". It replaces\nthe raw `os.open` with `build_file_from_blob(obj, mode, file_path)` and adds the\n`stat.S_ISLNK` arm. `build_file_from_blob` (hardened by d09f8af, PR #2259) removes a\nsymlink left at the target and writes a fresh regular file, and canonicalizes the mode.\n`fix_granularity` ATOMIC. Reachability: merged to `main` via 9995d077 (PR #2268) and shipped\nin dulwich-1.2.8 (tag 2026-07-05). The advisory also names symlinks at intermediate\ndirectories; at the fix parent `_checked_worktree_path` only ran `validate_path`\n(name-only). The intermediate-directory variant was closed two days later by the companion\nhardening 2ed5853e (#2278, `verify_leading_dirs`), which is also contained in 1.2.8. No\nreleased version exists in the gap: 1.2.8 is the first patched release and contains both\nhunks. `remaining_gap` = null (no open surface at 1.2.8). Evidence: 02-repair-and-versions.txt.\n\n## AI participation (step 4)\nNo admissible AI evidence binds the causal change. The BIC object a83ac1e7 is authored and\ncommitted by a recovered named human, Jelmer Vernooĳ <jelmer@jelmer.uk>; `identity_class` =\nHUMAN. The commit object and its message carry no AI trailer/agent author/disclosure\n(ai_marker ABSENT); the same holds for the fix object 9389fcb (fix_ai_marker ABSENT).\nThe repository does document Claude Code tooling at the BIC date (CLAUDE.md, 2025-05-16;\n\"Add more claude hints\", 2025-06-24), so `disclosure_convention` = POLICY_MENTIONS_AI;\nthat is repository-level activity and is NOT admissible to attribute this change (see\n`ai_admissibility`). The reporter/contributor identities in the retained material\n(manus-use; zx/Jace; Houlton McGuinn; Kartik Kenchi <netliomax25@gmail.com>) are\ndiscovery/repair-side people, not introducers. `ai_on_bic` = false. Evidence:\n03-ai-and-credit.txt.\n\n## Verdict and residual questions\nverdict NOT_AI: the defect's introducing change is human-authored, no admissible AI marker\nexists on any inspected carrier, and the repair is human-authored. This is a research\nfinding, not self-acceptance.\nUnresolved decisive questions: (1) no first-party PR/security-advisory body for #2268 or the\nreport was captured within the fixed window, so an AI disclosure living only there was not\ninspected; (2) `manus-use`'s identity (agent vs human account) is not resolved by the\nretained capture and does not change the causal verdict either way.\nFlip condition: a first-party disclosure or commit-local marker binding AI to a83ac1e7 (or\nto the incomplete coverage of the intermediate-directory variant before 2ed5853e) would\nmove `ai_on_bic`/verdict; conversely, capture of the named reporter/contributor identities\nas human would only harden NOT_AI.\n\n## Checks run / not run\nRecord structure and repo-object checks and the research-work reduction gate are recorded in\nevidence and SEAL.json. Checks that could not run are qualified there; no check result was\naltered to obtain PASS.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
