ust 1.85 and moved the crate to Rust 2024\nedition.</li>\n<li>Added a Hunt-style diff implementation exposed as\n<code>Algorithm::Hunt</code>.</li>\n<li>Added configurable inline refinement via\n<code>InlineChangeOptions</code> and\n<code>InlineChangeMode</code>, including semantic cleanup and new\n<code>TextDiff::iter_inline_changes_with_options*</code> methods. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/issues/92\">#92</a></li>\n<li>Added a global disjoint-input fast path in\n<code>algorithms::diff_deadline</code>\nto avoid pathological runtimes on large, fully distinct inputs.</li>\n<li>Improved <code>Algorithm::Myers</code> performance on heavily\nunbalanced diffs to\navoid pathological slowdowns.</li>\n<li>Added <code>diff_deadline_raw</code> entrypoints in the algorithm\nmodules to bypass\nshared heuristics and keep minimal intrinsic trait bounds where\nneeded.</li>\n<li>Added test files in <code>examples/diffs</code> that can be used\nwith the some of the\nexamples as input pairs.</li>\n<li>Added <code>CachedLookup</code>, a helper for adapting virtual or\ncomputed sequences by\nmaterializing items on first access and then serving borrowed values\nthrough\nnormal indexing. The <code>owned-lookup</code> example demonstrates this\napproach for\nissue <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/issues/33\">#33</a>.</li>\n<li>Fixed ranged indexing in the classic LCS table algorithm.</li>\n<li>Improved diff compaction to merge adjacent delete hunks across equal\nruns.</li>\n<li>Excluded development scripts from published crate contents. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/issues/87\">#87</a></li>\n<li><code>TextDiff::from_*</code> and\n<code>TextDiffConfig::diff_*</code> now accept owned inputs\n(<code>String</code>, <code>Vec&lt;u8&gt;</code>, <code>Cow</code>) in\naddition to borrowed inputs. This allows\nreturning text diffs from functions without external owner lifetimes. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/issues/65\">#65</a></li>\n<li><code>TextDiff</code> no longer exposes <code>old_slices</code> /\n<code>new_slices</code>. Use\n<code>old_len</code>, <code>new_len</code>, <code>old_slice</code>,\n<code>new_slice</code>, <code>iter_old_slices</code>,\n<code>iter_new_slices</code>, <code>old_lookup</code>, and\n<code>new_lookup</code> instead.</li>\n<li><code>TextDiff::iter_changes</code> now panics on invalid\nout-of-bounds <code>DiffOp</code>\nranges instead of silently truncating iteration.</li>\n<li><code>utils::diff_lines_inline</code> now takes\n<code>&amp;TextDiff</code> and options rather than\n<code>(Algorithm, old, new, options)</code>.</li>\n<li><code>utils::diff_lines</code> now avoids a second line-tokenization\npass.</li>\n<li>Renamed <code>get_diff_ratio</code> to <code>diff_ratio</code>.</li>\n<li>Added first-class <code>no_std + alloc</code> support with an\nexplicit default <code>std</code>\nfeature.</li>\n<li>Added optional <code>hashbrown</code> backend for\n<code>no_std</code> map storage</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/commit/8ae2c3f15c0e20e4e5ef6c7f88a1c04942f8a76b\"><code>8ae2c3f</code></a>\nchore(release): prepare 3.1.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/commit/37dfae498e557190a60dc7f8b92189c10ef1f3a5\"><code>37dfae4</code></a>\nAdd <code>use</code> clause to iterator types for improved lifetime\nmanagement (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/issues/93\">#93</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/commit/6e321ade6bbff9ba81078a7e14c60d190be4e574\"><code>6e321ad</code></a>\nfeat(api): add capture_diff_slices_by_key</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mitsuhiko/similar/commit/d943be327889c0bb7aec1b1de89b8af496f776b8\"><code>d943be3</code></a>\nfeat: Added a float bucket example</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://