base\", \"--is-ancestor\", \"e673babfc11d0b4001d9d08b9b9cef57c6aa67f5\", \"a83ac1e7e3258c0a663f229ddb9fb9007642b60e\"] EXIT 1 STDERR \n254:COMMAND [\"git\", \"--no-replace-objects\", \"--git-dir=/home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/incremental-causal-20261004-case-043/adjudicator/workspace/retained-git/auditor1/01.git\", \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", \"e673babfc11d0b4001d9d08b9b9cef57c6aa67f5\", \"2fd4b52d984c00822cf6baf54dd9a8f17257f721\"] EXIT 0 STDERR \n256:CLOSURE 2ed5853e869a580eded4e6f63e02ed7555cf2705^1 ROUTED HELPER True LEADING GUARD False\n258:CLOSURE 2ed5853e869a580eded4e6f63e02ed7555cf2705 ROUTED HELPER True LEADING GUARD True\n260:CLOSURE 9389fcb5cb9113adfc7f207d8be86a56904db3e8 ROUTED HELPER True LEADING GUARD False\n1053:    def reset_index(\n1069:            build_index_from_tree,\n1087:        if config.get_boolean(b\"core\", b\"symlinks\", True):\n1088:            symlink_fn = symlink\n1091:            def symlink_fn(  # type: ignore[misc,unused-ignore]\n1102:        return build_index_from_tree(\n1109:            symlink_fn=symlink_fn,  # type: ignore[arg-type,unused-ignore]\n\nAt affected tag `dulwich-1.2.7` (`e076b16aa4ee77c18fbdb3d639cd037d76daee0b`), and at the cited fix's parent `f321a189f3f8fc94119556e30821925955af3ef7`, the public `checkout` function selects its path-specific branch when `paths is not None`. A caller supplies the paths and target tree/ref; strings become bytes, target defaults to HEAD, the tree resolves each path to a mode and object, and the object is required to be a Blob. It then calls `_checked_worktree_path`, creates leading directories, optionally applies configured smudge normalization, opens a regular-file path with `O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC`, and writes the blob's bytes. Index staging occurs afterwards. No permission check or symlink check is interposed between the name validator and the open. Source: [affected porcelain](evidence/affected-porcelain.stdout), [source comparisons](evidence/source-comparisons.stdout), [cited repair](evidence/fix.stdout).\n\nThe trust boundary is attacker-controlled repository tree/blob content and an existing worktree symlink being consumed with the local caller's filesystem authority. The protected resource is any reachable writable target outside the intended worktree file, including repository administrative files. Both a final-component symlink and a symlink in an existing leading directory redirect the open; `makedirs(..., exist_ok=True)` does not validate such an existing directory. Name validation excludes literal absolute paths and invalid components, but cannot constrain a symlink's destination. The raw write bypasses `build_file_from_blob` completely. Configured filters may change the bytes; an ordinary non-LFS blob with no transforming filter suffices for the static causal argument.\n\nActivation requires a nonempty chosen path, a regular blob in the source tree and a preexisting usable symlink at that destination or a parent, plus target filesystem write permission. Repository-controlled symlinks can be materialized in symlink-capable worktrees; the affected `build_file_from_blob` has an `S_ISLNK` branch that creates the link from blob content. A configuration/platform that materializes links as ordinary files does not, by that action alone, establish this precondition. An empty `paths=[]` iterates no files and causes no write despite the shorthand in the advisory title. The public API is the exposed product operation; the inspected CLI `cmd_checkout` does **not** pass a paths argument, so this report does not claim that a plain Dulwich CLI checkout invokes this branch.\n\ncapture_utc: 2026-10-04T16:58:43Z\n$ git merge-base --is-ancestor a83ac1e7 dulwich-1.2.7 ; git merge-base --is-ancestor 9389fcb dulwich-1.2.7 ; git merge-base --is-ancestor 9389fcb dulwich-1.2.8 ; git merge-base --is-ancestor 2ed5853e dulwich-1.2.8\na83ac1e7 in 1.2.7=YES\n9389fcb in 1.2.7=NO\n9389fcb in 1.2.8=YES\n2ed5853e in 1.2.8=YES\n\n$ tag dates\n2025-08-01 00:43:48 +0100 release 0.24.0\n2026-06-12 11:58:01 +0100 Release 1.2.7\n2026-07-05 16:17:48 +0100 Release 1.2.8\n\n$ git show f321a189:dulwich/porcelain/__init__.py | sed -n '/def _checked_worktree_path/,/return os.path.join/p'\ndef _checked_worktree_path(repo: \"Repo\", tree_path: bytes) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"Resolve a working-tree path, refusing anything that escapes the repo.\n\n    ``checkout``, ``restore`` and ``reset_file`` write files at caller-supplied\n    paths. Those paths are normally trusted, but validating them as a matter of\n    defense in depth keeps a stray ``../`` or ``.git`` component from writing\n    outside the work tree or into the control directory, matching the bar git\n    applies to its own path operands.\n\n    Args:\n      repo: Repository the path is relative to.\n      tree_path: Path in tree form (``/``-separated), as produced by\n        ``_fs_to_tree_path``.\n\n    Returns:\n      The filesystem path under the repository root, as bytes.\n\n    Raises:\n      Error: If the path is absolute or carries a component the configured\n        ``core.protectNTFS``/``core.protectHFS`` validator rejects.\n    \"\"\"\n    from ..index import get_path_element_validator, validate_path\n\n    # Tree paths always use \"/\" as the separator; a leading \"/\" or \"\\\\\" would\n    # make os.path.join discard the repository root, so treat it as absolute.\n    if tree_path.startswith((b\"/\", b\"\\\\\")):\n        raise Error(f\"refusing to write path outside repository: {tree_path!r}\")\n    validator = get_path_element_validator(repo.get_config_stack())\n    if not validate_path(tree_path, validator):\n        raise Error(f\"refusing to write unsafe path: {tree_path!r}\")\n    return os.path.join(os.fsencode(repo.path), tree_path)\n\n$ git show 2ed5853e --stat + verify_leading_dirs presence at 1.2.8\n2ed5853e869a580eded4e6f63e02ed7555cf2705 Jelmer Vernooij <jelmer@jelmer.uk> 2026-07-05 16:44:34 +0200 porcelain: reject writes through intermediate symlink in checkout paths (#2278)\n\n NEWS                          |  6 +++++\n dulwich/index.py              | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n dulwich/porcelain/__init__.py | 27 +++++++++++++++++----\n dulwich/stash.py              | 50 ++-------------------------------------\n tests/porcelain/__init__.py   | 55 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 5 files changed, 138 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)\n2184:def verify_leading_dirs(\n\n$ NEWS 1.2.8 security entry (fix commit)\n * SECURITY: Canonicalize file modes to ``0o644``/``0o755`` before ``chmod``\n   on checkout and patch apply, matching git. An untrusted tree entry or\n   patch ``new file mode`` could otherwise set setuid/setgid/sticky or\n   world-writable bits on a materialized file. (netliomax25-code)\n\n * SECURITY(GHSA-8w8g-wq8h-fq33): Write files through ``build_file_from_blob``\n   in path-restricted ``porcelain.checkout(paths=...)`` instead of a raw\n   ``os.open``. The old path followed a symlink left at the target, so a\n   crafted repository could write attacker content outside the work tree\n   (e.g. into ``.git/hooks``) on ``checkout``. (reported by zx (Jace),\n   Jelmer Vernooĳ)\n\n1.2.6\t2026-05-31\n\n * SECURITY: Honor ``core.protectNTFS``/``core.protectHFS`` on all\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
