quest branches and second init override at repair; positive finite redirect-count parity is a distinct question. Auditor2 inspected temporary /tmp/axfull Git which may not survive sandbox; preserve absence truthfully and use available retained primary objects, never fabricate a clone check. Reconcile v1.7.0 versus v1.10.0 source introduction and actual package bytes. No redirect server, network test, exploit, deployed target or installation of missing runtime to execute attack regressions. Existing runtime failure remains visible.\n# Radar audit report — alias-2a1ef1a8d7e0ad48955683d1\n\n- Case: alias-2a1ef1a8d7e0ad48955683d1 (attempt 1, auditor2)\n- Batch: incremental-causal-20261004-case-044\n- Advisory cluster: GHSA-r4gj-5m52-g5wh / CVE-2026-101907\n- Protocol: 2026-09-27.3; research-work contract: causal-work-v1\n- Coverage cutoff: 2026-10-04T08:13:00Z\n- Endpoint: research handoff only (leader `incremental-causal-20261004T081300Z-lead`)\n- Verdict: **NOT_AI** (human-origin defect; no AI marker on the causal object)\n\n## 0. Advisory status (Step 0)\n\nBoth identifiers are live, not excluded.\n\n- `GHSA-r4gj-5m52-g5wh` (retained `inputs/00-github.json`): `type: reviewed`, `published_at`\n  `2026-09-30T15:31:58Z`, `withdrawn_at: null` → GitHub global-advisory format maps to **ACTIVE**.\n- `CVE-2026-101907` (retained `inputs/01-nvd.json`): `published` `2026-09-28T18:17:19Z`,\n  `vulnStatus: Awaiting Analysis`, `cveTags: []` → published, not rejected/withdrawn → **ACTIVE**.\n- `advisory_disposition` is reported for the keyed entry `advisory_ids[0] = GHSA-r4gj-5m52-g5wh`.\n  The CVE is an alias of the same vulnerability, not a duplicate advisory.\n- No `REJECTED`/`WITHDRAWN`/`DUPLICATE` state exists, so no false-positive ground applies.\n\n## 1. Reported behavior and mechanism (Step 1)\n\nClaim: with `maxRedirects: 0` (the documented redirect-based SSRF guard) the Node/fetch\nadapter ignores the option and the Fetch API default `redirect: 'follow'` applies, so a\nredirect is followed despite the caller's guard.\n\nObserved at the vulnerable revision immediately before the fix (`v1.19.0`,\n`lib/adapters/fetch.js`): the adapter destructures fields from `resolveConfig(config)`\n(`url, method, data, signal, cancelToken, timeout, onDownloadProgress, onUploadProgress,\nresponseType, headers, withCredentials, fetchOptions, maxContentLength, maxBodyLength`) and\nbuilds `resolvedOptions` without a `redirect` key. `git log -S maxRedirects -- lib/adapters/fetch.js`\nreturns only the fix commit `d19040bd`; a tag scan (`v1.10.0, v1.16.1, v1.17.0, v1.18.1, v1.19.0`)\nfinds no `maxRedirects`/`redirect` reference in `lib/adapters/fetch.js`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
