dvisory's `>= 1.17.0` lower bound was not recovered\n  from a primary source; the source history directly contradicts it as the origin.\n- No exploit was executed and no live target was contacted; the mechanism was established by\n  source reading of the affected and parent revisions.\n{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-2a1ef1a8d7e0ad48955683d1\",\n  \"repo\": \"axios/axios\",\n  \"protocol_version\": \"2026-09-27.3\",\n  \"advisory_ids\": [\n    \"CVE-2026-101907\",\n    \"GHSA-r4gj-5m52-g5wh\"\n  ],\n  \"advisory_disposition\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"advisory_aliases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CVE-2026-101907\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GHSA-r4gj-5m52-g5wh\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verdict\": \"NOT_AI\",\n  \"introducer_sha\": \"1e5552ac0e3293b666c1b87cdebac7c455f93270\",\n  \"introducer_parent\": \"72c888c6b3d1be3c11932c81afa9f5418871357b\",\n  \"landing_commit\": \"a3ff99b59d8ec2ab5dd049e68c043617a4072e42\",\n  \"landing_basis\": \"PROSE_CARRIER_ON_DEFAULT\",\n  \"landing_note\": \"PR 6371 member recovered through its bounded head-ref fetch. Parent has no fetch adapter; child adds coherent fetch feature and dispatch. Member-to-landing diff at fetch.js, adapters.js and defaults/index.js preserves the exact request-construction/fetch causal hunk; differences concern capability, progress and FormData handling. The full blobs differ, so this is hunk identity, not whole-file identity.\",\n  \"bic_granularity\": \"SQUASH_DECOMPOSED\",\n  \"decomposed_shas\": [\n    \"1e5552ac0e3293b666c1b87cdebac7c455f93270\"\n  ],\n  \"decomposition_probe\": \"git --git-dir=output/axios.git fetch origin refs/pull/6371/head:refs/audit/6371 exited 0; PR member metadata and actual objects recovered. See intro-pr-ref.receipt.json, intro-member.raw and intro-content-identity.raw.\",\n  \"ai_on_bic\": false,\n  \"ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"ABSENT\",\n    \"sha\": \"1e5552ac0e3293b666c1b87cdebac7c455f93270\",\n    \"scope\": \"Introducing object and original causal hunk carriers; unrelated AI-marked descendants are individually retained and causally excluded.\"\n  },\n  \"identity_class\": \"human\",\n  \"disclosure_convention\": \"CONVENTION_NOT_OBSERVED\",\n  \"ai_admissibility\": \"Named DigitalBrainJS/robotshara identity binds through the PR and Dmitriy Mozgovoy landed metadata. Inspected all 2382 local commits at the historical fetch path and full metadata of 650 broad omission carriers; unrelated descendant trailers do not attribute inherited code. HTTP sensitive-header AI assistance addresses a distinct invariant. Repair bot reviews and the August 2026 policy change do not attribute the April 2024 origin.\",\n  \"fix_sha\": \"d19040bda7a8be2f82c3c6e1a5bc03917daee39a\",\n  \"fix_parent\": \"e0a02dd16671deabe2b809334d4c2ebede29a233\",\n  \"fix_granularity\": \"CARRIER_BUNDLE\",\n  \"atomic_repair_sha\": null,\n  \"repair_members\": [\n    \"745160bc8a3cadf4180d0abccaf87aed8555485e\",\n    \"4bee948a922627f281d7c6ca8655245f38998630\"\n  ],\n  \"repair_note\": \"Redirect-only atomic commit not asserted: 745160b introduces the zero-to-manual hunk and removes second init; 4bee948 restores sanitized second init while forcing manual there too. Both are broader runtime changes. Minimum repairing logic is isolated at hunk level, and the final fetch file equals the default landing. repair_members are not alternate landings.\",\n  \"fix_ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"ABSENT\",\n    \"sha\": \"d19040bda7a8be2f82c3c6e1a5bc03917daee39a\",\n    \"scope\": \"No marker in inspected landing/member commit metadata; repair PR has bot review activity, not a demonstrated defect-generating contribution.\"\n  },\n  \"mechanism\": \"With numeric maxRedirects zero, affected fetch adapter ignores the option and supplies no redirect mode, so compliant Fetch follows redirects. Requires fetch adapter selection, attacker-controlled redirect source, target reachability and application reliance on this guard. Response data