6f6634c52f4fe116e33bf5f09**, authored by Dmitriy Mozgovoy at the same address. The original PR metadata identifies that landing.\n+\n+`member-landing-diff.raw` shows no registration/default differences and only progress scheduling, capability, and FormData changes in fetch.js. The constructor/call hunk and its omission are preserved although complete fetch blobs differ. Therefore BIC granularity is SQUASH_DECOMPOSED with the recovered member named, and landing_commit names the distinct squash. Auditor2'\"'s “single feature” assessment explains logical coherence but does not erase a reconstructable member. The repository is non-shallow; parent-path read failures here establish actual absent paths, not missing commits. Primary observations: commit-1e5552ac.raw, commit-72c888c6.raw, commit-a3ff99b5.raw, intro-tree.raw, intro-parent-tree.raw, fetch-1e5552ac.raw, member-landing-diff.raw and their receipts. Existing PR-ref recovery is retained through the original sealed receipts; no repeated recovery or alternate route around a denial was needed.\n+\n+## Contribution-specific AI assessment\n+\n+The introducing object's complete metadata has a named address/account and no AI author, trailer, or tool disclosure. Fifteen preceding commit messages and the source tree at the epoch provide the contemporaneous spot check: CONVENTION_NOT_OBSERVED. No marker-policy file at that epoch is used as proof of human-only authorship. The same address, original PR identity and landed metadata recover the identity binding rather than guessing from a display name.\n+\n+This adjudicator independently enumerated **2,382 physically retained commit objects**, including unreachable objects, read every full commit object and its historical fetch path, and retained **44 unique fetch blobs** and the path map. **650 commits** carry fetch source with no maxRedirects reference. These are a broad inherited-omission universe, not 650 separate introductions. Raw enumeration, batch metadata, path/blob reads, query lists and receipts are \"'`all-object-universe.*`, `all-commit-metadata.*`, `all-fetch-path-objects.*`, `carrier-path-map.json`, and `carrier-survey.json`. There is no claim to all deleted/public objects. The historical path is supported by follow-history back to its addition.\n+\n+A deliberately broad lexical scan produced 66 candidates across affected and repaired history. Focusing on omission carriers'\"' identities/messages yields 50 leads, including repository policies and non-causal mentions; these are **not 50 AI contributions**. Their full diffs and exact metadata are retained. Auditor2's empty reachable-history scan is contradicted by 696fa753c5366afbd21859c294c64c9ff2b359ab, whose trailer reads \"'`Co-authored-by: cubic-dev-ai[bot] <191113872+cubic-dev-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>`, and ef3711d1b3a3c1eb4f11dc43e8db38e9c5342448 with the same trailer. The former changes error objects after failure; the latter reformats fetch/dispatch/config code. Their before/after request policy does not introduce or repair numeric-zero following. An inherited causal blob/hunk on a marked descendant does not attribute its old authoring to that descendant.\n+\n+Other plausible counterexamples were examined: 6bb12c191f5380fad321322fb90216ae0dc36985 discloses Claude Sonnet 4.6 and cubic assistance, but its sensitiveHeaders code and documentation explicitly apply to Node HTTP redirects and exclude maxRedirects zero. FormData/header/cookie/prototype fixes alter different authority/data conditions. f2dc4495472071d3ed9a5637f35660226c8e44c6 has a Claude Opus 4.6 trailer and changes malformed scheme parsing; a valid initial URL under the same fetch selection remains affected before/after it. The recovered April fetch body/content limit members add size accounting, not redirect authorization. The URL-object support bundle 847d89b4 broadens accepted input representation and mentions cubic review: it normalizes URL objects to the same string path, and the aggregate review mention does not disclose AI authorship of the enabling hunk. Its existence neither dates this established string-input defect to 2026 nor supplies contribution-specific attribution of that exposure. All runtime-path leads preserve the already reachable valid string URL / numeric-zero omission under the stated conditions.\n+\n+Repair PR Greptile/cubic reviews are retained separately; they are activity on repair revisions, not evidence of defect creation. The August 2026 policy removal cannot establish an April 2024 attribution convention. Named origin, actual object metadata, contemporary spot check, and causal exclusion of inspected later markers support NOT_AI within the frozen threshold. A contribution-specific disclosure tied to an original or later exposing hunk would require a new attribution assessment.\n+\n+## Repair, both invocation branches, and residual\n+\n+First default-branch closure is **d19040bda7a8be2f82c3c6e1a5bc03917daee39a**, parent **e0a02dd16671deabe2b809334d4c2ebede29a233**. Official repository metadata names v1.x as default and the retained first-parent history contains the landing. The landing is a runtime-hardening bundle; atomic_repair_sha is null rather than an invented redirect-only commit.\n+\n+Member **745160bc8a3cadf4180d0abccaf87aed8555485e**, parent **2c94646eb7cb7ab9dcb2aefdb04ab1b040c28e16**, first reads maxRedirects, sets resolvedOptions.redirect to manual for numeric zero, and removes the second Request-init argument at the fetch call. Member **4bee948a922627f281d7c6ca8655245f38998630** restores sanitized second options and forces their redirect to manual too. Its fetch blob equals the default landing exactly. Both members are broader runtime changes, so repair identification is at hunk level within the recovered bundle sequence. Auditor2'\"'s “no member” claim inferred from default pickaxe alone fails against these actual objects; naming the carrier as atomic_repair_sha also misstates granularity.\n+\n+The guard executes before Request construction. On the Request branch, manual appears in both the constructed Request and any safe second init so caller follow cannot override it. With Request absent, \"'`_fetch(url, resolvedOptions)` receives manual directly. An absent fetchOptions value still leaves the constructed Request manual. Numeric-zero precedence also holds when fetchOptions explicitly asks to follow. A noncompliant custom fetch is outside this guard'\"'s guarantee. Manual browser responses may be opaque instead of the visible Node 3xx response. No zero-redirect residual is found in these branches; positive finite limits remain a distinct invariant. Primary observations: repair-chain.raw, repair-default-diff.raw, fetch-745160bc.raw, fetch-4bee948a.raw, fetch-d19040bd.raw, default-first-parent.raw, repair-members-diff.receipt.json (exit zero with empty raw diff), retained-repo-metadata.raw. Upstream regression source is inspected as source only.\n+\n+## Released and distributed content\n+\n+Official v1.7.0 is stable, published 2024-05-19T20:24:58Z. v1.6.8 has no fetch adapter. The v1.7.0 source and **actual npm 1.7.0 archive** contain the omission, disproving v1.10.0 as the first fetch source release and >=1.17.0 as the true lower boundary for this mechanism. The exact 1.7.0 registry version and its dist.tarball were retrieved here; SHA512 matches registry integrity and packaged fetch.js exactly equals the Git tag. The original failed/not-attempted routes are not rewritten by this added evidence. The publisher's reason for the advisory range is unknown; no motive or exhaustive semver range is fabricated.\n+\n+v1.19.0 tagged source and packaged code omit the guard. Stable v1.20.0, published 2026-08-24T13:40:40Z, contains d19040bd and the numeric-zero guard. The retained npm 1.19.0/1.20.0 archives were independently integrity-checked and read without extraction/execution. Packaged fetch.js equals each source tag. Node CJS, browser CJS, UMD source, and ESM source bundles were inspected and exhibit the same omission/guard change. These strengthen shipment beyond tagged ancestry. \"'`package-verification.json` binds every inspected member hash and request excerpt; tarball and registry receipts preserve original retrieval identity/date. Minified variants, every CDN build, and deployments are outside that observed artifact scope; no assertion that every uploaded asset was tested is made.\n+\n+## Failures, work state, and delivery\n+\n+Original auditor1 failures remain visible: obsolete singular test-path lookup and absent Git dist-member reads exited 128; corrected test source and registry archive inspection answered the unaffected source/shipment questions. The original optional runtime check could not launch because node was absent (initial FileNotFoundError and later exit-127 receipt). This adjudicator'\"'s \"'`numactl ... node --version` also failed (exit 1 from numactl, missing executable); no runtime was installed, redirect server run, operational payload created, exploit executed, or deployed target contacted. Source and normative semantics support the finding without a passing runtime test. Missing cgroup paths in the original environment inspection were not source denials or assignment-wide safety stops. There is no recorded source denial that this work rerouted.\n+\n+An exploratory read guessed carrier_scan.py instead of the retained carriers.py and failed with sed'\"'s missing-file diagnostic; no evidence claim depends on it. The enclosing grouped shell exited zero, so its successful exit is not presented as a successful file read. The correct available files were located afterward, and the independent scanner above was written in owned output.\n+\n+Both original records pass frozen strict and relevant local-object checks using the available retained primary objects. Their research objects have six structurally COMPLETE dimensions and matching evidence hashes. Auditor1 references an empty successful member diff directly; under the reduction gate's stricter nonempty-receipt callback this creates two receipt flags. This is an input packaging qualification, not absent member evidence: its original nonempty command receipt exists, and the independent successful comparison is retained here as a nonempty receipt. Original bytes remain unchanged. Auditor2's old temporary-clone check cannot be recreated from its own assigned retention; local object corroboration from the available retained repository is explicitly distinguished.\n+\n+\"'`research.json` records six supported findings, actual decisive observations, and their receipt hashes. The execution failures are separate from decisive source questions. `record.json` is derived after this report. `output/decisions.json` binds both exact original records, accepted bytes, full reports/sidecars/seals, manifest, brief, contract and gate code, and per-dimension resolutions including input quality and residual. Strict record checks, local-object checks, research/hash checks, and the frozen full-N reduction gate are saved without changing findings to satisfy a check. Readback must agree before sealing. The case SEAL.json excludes itself; decisions are sealed separately outside their payload. runtime-home and runner-final remain outside the sealed case.\n+\n+The adjudicator proposes ACCEPTED research within these explicit conditions; leader acceptance, ledger state, and publication remain separate. The flip condition is primary contribution-specific AI evidence, an earlier causal origin, previously enforcing affected source, or contradictory package/repair bytes. No unresolved decisive question is handed off as completed work; the leader receives the bounded finding and preserved execution/input qualifications.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA output/alias-2a1ef1a8d7e0ad48955683d1/REPORT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
