R #201) escaped `userinfo`,\n`query` and `fragment` but left the port path untouched. Host-delimiter escaping\n(`reescapeHostDelimiters`, `6c86c17`, later `9da8b0a`) is also human. The port injection\nis independently exploitable at the origin, so the atomic introducing change is the\norigin, not the later hardening.\n\n## 3. Repair and release\n`fix_sha` = `820e8478dd7da3d09f187bfaf35d50b71f67b8b4`, the first mechanism-closing\nchange on the default branch: it adds `isPort = /^\\d*$/u` and rejects any non-digit\nport in `recomposeAuthority` with `TypeError('URI port is malformed.')`, plus the\nregression test. Single-parent signed commit on `main` (parent `e0081523…`); `main`\nHEAD `a2b6779` contains it. Other landings of the same repair (backports):\n`9f4c943e…` (v3.x, #216) and `812bd8e2…` (v2.x, #215), both cherry-picking `820e847`.\nReleased scope verified by tag content, not ancestry alone:\n- v4.1.3 vulnerable (line 773) → v4.1.4 fixed (`isPort` guard); tags containing 820e847: v4.1.4, v4.1.5, v4.2.0, v4.2.1.\n- v3.1.6 vulnerable → v3.1.7 fixed.\n- v2.4.5 vulnerable → v2.4.6 fixed.\nThis matches the advisory's 2.4.6 / 3.1.7 / 4.1.4 fixed versions.\n\n## 4. AI participation\nNo AI marker sits on any object carrying the causal content. Enumerated all 287 local\ncommit objects; the ONLY non-dependabot AI marker is\n`0542a216860fd70c062a4730e620576f62ded057` (`Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8\n<noreply@anthropic.com>`), whose content is the literal-backslash host-confusion fix\n(GHSA-v39h-62p7-jpjc / GHSA-4c8g-83qw-93j6), a different vulnerability. The BIC\n`30aba8c` and its sibling carrier `3f9f9d9` are authored by a recovered named human,\nVincent LE GOFF <vince.legoff@gmail.com> (`identity_class: human`), with no AI trailer\nor disclosure. The fix and both backports are by Matteo Collina (human), no marker.\nBounded PR-ref probe fetched refs/pull/{201,210..217}/head: no fetched fork head carries\nthe port fix with an AI marker; PR #201 head confirms `62a776e`'s