b5821051a27; no smaller original member was exposed. See origin-history-probe and object-coverage receipts.\",\n  \"ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"ABSENT\",\n    \"sha\": \"9a5bef783fad507aed02242ce726f89640bf42d1\",\n    \"source\": \"commit\",\n    \"scope\": \"Inspected bundle metadata only; atomic member provenance is unresolved.\"\n  },\n  \"ai_admissibility\": \"PR132/133 first-party text discloses Claude assistance for heads 7bef527a0a186248a13c9c084a40d5c012b1be8d and 44c774a36f094532dc0d73c56d1350cb323aefc0. Both closed unmerged, differ from shipped iterative code and have no demonstrated product landing/content identity. Admissible for those proposed length-limit diffs only, not the BIC, shipped incomplete nesting remediation, or final depth repair. Repository .claude ignores are not hunk attribution.\",\n  \"identity_class\": \"human\",\n  \"disclosure_convention\": \"CONVENTION_NOT_OBSERVED\",\n  \"fix_sha\": \"935d78f32f335b2ff76578e5c5e877d31ae9888c\",\n  \"fix_parent\": \"df7682f386cdf2d7fef6067bc78ed70d824e1f3f\",\n  \"fix_granularity\": \"ATOMIC\",\n  \"fix_shas\": [\n    \"1efee7c397c191da6287a78ec19512476a966a7b\",\n    \"1ba3c71f89fb3448c8be6dcf2d17b543c2738f16\",\n    \"de84f144e9816f30e25fc8179e2e1249ab6df0db\"\n  ],\n  \"fix_ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"ABSENT\",\n    \"sha\": \"935d78f32f335b2ff76578e5c5e877d31ae9888c\",\n    \"source\": \"commit\"\n  },\n  \"mechanism\": \"Exported expand accepts a caller-controlled pattern; nested comma members and single-part sets recurse before output accounting, retaining native frames without a depth budget. An uncaught RangeError can terminate the embedding Node process. Remote unauthenticated reachability depends on the consumer and was not established for a deployed application.\",\n  \"fix_reasoning\": \"The direct main-first-parent change initializes depth=0 at the actual caller, applies depth > maxDepth before parsing and increments at both nested call sites. Default maxDepth=1000 bounds the