tions: the caller passes untrusted input to expand() directly or through minimatch/glob; no extra role, configuration, session or transaction state is required. Counterevidence: chained-input recursion on m.post was already made iterative by the earlier CVE-2026-14257 fix and parseCommaParts recursion by GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p, so those payload shapes do not establish this defect; the surviving two nesting sites are confirmed by the repair patch.\",\n  \"mechanisms\": [\"uncontrolled recursion on nested brace groups causing native stack exhaustion (CWE-674/CWE-400), denial of service\"],\n  \"mechanism\": \"uncontrolled recursion on nested brace groups causing native stack exhaustion (CWE-674/CWE-400), denial of service\",\n  \"bug_semantics\": \"expand_() recurses on nesting depth, but max and maxLength bound only output size, so recursion depth is unbounded up to native stack limits.\",\n  \"flaw_origin\": \"Recursive expansion implementation first shipped in commit 9a5bef783fad507aed02242ce726f89640bf42d1 (ready for first publish, Julian Gruber, 2013-10-13); the comma-member and tail recursive calls are already present there, while the initial commit 3624453f42ebf1d5fda9247ec4f87b5821051a27 has a non-recursive expand.\",\n  \"introducer_sha\": \"9a5bef783fad507aed02242ce726f89640bf42d1\",\n  \"introducer_parent\": \"3624453f42ebf1d5fda9247ec4f87b5821051a27\",\n  \"bic_granularity\": \"ATOMIC\",\n  \"bic_minimality\": \"The causal hunk is the recursive expand() body itself; its immediate parent 3624453f42eb carries a non-recursive expand, and the child 9a5bef783fad adds recursion. It is the earliest observable boundary (project first publish), not a member of a bundle.\",\n  \"bic_note\": \"9a5bef783fad is the atomic content-introducing change for the nested recursion; it is a direct single-parent commit and the earliest observable boundary for this implementation, so no pre-import origin is inferred.\",\n  \"landing_commit\": null,\n  \"landing_basis\": \"INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT\",\n  \"landing_note\": \"The introducer is itself a direct commit on the mainline with no separate merge/squash carrier, so no landing object is named; this is a root/content boundary rather than a decomposed bundle.\",\n  \"decomposed_shas\": [],\n  \"decomposition_probe\": \"GitHub commits API path=index.js per_page=10 pages 1-3 (evidence/idx-1.json, evidence/idx-2.json, evidence/idx-3.json): the oldest commit touching index.js is 3624453f42eb (initial commit), then 9a5bef783fad (ready for first publish), which already contains the recursive calls. Raw blob reads confirm non-recursive parent versus recursive child.\",\n  \"fix_sha\": \"935d78f32f335b2ff76578e5c5e877d31ae9888c\",\n  \"direct_fix_sha\": \"935d78f32f335b2ff76578e5c5e877d31ae9888c\",\n  \"fix_granularity\": \"ATOMIC\",\n  \"fix_shas\": [\"1efee7c397c191da6287a78ec19512476a966a7b\", \"de84f144e9816f30e25fc8179e2e1249ab6df0db\"],\n  \"fix_note\": \"935d78f32f335b2ff76578e5c5e877d31ae9888c is the mechanism-closing change on default branch main (parent df7682f386cdf2d7fef6067bc78ed70d824e1f3f, the 5.0.10 tree, src/index.ts). It threads maxDepth (EXPANSION_MAX_DEPTH=1000) into expand_ and returns a group literally past the cap, bounding both recursion sites. 1efee7c397c191da6287a78ec19512476a966a7b (parent tree 1.1.19) and de84f144e9816f30e25fc8179e2e1249ab6df0db (parent tree 3.0.7) are the other branch landings of the same repair, released as 1.1.20 and 3.0.8. Released tarball content for 5.0.11, 3.0.8, 2.1.6 and 1.1.20 contains maxDepth; 5.0.9 and 1.1.18 do not.\",\n  \"remaining_gap\": \"The 2.1.6 backport commit object is not among the advisory's three referenced SHAs and is not pinned in this record, although 2.1.6 release content contains the maxDepth fix. Full local-object carrier enumeration and --repo verification were also not run because no local clone was provisioned; they do not affect the origin or repair conclusions but would complete marker-coverage.\",\n  \"flip_condition\": \