separable bundle and root parent; no constituent member. This does not establish absence of private history.\",\n          \"evidence\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/object-coverage.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"53dcc3abaabb60714a5805023a5e3a06df349b931abc0a9a9a08e4296e240b88\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/origin-prs.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"8869cd59639bff21453e416f7d63a601f14be43cb370a14e3f248db608f81a12\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/origin-history-probe.receipt.json\",\n              \"sha256\": \"24e27db622602358c83238e11085425ab8487f5f8bbcf7051d2380967446e698\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/origin-history-probe.stderr\",\n              \"sha256\": \"a5810ac4d1aace52123af417bfeb78e53dbdcf6e6ca9b3a7a60e121e96e71c3c\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/origins.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"14b9bb03721466f2590dac07df3a7bf9b1f3abac01b4b240390d6a1f307470e0\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"disclosed-proposal-landing\",\n          \"question\": \"Do the first-party Claude disclosures bind to shipped code carrying this nesting defect?\",\n          \"source\": \"upstream PR132/133 records, fetched heads and product history\",\n          \"evidence_type\": \"proposal metadata and source/landing comparison\",\n          \"status\": \"ANSWERED\",\n          \"observation\": \"Both closed unmerged; heads absent from product branch ancestry and proposed recursive-tail length fixes differ from the shipped iterative algorithm. Disclosures are not attribution for the case BIC.\",\n          \"evidence\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/ai-backport-132.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"71980c1777ca58a1d645a6499e4014b74e6eab38bc855bb1ca0001a90c6d9a8c\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/ai-backport-133.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"e91771b5e14f6c3e7957188930bf007ccd20e74f44fafb73f4da9eaaa0107a84\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/ai-backport-diffs.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"3c67fd31891063dfcaa5932c5a79638e4742fd8f86502b87b5d1392c8a36c597\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"evidence/causal-comparisons.stdout\",\n              \"sha256\": \"c21e1236272da03ec90f796be94ecaeb1c22b257e0139c28fba657d0447fb43f\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"fix\": {\n      \"evidence_grade\": \"BOUND\",\n      \"work_state\": \"COMPLETE\",\n      \"finding\": \"The direct main-first-parent change initializes depth=0 at the actual caller, applies depth > maxDepth before parsing and increments at both nested call sites. Default maxDepth=1000 bounds the recursive chain; literal truncation preserves shallow semantics by inspection. Deliberately excessive, Infinity or NaN option values are outside this finite-default claim. No deep-stack test was run. The object directly follows the affected release on main first-parent history; v1/v2/v3 other landings carry equivalent depth wiring.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/main-repair.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"2ef58b00078ce2e22abb3d080958fab07fcf3f7e8fd57e0787ad84e8c73fceb1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/causal-comparisons.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"c21e1236272da03ec90f796be94ecaeb1c22b257e0139c28fba657d0447fb43f\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/source-set.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"51fdc926eb0939852664665d3117fc9ccd5ee47f759b4400803915cc545f38bd\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"missing_fact\": null,\n      \"next_permitted_route\": null,\n      \"routes\": []\n    },\n    \"versions\": {\n      \"evidence_grade\": \"BOUND\",\n      \"work_state\": \"COMPLETE\",\n      \"finding\": \"Publisher npm metadata, actual tarballs and export wiring establish the depth guard in four claimed fixed stable versions and its absence in inspected preceding releases. Actual tags resolve to metadata gitHeads. All publication times precede cutoff; metadata was captured retrospectively. Entire broad advisory ranges were not exhaustively tested.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/releases.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"7883b045ab24f89e8793a4a5e8f1da805a1db82708fda4faa1c578e97c30909e\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/npm.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"c78bc17243cec6af7436c61c812d28ceeb6be811449fe522eb960423991b06ae\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/release-content.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"bdc2fd5422e5bbd06c0d01cb0926454d56acc7ef2c35420aba530bab6b895e29\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"evidence/causal-comparisons.stdout\",\n          \"sha256\": \"c21e1236272da03ec90f796be94ecaeb1c22b257e0139c28fba657d0447fb43f\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"missing_fact\": null,\n      \"next_permitted_route\": null,\n      \"routes\": []\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
