{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 sh -c 'sed -n \\\"230,298p\\\" contract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py; sed -n \\\"290,339p\\\" contract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md; cat sealed-auditors/auditor1/SEAL.json | head -c 1800; cat sealed-auditors/auditor2/SEAL.json | head -c 1800; sed -n \\\"72,115p\\\" contract/docs/AUDIT-PROTOCOL.md'\"","aggregated_output":"            continue\n        inputs = {name: snapshots[name][0][cid] for name in paths}\n        final = snapshots['accepted'][0][cid]\n        bound = decision.get('sha256')\n        if not isinstance(bound, dict) or set(bound) != set(roots):\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: digest bindings must include exactly all auditor inputs and accepted')\n        for name, (records, hashes) in snapshots.items():\n            if records[cid].get('class_id') != cid:\n                problems.append(f'{cid}: {name} record needs its explicit class_id')\n            if not text(records[cid].get('verdict')):\n                problems.append(f'{cid}: {name} verdict must be a nonempty string')\n            if not isinstance(bound, dict) or bound.get(name) != hashes[cid]:\n                problems.append(f'{cid}: {name} digest missing or changed since adjudication')\n        problems.extend(check_record(final) + check_record_strict(final))\n        status = decision.get('status')\n        counts[str(status)] += 1\n        if status == 'BLOCKED':\n            if not text(decision.get('next_question')):\n                problems.append(f'{cid}: BLOCKED needs the next decisive question')\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: research remains BLOCKED')\n        elif status != 'ACCEPTED':\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: status must be ACCEPTED or BLOCKED')\n        elif final.get('verdict') in ('EVIDENCE_GAP', 'BLOCKED'):\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: an open verdict cannot be research ACCEPTED')\n        if not text(decision.get('basis')):\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: needs the reducer\\'s whole-chain acceptance basis')\n        reviewed = decision.get('reviewed_dimensions')\n        if not isinstance(reviewed, list) or set(map(str, reviewed)) != set(RESEARCH_FIELDS):\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: explicitly review every research dimension')\n        required = set(research_differences_many({**inputs, 'accepted': final}))\n        all_records = [*inputs.values(), final]\n        # Agreement does not waive primary-evidence scrutiny on publication-sensitive claims.\n        if any(text(r.get('verdict')) and r['verdict'] in AI_VERDICTS for r in all_records):\n            required.update(('bic', 'ai', 'fix'))\n        if any(review_signals(r) for r in all_records):\n            required.add('residual')\n        if any(check_record(r) + check_record_strict(r) for r in inputs.values()):\n            required.add('input_quality')\n        resolutions = decision.get('resolutions')\n        if not isinstance(resolutions, dict):\n            resolutions = {}\n        if contract == RESEARCH_CONTRACT:\n            required.update(resolutions)\n        for dimension in sorted(required):\n            resolution = resolutions.get(dimension)\n            if contract == RESEARCH_CONTRACT:\n                if not isinstance(resolution, dict):\n                    problems.append(f'{cid}: unresolved {dimension}; needs structured claims, observation, reasoning and conclusion')\n                    continue\n                claims = resolution.get('claims')\n                if not isinstance(claims, dict) or set(claims) != set(paths) or not all(text(v) for v in claims.values()):\n                    problems.append(f'{cid}: {dimension} claims must account for every assigned lane')\n                for key in ('observation', 'reasoning', 'conclusion'):\n                    if not text(resolution.get(key)):\n                        problems.append(f'{cid}: {dimension} resolution needs {key}')\n                if not isinstance(resolution.get('evidence'), list) or not resolution['evidence']:\n                    problems.append(f'{cid}: {dimension} resolution needs primary receipts')\n                else:\n                    for item in resolution['evidence']:\n                        receipt(item, f'{cid} {dimension} resolution evidence')\n            elif not text(resolution):\n                problems.append(f'{cid}: unresolved {dimension}; explain the competing readings and evidence')\n        evidence = decision.get('evidence')\n        if not isinstance(evidence, list) or not evidence:\n            problems.append(f'{cid}: retain primary evidence receipts')\n        else:\n            for item in evidence:\n                receipt(item, f'{cid} evidence')\n\nNew batches adopting the current contract retain the sidecar introduced in\n`2026-09-25.1`: set `reduction.research_contract` to\n`causal-work-v1` and freeze the gate invocation with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`.\nThe option rejects an omitted or different declaration; older frozen batches retain\ntheir existing contract. This is local coordination data, never ledger or site data.\n\nEach decision has a `research` object with `advisory`, `mechanism`, `bic`, `ai`, `fix`\nand `versions` entries. Auditors keep the same object in their owned research sidecar,\nlinked from the sealed report; adjudicators write their own synthesis in the decision.\nThe existing `basis`, `residual` resolution and per-dimension `missing_fact` describe\nthe remaining uncertainty. A single entry has this shape (not a prewritten finding):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"evidence_grade\": \"QUALIFIED_BOUNDARY\",\n  \"work_state\": \"UNFINISHED\",\n  \"finding\": \"State the supported causal conclusion, conditions and counterevidence.\",\n  \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"evidence/source.txt\", \"sha256\": \"<64 hex>\"}],\n  \"missing_fact\": \"State the decisive fact still unknown.\",\n  \"next_permitted_route\": \"original-member\",\n  \"routes\": [{\n    \"id\": \"original-member\",\n    \"question\": \"Which parent/child change first introduced the relevant behavior?\",\n    \"source\": \"upstream repository history\",\n    \"evidence_type\": \"parent/child source comparison\",\n    \"status\": \"PENDING\"\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n`evidence_grade` is `BOUND`, `QUALIFIED_BOUNDARY` or `UNRESOLVED`. It describes the\nsupported conclusion, independently of work remaining. `BOUND` need not assert a\nvulnerability or an existing fix: an affirmative refutation or the keyed advisory's\ndocumented exclusion of further work can support a scoped conclusion. State that scope;\ndo not invent code findings for a rejected advisory or extend an absence claim.\nA `BOUND` finding has no decisive `missing_fact`: represent it with JSON null, not an\nempty string. Genuine remaining gaps use the other evidence grades and a named fact.\n\n`work_state` is `UNFINISHED` while an identified, permitted, decisive investigation\nremains, regardless of the grade or case verdict. `next_permitted_route` names a\n`PENDING` or `FAILED` route. `COMPLETE` requires a null next route and no unfinished\nroute; a non-BOUND conclusion also needs a nonempty `missing_fact` and route history.\nCompletion is the researcher's claim about the recorded questions and evidence available\nat that point, not proof that every possible source was discovered. Omitted or invalid\nresearch objects are unassessed, never zero outstanding work.\n\nA route is a question plus an authoritative source and evidence type. Alternate URLs\nfor the same observation are attempts within that route, not extra research coverage.\nChoose routes for the facts they can distinguish; after a decisive answer, do not keep\nsearching merely to fill source categories. If a planned alternative becomes redundant,\n{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-31b59d85d0a2e70df260e6c1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"incremental-causal-20261004-case-046-auditor1\",\n  \"task_binding\": \"190563ccf16248883c84909fab8c1c29c7ea0437de7e571d9d30411170cd9f0f\",\n  \"sealed_at\": \"2026-10-04T17:53:51.027576+00:00\",\n  \"algorithm\": \"sha256\",\n  \"excluded\": [\n    \"SEAL.json\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"REPORT.md\",\n      \"bytes\": 18542,\n      \"sha256\": \"40d1f0b36d57a609243479cf70d134ab4ceca9d4f4617c3c8cc4ddd02518ab1e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/00-github.json\",\n      \"bytes\": 8201,\n      \"sha256\": \"4b9ecc19637da305f04714a0ef4d7a30ba679ca0e68a136185867b16763d3055\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/01-nvd.json\",\n      \"bytes\": 3976,\n      \"sha256\": \"e26d52b0b104bba084d0c64ed4b94378e84a985b6d4e2e184d1f57952c5c8b2c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/030a0f89a118dd1f3331526cbf121e0d705433e9-index.js\",\n      \"bytes\": 3561,\n      \"sha256\": \"43fe1d3474a0cf0ebe6a70867ca601d900272acfb13d7f9d5f5f44b4134fde23\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/030a0f89a118dd1f3331526cbf121e0d705433e9-parent-index.js\",\n      \"bytes\": 2847,\n      \"sha256\": \"d3d77e56b36a713f0fe8a7cfce40382e71ccf61413c78d14b000a47a15c7a99c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/1ba3c71f89fb3448c8be6dcf2d17b543c2738f16-index.js\",\n      \"bytes\": 11375,\n      \"sha256\": \"e3d453a435c12c53364714757208a53859ed02d9b1444853be728fb5d785f081\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/1ba3c71f89fb3448c8be6dcf2d17b543c2738f16-parent-index.js\",\n      \"bytes\": 10314,\n      \"sha256\": \"4089a7acabfcc6de673f54094f1bf96977ab7cc01b7b490bc978ef63dd9a6847\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/1efee7c397c191da6287a78ec19512476a966a7b-index.js\",\n      \"bytes\": 13387,\n      \"sha256\": \"8ab93974fc9a4eede1868557f69a181fe9d2a87cdaa54b7294a8a8516fe906dc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/1efee7{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-31b59d85d0a2e70df260e6c1\",\n  \"task\": \"incremental-causal-20261004-case-046\",\n  \"role\": \"auditor2\",\n  \"attempt\": 1,\n  \"protocol\": \"2026-09-27.3\",\n  \"research_contract\": \"causal-work-v1\",\n  \"coverage_cutoff\": \"2026-10-04T08:13:00Z\",\n  \"excludes\": [\n    \"SEAL.json\",\n    \"runtime-home/\",\n    \"runner-final/\"\n  ],\n  \"file_count\": 109,\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"REPORT.md\",\n      \"sha256\": \"24044e33172425492c3cb572192de704c6ba36aad148c609da76fe0b501af036\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/commit-1efee7c397c191da6287a78ec19512476a966a7b.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"029abba4c2811a171aed8281fbdef70af625c4346fd11c8cb394f5449abc66b2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/commit-935d78f32f335b2ff76578e5c5e877d31ae9888c.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"b3a07260ec759d93216748581745b1570e746fb24881dc73890ae478570ff9d8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/commit-de84f144e9816f30e25fc8179e2e1249ab6df0db.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"a737a8b390395e241a516017823f4c4ec3303e52f93909accac921bc37f603dd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/h2.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"9db3e191284e5df6ce45272931e6a8333d34780fee165afcd4a613a6f174fd56\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/hdr.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"b0df974f5aaafdde750adc075340eaecdcceac3de417073f6ecc2618c5fb2bc0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/idx-1.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"c9b0382878706afd708bfca5809a67025bcf9fc5152a91ca47b1ef2f7482ac89\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/idx-2.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"6fae6db44a861b4e9db9fc9f0214dbfb782573591d59da510b0319a8ff95318e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/idx-3.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"4027b03cbd8daadf3ed6ca11a1918f43e16a1e849ff718b6b33b7ddc840f9b91\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/npm-registry.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d64701dc19c759f500c7db606ff5bef33cdc1061ef16e01db42549b202d2   Check shallow boundaries before treating a root or a failed ancestry walk as evidence.\n   Missing local objects are not proof that public history is unavailable: distinguish a\n   commit, its trees/blobs and the product repository from a reporter or umbrella clone.\n   Recover missing objects through one bounded authoritative probe in an owned scratch\n   clone, preserving shared read-only clones; retain its command and output. If the BIC\n   itself is unknown, use the explicit nulls allowed for open records by DATA-SCHEMA.\n\n3. **Fix:** the minimum repairing hunks/commit set and why it closes the defect; follow\n   partial repairs through the residual defect to closure; verify affected/fixed versions\n   separately, and substantiate an unpatched state plus a proposed repair when no fix exists.\n   `fix_sha` is the first mechanism-closing change on the default branch, not whichever\n   landing a lane named. If a side-branch repair reaches the default branch through a\n   merge, identify that integration and compare its default-branch parent with the merged\n   content. Later ancestry alone does not make the side-branch commit the default-branch\n   closure; retain its member and other landing roles separately. Fix-side AI is informational: it never substitutes for BIC-side\n   attribution, and a fix-side marker alone does not move the verdict. If the remediation is\n   partial, or a claimed patched release does not contain the fix, `remaining_gap` names the\n   still-open surface and its closing commit, or none.\n\n4. **AI:** tie AI evidence to causal changes across the history, within its disclosed scope,\n   and record how it was admitted (`ai_admissibility`): first establish that the named object\n   carries the causal change at the claimed granularity, then read its actual marker.\n   A first-party disclosure bound to that causal change is admissible once the\n   record says what binds it; repository-level AI activity, changelog habits, labels and org\n   policy are never admissible. A TP needs demonstrated AI contribution to the defect:\n   introduction, new exposure or incomplete remediation can qualify after a human BIC, and a\n   successful repair alone does not. `NOT_AI` needs