## Mechanism, accounting and counterevidence

At df7682f386cdf2d7fef6067bc78ed70d824e1f3f, the immediate pre-fix 5.0.10 source,
the exported expand escapes input, obtains max/maxLength, calls expand_, then
unescapes results. balanced-match separates brace groups; parseCommaParts and the
top-level tail loop are already iterative. The dependency's retained 4.0.2 source
uses an iterative scan with an array of positions, rather than recursive expansion.

Two nested paths remain: single-part sets call expand_ on the inner part before
mapping embrace; comma-member iteration calls expand_ before reading the returned
array and applying values.length/valuesLength checks. Frames and their string/parser
state and local arrays remain live until nested work returns. Nesting therefore grows
the in-flight frame chain with depth even where completed output stays small.
max limits kept output count and maxLength accounts for emitted/combined characters;
neither charges stack depth before descent. These budgets are not bounds on every
retained substring, parser position array, repeated scan or total CPU/heap use.
Repeated invocations release ordinary call state on return/unwind; a catch can limit
termination but supplies no parser work budget.

The root 3624453f42ebf1d5fda9247ec4f87b5821051a27 is not globally non-recursive:
expandBraces and expandRanges recurse on pre/post. Its exported expand has no direct
self-call, but auditor2's stronger "non-recursive implementation" inference is false.
The root splits the matched body without recursively expanding members. In the child
9a5bef, balanced matching retains nested member groups and the new
`concatMap(n, function(el) { return expand(el) })` descends into them. This identifies
the relevant nested-member transition independently of older tail recursion.
The 2014 refactor 030a0f89a118dd1f3331526cbf121e0d705433e9 adds the explicit
single-set rewrap shape; its parent already has member recursion. It explains the
modern call site rather than relocating the origin of nesting descent.

Earlier iterative-tail and comma-parser changes, output budgets and normal shallow
syntax are meaningful counterevidence to a claim that every recursive-looking or
malformed pattern has this mechanism. They do not remove these two nested calls.
Source inspection establishes the missing depth invariant. Advisory crash depths
and differential counts remain upstream observations, not reproduced measurements.

