{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 sh -c 'cat sealed-auditors/auditor1/record.json sealed-auditors/auditor2/record.json; cat additional-primary/*md additional-primary/SOURCES.json; cat /home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/.ai-slop/state/incremental-causal-20261004T081300Z/case-047/adjudicator-brief.txt; cat /home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/incremental-causal-20261004-case-047/manifest.txt'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-3389297662643f29363dbb4b\",\n  \"protocol_version\": \"2026-09-27.3\",\n  \"verdict\": \"EVIDENCE_GAP\",\n  \"advisory_ids\": [\n    \"GHSA-3cv6-jpf6-8222\",\n    \"CVE-2026-84377\"\n  ],\n  \"advisory_disposition\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"advisory_aliases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GHSA-3cv6-jpf6-8222\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CVE-2026-84377\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"introducer_sha\": null,\n  \"introducer_parent\": null,\n  \"landing_commit\": null,\n  \"landing_basis\": \"NO_LANDING_NAMED\",\n  \"landing_note\": \"Several distinct causal paths are grouped. Specific health config-inheritance origin 0e2fcde145e9ffb27812badbc314b1c6f2af74d9 is retained in evidence, not assigned as the atomic whole-cluster introducer.\",\n  \"bic_granularity\": null,\n  \"decomposed_shas\": [],\n  \"decomposition_probe\": \"Owned bounded PR-ref fetches for 34189, 36011, 30585 and 26996 succeeded. Member tables distinguish maintenance bundles but do not attribute each logical hunk. Exact commands and exits retained.\",\n  \"ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"UNKNOWN\"\n  },\n  \"fix_ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"UNKNOWN\"\n  },\n  \"ai_admissibility\": \"Claude co-author markers on 0d4875d and 90fd791 establish participation at bundled-object scope, not an attributed atomic defective hunk. Cursor Bugbot disclosure on PR36011 is review-side only. No fix-side disclosure is substituted for BIC attribution. Unrelated AI-authored descendants with an unchanged auth blob are not evidence that AI wrote that blob.\",\n  \"fix_sha\": null,\n  \"fix_granularity\": null,\n  \"remaining_gap\": \"The atomic flawed/exposing contribution and contribution-specific AI attribution across the grouped body/path/form/health mechanisms remain unresolved. AI-marked 0d4875d and 90fd791 bundle distinct changes. At v1.96.2 the health config-stripping patch still reaches provider global/environment-key fallback in inspected source; complete intervening-wrapper/configuration review and a non-network ordinary regression are unfinished. No universal closure object is proved.\",\n  \"flip_condition\": \"A content-bound atomic member or contemporaneous contribution-specific disclosure tying AI to the flawed/exposing code would support an AI verdict. Complete carrier/identity/convention evidence could instead support NOT_AI for a scoped causal change. A source-bound intervening guard plus isolated non-network regression preventing global/environment credentials at a caller-selected health destination, or a later effective repair, would settle the remaining closure question.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Real connection/credential composition failures are supported. Parent/child health sources isolate deployment credential inheritance. Body/path/form validators operate on different representations; the cited repair adds actual callers and credential-reference stripping. All nine named source releases carry the patch, but patch presence is not universal closure and AI attribution is not resolved. See REPORT.md and six-dimensional research.json.\",\n  \"flaw_origin\": {\n    \"sha\": \"0e2fcde145e9ffb27812badbc314b1c6f2af74d9\",\n    \"parent\": \"9a7831dd33115e598defe3d423e6a1c52dc0d380\",\n    \"scope\": \"Specific health-test deployment config-under-request merge; not asserted to originate every advisory surface or to establish absence of AI.\"\n  },\n  \"candidate_set\": [\n    \"32d0277f0374e01bea384a8c445bb1ea9e3432ba\",\n    \"47214be317f45a2d2ac08258362e0481411eb427\",\n    \"0d4875dec978e7b458336e943b89c31efa92a4a2\",\n    \"90fd791e0d4c794bd009ca0d84c558d9ff3d604a\",\n    \"065faf6e695be64a1a367601271839914e4a6621\",\n    \"c898d341c02299cf2506d0d8e84cc67953043593\",\n    \"714fff696aa7141e104a314d7f872757bdecf9c5\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/retained-ghsa.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"3e06e6501ef0b3cf6b88e4e73bc8ea365063b1665b2567f4557aadde06861826\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/cve.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"adc0e5cb43a49731f7eba9c7d7da62bb90ceeeb8de2c1a40dedc2765e43113ef\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/health-origin-parent.py\",\n      \"sha256\": \"48c1f5885d995a93e441ae20adc03720a90bd8eba956cf6e815ce11bc3e54918\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/health-origin-child.py\",\n      \"sha256\": \"94b78f031469fe50cb46241dbb2dcc268052af3177fa11f3e9d773bec781a041\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/commit-c898.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"e86b62cb916f81b119d7bd6179d1165925aae4a1cebf4be087eef2b6f090b69a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/commit-0d487.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"9b3e8cf292f110cf4dcad7bd55d92ec451c7ba519f6f1cde831a7c6195aab46d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/commit-90fd.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d902aa628a92f26877bf088f8d57b80fd367dc2dc5863da7738dcc9328581644\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/carriers.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"8ea795f9375ea6febd5216c14b451ea6d8f5b3adbdf8937bc88c87c6e242b25b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/release-content.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"85bf76d1acd1ad8c4d7e69a8da36ccafeb0731d4149d0ff48d47eaff172d8aef\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/v1962-health.py\",\n      \"sha256\": \"8800205f4099b6b6f089576cfade2c3a6bfeaeea5a8c308e6ee05be69e722d67\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/v1962-main.py\",\n      \"sha256\": \"ceb6cfc092d9e1e63db81e2952708c01a8338575206902a3fd61c9638e91043a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/v1962-helpers.py\",\n      \"sha256\": \"38f916a6d3ca85cbf1f5c6f9b01ff287cb1cee6bac7c1e082fce13bb95c183fc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/openai-handler.py\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d4dac8a4b95256cd35b3dec2b610a6ce8d4ea00623f1234058b0e0f1b61eaaba\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/attempt-history.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"604fc12752d1f4974755eab2b7fe2ec7d563e1ad2b18944dbfe29a5a9f062019\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-3389297662643f29363dbb4b\",\n  \"verdict\": \"AI_CODE_FLAWED\",\n  \"advisory_ids\": [\n    \"GHSA-3CV6-JPF6-8222\",\n    \"CVE-2026-84377\"\n  ],\n  \"advisory_disposition\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"advisory_aliases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GHSA-3CV6-JPF6-8222\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CVE-2026-84377\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Authenticated SSRF + provider-credential exfiltration through an incomplete request-parameter control in the LiteLLM proxy: nested metadata supplied as bracket-notation form keys escaped the banned-parameter check, path-supplied model names escaped the URL-destination guard, and the health connection test merged configured credentials under caller-supplied connection parameters.\",\n  \"cause\": \"An authenticated proxy user controls request parameters that are merged into the upstream call. is_request_body_safe() denies sensitive fields at root and walks metadata/litellm_metadata, but only parses them as dict/JSON; bracket-notation form keys (litellm_metadata[api_base]) bypass it. The URL-valued destination guard is not applied to path-supplied model, and test_model_connection merges configured credentials under caller connection params without dropping litellm_credential_name.\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"Attacker-controlled routing/credential parameter -> is_request_body_safe/denylist or destination guard -> upstream LiteLLM provider call -> operator's stored provider credentials sent to the attacker destination, and SSRF to internal services.\",\n  \"bug_semantics\": \"Denylist/representation mismatch (bracket-notation multipart metadata not inspected), a guard applied on the body but not the path-supplied model identifier, and an order-of-merge defect that lets caller connection fields coexist with configured credentials.\",\n  \"introducer_sha\": \"37a22acf6f527870d4873c33c67a1078dc20f52b\",\n  \"introducer_parent\": \"c94a8d6514936164ef869a6dda8bb7897b3958c2\",\n  \"bic_granularity\": \"ATOMIC\",\n  \"bic_minimality\": \"Single logically atomic control change: extending is_request_body_safe to walk metadata/litellm_metadata without a bracket-notation branch, which is the residual bypass the advisory fixes.\",\n  \"bic_note\": \"The introducer is the AI-attributed change that widened the denylist walk to the nested metadata fields fixed here; the human clientside-credential/health-merge surfaces are recorded in flaw_origin, not as introducer_sha.\",\n  \"landing_commit\": null,\n  \"landing_basis\": \"INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT\",\n  \"landing_note\": \"Introducer is itself reachable on the default branch (ancestor of main HEAD e1d16f51d1); no distinct carrier object is asserted.\",\n  \"flaw_origin\": \"Earlier human surfaces extended here: litellm/router_utils/clientside_credential_handler.py (Krish Dholakia, 2025-03-03, 2fc6262675) and the health-check credential merge in litellm/proxy/health_endpoints/_health_endpoints.py (yuneng-jiang, 2025-12-09, 0e2fcde145, 'Change health check to read env var like chat completions'). These establish an older human origin for the credential-retention surface while the AI change introduced the nested-metadata denylist bypass.\",\n  \"ai_on_bic\": true,\n  \"ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"PRESENT\",\n    \"sha\": \"37a22acf6f527870d4873c33c67a1078dc20f52b\",\n    \"quote\": \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\n    \"source\": \"commit\"\n  },\n  \"