{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 sh -c 'cat additional-primary/SOURCE-QUESTIONS.txt; ls retained-git/auditor1 retained-git/auditor2; sed -n \\\"48,64p\\\" sealed-auditors/auditor1/REPORT.md; sed -n \\\"69,86p\\\" sealed-auditors/auditor2/REPORT.md; cat sealed-auditors/auditor2/receipts/git_history.txt'\"","aggregated_output":"Investigate whole reported body/form/path/health cluster without collapsing distinct authority/caller/origin branches. Compare exact37a22acf member and parent, full logical scope/possible carrier, intended nested-metadata remediation invariant and actual bracket-form consumer at that epoch. A genuine AI-attributed incomplete remediation may qualify; neither favorable label nor aggregate marker makes the causal binding automatic. Earlier0d4875/90fd bundles and37a22 member are distinct evidence leads. Resolve real default main versus staging repair integration and each member/prerequisite rather than calling final PR tip alone the repairing unit. Health route requires actual proxy/team-admin authorization; examine configured-key filtering versus global/environment SDK fallback, real wrapper policy and trusted opt-in boundaries at same revision. Follow available decisive static evidence; no credential-exfiltration reproduction, payload generation, live/mock hostile endpoint, provider call or deployed target. A purely inert ordinary control may test bookkeeping, but do not execute the reported attack under a mocked label. Preserve nine source-release lines and later capture dates separately from package/deployment evidence. Honor all original exhausted/denied probes; preserve promisor/lazy-fetch/resource failures.\nretained-git/auditor1:\n01.git\nSOURCES.json\n\nretained-git/auditor2:\n01.git\nSOURCES.json\n### Residual source of credentials\n\nIn v1.96.2, `v1962-health.py:1907` filters deployment config and then merges the request, calls authorization, and calls `litellm.ahealth_check`. `v1962-main.py:8212` dispatches through `HealthCheckHelpers`; `v1962-helpers.py` routes chat to `litellm.acompletion(**model_params)`. The OpenAI dispatch in `v1962-main.py` independently resolves the API base and resolves a missing key from `litellm.api_key`, `litellm.openai_key`, or `get_secret(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")` (around line 2376). `openai-handler.py:370` constructs AsyncOpenAI with both api_key and base_url. Removing the deployment dictionary's key is therefore not, by itself, a prohibition on using process-owned keys at a caller-selected endpoint.\n\nThis is a conditional static inference for an authorized health-test caller and an environment/global-key configuration; it is not a claim of observed theft, a public-target result, or the same low-privilege scope as the ordinary inference-route allegation. It also explains why the blanket workaround “allow_client_side_credentials=false” is insufficient evidence of closure across every route and credential source. A further check must establish whether any active wrapper policy prevents this combination before outbound client construction, and whether all relevant installed configurations satisfy that policy. No all-version residual claim is made from one release's dispatch code.\n\n## Origin and comparison with immediate parents\n\n1. `32d0277f0374e01bea384a8c445bb1ea9e3432ba`, parent `a1f0169fc18ecf097df2194780278041f1e60b33`, changes unconditional rejection of api_base/base_url into an exception when `check_complete_credentials` returns true. Its code treats the presence of api_key as completeness for selected model families. This is an earlier weakening of the invariant; it is not established as the origin of every nested/path/health mechanism in this cluster. It names Krish Dholakia, but that alone does not prove NOT_AI for the later chain.\n2. `47214be317f45a2d2ac08258362e0481411eb427`, parent `93faf321df159b1ef65a98cc29a70958a96d184a`, adds user_config to a then-short denylist and also changes internal-context and metadata plumbing. The author display name is `user` with a GitHub-noreply account, not a recovered named identity sufficient for the protocol's NOT_AI threshold. No attribution is inferred from the subject “harden.”\n3. `0e2fcde145e9ffb27812badbc314b1c6f2af74d9`, parent `9a7831dd33115e598defe3d423e6a1c52dc0d380`, introduces deployment lookup and config-under-request merging in health tests, alongside request environment-reference resolution. The raw parent lacks that config merge; the raw child has it before the authorization and SDK call. This establishes a specific health credential-inheritance origin, not a universal cluster BIC. The earlier endpoint-creation commit `c84717c9e08564d0119607688e6da797a3777c66` accepted a model and called health checking but did not contain that deployment inheritance logic. Receipts: `health-origin.json`, `health-origin-parent.py`, `health-origin-child.py`, `health-root.json`.\n4. AI-marked `0d4875dec978e7b458336e943b89c31efa92a4a2`, parent `934ecdca78daf7ec9514efd47df77bf7495c822d`, adds nested embedding-config validation but also repairs unrelated upstream polling URL checks and carries generated UI files. Follow-up `90fd791e0d4c794bd009ca0d84c558d9ff3d604a` replaces recursive validation with fixed single-level descent and changes hostname-error disclosure. These are multi-change objects. Their marker cannot be mechanically assigned to one omitted sibling or treated as proof of first introduction. The raw auth parent/child and both patches establish the inspected scope, while PR #26996's member table and bounded ref fetch did not expose a finer member for each logical change.\n\nThe chain must still distinguish earlier origin, later exposure and incomplete remediation per actual consuming operation. There is no justified single atomic introducer covering all of these surfaces. Thus introducer_sha/bic_granularity are explicitly unknown in the record, while the observed objects remain in evidence.\n\n## AI participation\n\n`introducer_sha = 37a22acf6f527870d4873c33c67a1078dc20f52b` (\"chore(proxy): close callback-config and observability-credential\nside channels\", 2026-05-03, ancestor of `main`). This change extended `is_request_body_safe` to\nwalk `metadata`/`litellm_metadata` (`_NESTED_METADATA_KEYS`) using the dict/JSON parser only. That\nis the exact control whose unhandled bracket-notation form (#1 above) is the residual bypass the\nadvisory fixes; the fix `5b2c92d7` adds the bracket-notation branch to this very loop.\n`bic_granularity = ATOMIC`: the object is one logically atomic control change, not a PR carrier.\n`introducer_parent = c94a8d6514936164ef869a6dda8bb7897b3958c2`. `landing_basis = INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT`, `landing_commit = null`\n(the introducing object is itself reachable on the default branch; no distinct carrier object is asserted).\n\n`flaw_origin` (earlier human) is separate and is *not* the BIC: the clientside-credential /\nrequest-parameter boundary predates this change (`litellm/router_utils/clientside_credential_handler.py`\ntracing to Krish Dholakia 2025-03-03 `2fc6262675`), and the health-check credential-merge behavior\nappears in the health endpoint around 2025-12-09 (`0e2fcde145`, yuneng-jiang, \"Change health check to\nread env var like chat completions\"). Both are human-authored surfaces that the AI change extended\nwithout closing #1/#3.\n\nGranularity caveat: the advisory aggregates several mechanisms with separate origins (path-model\ncheck, health-check credential merge, `litellm_credential_name`). I bind the BIC to the\n# git receipts for alias-3389297662643f29363dbb4b  capture=2026-10-04\n## clone: GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH not set (owned blobless scratch) ; repo BerriAI/litellm default_branch=main\n## git rev-parse HEAD\ne1d16f51d14849c1b3decf17cd81a3bcb4863dca\n\n## ancestry (merge-base --is-ancestor <sha> HEAD)\nc898d341c02299cf2506d0d8e84cc67953043593 ancestor\n37a22acf6f527870d4873c33c67a1078dc20f