{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: output/alias-3389297662643f29363dbb4b/REPORT.md\n+# Adjudication: alias-3389297662643f29363dbb4b\n+\n+Reducer incremental-causal-20261004-case-047-adjudicator, attempt 1; task binding 7d2a45e8623efdf43c9dbcef50d6116e2acd5740a689107f5b7046729c360849. Recipient incremental-causal-20261004T081300Z-lead. Protocol 2026-09-27.3 and causal-work-v1. This is a research handoff, not ledger acceptance or publication. Both original independent lanes are retained and bound in decisions.json. The research sidecar is research.json.\n+\n+The synthesis verdict is EVIDENCE_GAP, with a BLOCKED research decision for contribution-specific causal attribution. The vulnerability is real; this is neither a false-positive finding nor a finding of no AI use. Auditor2's AI_CODE_FLAWED account overstates atomicity, provider credential consumption, health authority and universal repair. Auditor1's source-release result is supported. Its unresolved wrapper question can now be narrowed: the inspected default SDK wrapper supplies no mandatory credential/destination isolation policy. An authorized health caller in a process-global/environment-key configuration still reaches independent provider-key fallback after the deployment dictionary is stripped. No attack or provider call was executed.\n+\n+## Advisory and coverage\n+\n+The exact retained GitHub global advisory has ghsa_id GHSA-3cv6-jpf6-8222, published_at 2026-09-30T21:11:25Z, and withdrawn_at explicitly null: ACTIVE. The retained CVE record identifies CVE-2026-84377 as PUBLISHED. The identifiers are aliases, not rejected duplicates. GitHub enumerates nine maintenance lines; the CVE's coarse middle interval must not replace them. Primary copies and metadata are retained in evidence/ and the original lane directories. The coverage cutoff remains 2026-10-04T08:13:00Z. Auditor captures and this adjudicator's acquisitions after that instant are later observations of identified historical bytes. Auditor2's broad statement that its evidence was within the window is not accepted without matching receipt timestamps.\n+\n+## Mechanism and authority\n+\n+At aa1180c0, auth_utils checks root fields, selected nested configuration, dict/JSON metadata, and fallback structures. An operator can expressly permit client credentials globally or per deployment. Those legitimate exceptions are distinct from the default-closed omissions.\n+\n+The body validator does not reconstruct bracket-form fields, although downstream form consumers do. The destination check validates body values before common processing chooses the effective model from server defaults, CLI settings, URL path and body. A caller-controlled path value therefore needs validation at selection, not merely an earlier body check. The repair adds that call in common processing and image endpoints. Model defaults and explicitly allowed destination hosts remain material conditions. Metadata callback destinations and provider connection parameters are different consumers: inserting api_base into metadata is not itself proof the provider reads that value as its connection endpoint.\n+\n+The pre-repair health endpoint looks up a deployment and merges its resolved configuration underneath request parameters. Changing connection fields while omitting a key preserves the deployment's key/reference. This is a different authority branch. At v1.96.2, the database must be connected, loaded model_info takes precedence, non-team models require PROXY_ADMIN, and team models invoke team-model authorization. The actual health route is not available to every ordinary authenticated virtual-key holder. Configured model tests without overrides legitimately retain their connection; wholly caller-owned connections and explicit operator opt-ins must also be distinguished.\n+\n+## Introduction and AI scope\n+\n+The specific health inheritance boundary is 0e2fcde145e9ffb27812badbc314b1c6f2af74d9 versus 9a7831dd33115e598defe3d423e6a1c52dc0d380. Earlier path/credential and validator objects are independent leads, not decomposed members of one whole-cluster introduction.\n+\n+New exact primary evidence recovers 37a22acf6f527870d4873c33c67a1078dc20f52b and immediate parent c94a8d6514936164ef869a6dda8bb7897b3958c2. The object genuinely adds _NESTED_METADATA_KEYS and dict/JSON coercion without bracket reconstruction. Its full message carries \"'`Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>`. PR27081'\"'s actual table contains that object and 01323e890357f34ea39eab025e7fff55391ed26e; its base is internal staging and its carrier is e4ac46b5d148c13d4e97d7644de98024d5b49556. A reachable member is not automatically an atomic vulnerability change or a default-branch integration.\n+\n+The full 37a22 change also derives broad observability bans and separately blocks root callback fields that mutate worker-wide callback state. Its tests cover those separate branches. The trailer establishes participation in this recovered object, not a line-specific attribution to an isolated causal member. It is stronger evidence than the earlier 0d4875/90fd markers, but auditor2's assertion of a single atomic control ignores the object's independently described callback-state branch.\n+\n+The consumer comparison is now anchored to the same epoch: epoch37-files_endpoints.py reconstructs flat litellm_metadata bracket fields before add_litellm_data_to_request; epoch37-form-utils.py implements that reconstruction, while epoch37-auth.py only checks dict/JSON containers. This establishes incomplete representation coverage in the AI-marked hardening. It does not establish that every reconstructed metadata connection field redirects the provider while retaining its key. epoch37-dynamic-callbacks.py consumes only its supported callback fields and rejects request-supplied environment references. epoch37-langfuse.py includes credential-isolation behavior when environment credentials are disabled. These are contrary evidence against equating every metadata destination bypass with provider-key leakage. A supported AI incomplete remediation is possible, but the complete relevant callback consumer and credential provenance, logical granularity and contribution binding remain decisive unfinished work. No NOT_AI conclusion follows from missing disclosures or human carrier identities.\n+\n+## Repair and residual\n+\n+The six PR36011 members perform distinct work: fc4be70 adds path validation; 5b2c92 reconstructs bracket metadata; e5effcb changes health precedence; b468acb filters connection credentials; 59173c restores explicit opt-ins; 298fb8c removes stored credential references. The final tip alone is not the minimum whole-cluster repair. c898d341 is an internal-staging merge, not the first default-main closure. Default branch metadata and parent/integration captures place the inspected auth/health landing at 714fff696aa7141e104a314d7f872757bdecf9c5 versus ead62528e607b9d8e61273def638799c9c3a69ba. Backports are separate content landings. These facts correct auditor2 even independently of the residual.\n+\n+At v1.96.2, _config_base_for_health_check strips configured connection/credential fields including litellm_credential_name when request connection parameters trigger filtering, unless the operator opts in. test_model_connection then authorizes and calls ahealth_check, whose chat handler calls acompletion directly. The @client async wrapper runs optional deployment hooks, loads named credentials if present, and invokes the original function. Its optional hook dispatcher iterates configured callbacks; it is not an unconditional destination/key policy. The SDK dispatch independently selects api_base and falls back from an omitted api_key to litellm.api_key, litellm.openai_key or OPENAI_API_KEY. The exact v1.96.2 OpenAI handler constructs its client from those independently selected values. Thus deployment stripping does not guarantee isolation of process-owned credentials. The conditional residual is statically supported for the permitted administrative caller, applicable process key, and no additional operator hook preventing the combination. It is not observed exfiltration, a low-privilege health finding, or an all-version claim. No future vendor fix is required to conclude that this inspected patch is partial.\n+\n+## Releases and delivery limits\n+\n+All nine named source releases are preserved: 1.88.6, 1.89.7, 1.90.7, 1.91.5, 1.92.2, 1.93.2, 1.94.3, 1.95.1 and 1.96.2. Retained release metadata and forty-five runtime files establish source content and caller wiring; an independent syntax/AST inspection receipt is included. This answers auditor2's unresolved source-containment question by actual content rather than requiring the same backport SHA in every divergent branch. v1.96.0 lacks the final health/form changes. These findings do not identify every wheel/container's bytes or prove deployment safety. A failed guessed v1.96.1 tag is not an absent-shipment proof beyond that name.\n+\n+The remaining decisive question belongs to this adjudicator/leader handoff: which logically atomic flawed or exposing contribution and actual callback/provider consumer binds the supported incomplete metadata control to the advisory impact and the Claude disclosure? Consumer-specific provenance work remains unfinished within the original operating limit; no public-source exhaustion is claimed. Wrapper and partial-repair questions have advanced through permitted static evidence. Prohibited attack replay is not a substitute for that work.\n+\n+Execution failures are preserved in evidence receipts: the initial compare invocation omitted the required --json pathname; the corrected comparison is retained separately. Local full-diff inspection of 37a22 failed on unavailable promisor blob c146b5ded5b99d075b02f02201dc61529d205bfc; exact official API and parent/child raw sources recovered the relevant observations without shared Git fetching. Early listing globs for nonexistent additional-primary markdown/SOURCES files failed; SOURCE-QUESTIONS.txt was subsequently read. Original auditor1 shell-glob and missing-object failures and auditor2 lazy-fetch/resource/tag failures remain in unchanged sealed inputs. No source denial or safety stop was bypassed. Only static inspection, syntax parsing and frozen delivery checks were performed. Exact checks, exits, readback and seals are outside the decision payload; a reduction rejection for BLOCKED research is expected and must not be presented as acceptance.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
