ied sidecar before relying\ncontract/scripts/README.md:266:loader recursively parses JSON, so source-response arrays, receipts and scratch checkouts\ncontract/scripts/README.md:268:original reports and evidence for research and decision pins. A packaging retry preserves\ncontract/scripts/README.md:269:the failed invocation and is not a fresh independent research attempt.\ncontract/scripts/README.md:276:exact check commands/results (including failures or checks not run), and any unresolved\ncontract/scripts/README.md:281:completed command, sealed submission or accepted research grants no claim-release,\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:1:# Data contract\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:13:[published types](../web/src/lib/research-data.ts).\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:17:define the research evidence standard.\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:19:## Ledger\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:35:  New terminal updates require nonempty `row.causal_research` with `verdict`\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:38:- Publisher/envelope use `row.causal_research` whenever the key exists; null, empty\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:43:## Audit records\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:45:Current research contract: `2026-09-27.3` (see AUDIT-PROTOCOL). The base record\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:46:format originated in `2026-09-19.1`; the research-work sidecar was added in\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:50:One JSON record per case, kept in the batch's research directory; the accepted\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:51:synthesis lands in the ledger row's `causal_research` in the same shape. Required\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:62:    python3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict research/<batch>/<case>.json\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:63:    python3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict --repo <clone_dir> research/<batch>/<case>.json\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:76:  research. Do not claim a landing, decomposed members or repair SHAs, and omit\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:156:  The local Git check accepts legacy `value` as the quote and defaults an omitted\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:160:  `ai_admissibility` binding the disclosure to the causal change. The Git check only\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:161:  checks the shape of this web evidence; the reducer must verify the saved source.\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:208:  no AI marker, and a contemporaneous disclosure-convention check. An absent marker\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:219:## Reducer decisions (local coordination)\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:225:into frozen decisions. Legacy frozen layouts retain their original checks until\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:231:The baseline envelope below uses legacy prose resolutions; newly adopted research-work\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:278:unpatched research can be `ACCEPTED` with its qualified repair conclusion. Record\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:280:payloads, reports and other deliverables. Preserve the full accepted research when\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:284:`audit_reduction_gate.py` together and invoke that copy. The gate checks the hashes of\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:288:### Research-work contract\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:291:`2026-09-25.1`: set `reduction.research_contract` to\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:292:`causal-work-v1` and freeze the gate invocation with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`.\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:296:Each decision has a `research` object with `advisory`, `mechanism`, `bic`, `ai`, `fix`\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:297:and `versions` entries. Auditors keep the same object in their owned research sidecar,\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:332:Completion is the researcher's claim about the recorded questions and evidence available\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:334:research objects are unassessed, never zero outstanding work.\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:337:for the same observation are attempts within that route, not extra research coverage.\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:358:The gate checks the declared statuses and pinned bytes, not the truth of their interpretation.\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:364:supplied resolution is checked, including optional ones. Existing TP and input-quality\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:367:The reduction gate returns `research_work.worklist` from unfinished entries, including\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:369:The list concerns declared research only. A zero-length list neither proves discovery\ncontract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md:374:## Published cases\n{\n  \"ghsa_id\": \"GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-87859\",\n  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"summary\": \"morgan vulnerable to Log Injection via unescaped double quote in quoted log fields\",\n  \"description\": \"### Impact\\n\\nMorgan writes attacker-controlled request data to the access log. Its escaping (added in 1.11.0 and 1.12.0) neutralizes control characters, the Unicode line separators, and backslash, but not the double quote (`0x22`), which is the field delimiter of the Apache combined log format morgan emits. An attacker who controls a quoted field (`:user-agent`, `:referrer`, the request URL, or the Basic auth `:remote-user`) can inject a double quote to close the field early and forge additional fields in the log record. The `combined`, `common`, and `default` formats, and any custom format that quotes a token, are affected. This is an incomplete fix of CVE-2026-5078 and CVE-2026-15603.\\n\\n### Patches\\n\\nUsers should upgrade to version 1.12.1.\\n\\n### Workarounds\\n\\nUpdate to version 1.12.1.\",\n  \"type\": \"reviewed\",\n  \"severity\": \"medium\",\n  \"repository_advisory_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/expressjs/morgan/security-advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"source_code_location\": \"https://github.com/expressjs/morgan\",\n  \"identifiers\": [\n    {\n      \"value\": \"GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n      \"type\": \"GHSA\"\n    },\n    {\