co-author trailers, including human collaborators; no AI-specific disclosure convention was established by this bounded spot check. The source trees have no dedicated contribution-policy file in those revisions. This is not an organization-wide claim.\n+\n+The initial carrier scan omitted pre-combined `exports.token` sources from its matching predicate, despite enumerating the commits. That analytical coverage defect is preserved in `all-carriers.out` and corrected in `all-carriers-v2.out`, which matches all 428 commits. The v2 observation governs; the v1 output does not support complete carrier coverage. No negative classification is inferred from the initial search or from human signatures alone. AI marker state is UNKNOWN for the unrecovered atomic BIC; the final repair'\"'s own inspected metadata has ABSENT AI marker. No true/false \"'`ai_on_bic` is asserted.\n+\n+## Unresolved decisive question and handoff\n+\n+The missing object is the original logically atomic contribution of Connect'\"'s \"'`filters/log.js` already present in the 2010 root, with its immediate predecessor and attributable provenance. A recovered member or authoritative original source history would distinguish authorship of that logger from authorship of its aggregate carrier. Contribution-specific AI disclosure bound by content identity to either incomplete hardening would also change the classification, even though the quote defect is older. The present bounded probes answer exposure, repair and shipment; they do not settle those contribution-level facts. The next owner is the named leader, who can route newly supplied original history or first-party disclosure without changing this independent original.\n+\n+No network source denial, retrieval timeout, exploit execution or runtime reproduction occurred. Relevant fetches and source/object validations succeeded. An optional `git config --get-regexp` query in a grouped read had no matching partial-clone/promisor configuration (normal exit 1); its grouped command'\"'s final success must not be read as every subcommand succeeding. The separate explicit fsck/non-shallow and object-identity validation is authoritative. Some interactive command displays truncated; complete collected stdout files were retained. Inline release-identity checking is supplemented by the retained \"'`verify_sources.py` and its explicit per-command exits. Strict gates, sidecar hash validation and final agreement checks are recorded in `VALIDATION.md` and corresponding receipts. They check delivery, not truth or acceptance.\n+\n+The structured record is derived after this report. The six-dimension sidecar is `research.json`. Stable files, including raw receipts, scripts, report and record, are sealed by exact SHA256 in `SEAL.json`, which excludes itself. Runtime home, scratch clones and runner-final remain outside the sealed case payload. No database, claims, deployment, production, publication or canonical writes were made.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
