{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc 'cd /tmp && export GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0\nfor g in GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m GHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m; do\n  echo \"=== $g ===\"\n  numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 curl -sS -H '\"'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' \\\"https://api.github.com/advisories/\"'$g\" 2>&1 | python3 -c '\"'import sys,json;d=json.load(sys.stdin);print(\\\"id\\\",d.get(\\\"ghsa_id\\\"));print(\\\"cve\\\",d.get(\\\"cve_id\\\"));print(\\\"summary\\\",d.get(\\\"summary\\\"));print(\\\"published\\\",d.get(\\\"published_at\\\"));print(\\\"withdrawn\\\",d.get(\\\"withdrawn_at\\\"));print(\\\"desc\\\",(d.get(\\\"description\\\") or \\\"\\\")[:700]);print(\\\"vulns\\\",json.dumps(d.get(\\\"vulnerabilities\\\")))' 2>&1 | head -30\ndone\"","aggregated_output":"=== GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m ===\nid GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m\ncve CVE-2026-5078\nsummary morgan vulnerable to Log Forging via unneutralized control characters in :remote-user\npublished 2026-07-10T14:32:15Z\nwithdrawn None\ndesc ### Impact\n\nMorgan's `:remote-user` token extracts the Basic auth username from the `Authorization` header and writes it to the log stream without neutralizing control characters. An attacker can send a crafted `Authorization: Basic` header containing CR/LF characters to inject forged log lines, corrupting the one-request-per-line structure of access logs.\n\nThe built-in `combined`, `common`, `default`, and `short` formats are affected, as well as any custom format that includes `:remote-user`.\n\n### Patches\n\nUsers should upgrade to version 1.11.0.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nUse a custom format string that does not include `:remote-user`.\nvulns [{\"package\": {\"ecosystem\": \"npm\", \"name\": \"morgan\"}, \"vulnerable_version_range\": \">= 1.2.0, <= 1.10.1\", \"first_patched_version\": \"1.11.0\", \"vulnerable_functions\": []}]\n=== GHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m ===\nid GHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m\ncve CVE-2026-15603\nsummary morgan vulnerable to Log Forging via unescaped Unicode line separators\npublished 2026-09-08T21:28:26Z\nwithdrawn None\ndesc ### Impact\n\nMorgan writes attacker-controlled request data to the access log through its tokens. The 1.11.0 fix neutralizes C0 control characters, DEL, and backslash, but it does not escape the Unicode line separators `U+0085` (NEL), `U+2028` (LINE SEPARATOR), or `U+2029` (PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR). These code points are reachable through several tokens, including the request URL (`:url`), request headers such as `:user-agent` and `:referrer`, arbitrary `:req[header]` values, and the Basic auth username (`:remote-user`). NEL is valid `obs-text` in HTTP header values, so an attacker can place it in an ordinary request header.\n\nWhen such a value is logged, the raw code points survive into the emitt\nvulns [{\"package\": {\"ecosystem\": \"npm\", \"name\": \"morgan\"}, \"vulnerable_version_range\": \"< 1.12.0\", \"first_patched_version\": \"1.12.0\", \"vulnerable_functions\": []}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
