*all** string tokens, so the incomplete escaping now covers the quoted fields\n  the advisory names (`:user-agent`, `:referrer`, `:url`). Its immediate parent\n  03383991f55ec5d5e2c0cbdeb783a252f27196a5 still carries `['\"\\\\u0000-\\\\u001f\\\\u007f\\\\\\\\]\"'` and no\n  token wrapper.\n\nI bind **introducer_sha = fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe**, ATOMIC,\n`landing_basis INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT` (it is a normal single-parent commit directly on the\ndefault branch; `git tag --contains` reaches 1.12.0/1.12.1, and the 1.12.0 release commit\n063f084a8de1fe02e52333f0b5df2533ced85e42 has fbf9383 as its only-parent descent). Competing\nexplanation retained: b3f5d9b is the origin of the escaping helper and the first incomplete\nfix; the pre-1.11.0 origin is a pre-VCS/import boundary (NON_GIT_BOUNDARY-like). The choice\nbetween these candidates does **not** change the AI verdict, because all three carry named\nhuman identities and no AI marker (see §4). Evidence:\n`evidence/receipt-parent-and-regex.txt`, `evidence/receipt-remediation-diffs.txt`,\n`evidence/receipt-object-enumeration.txt`.\n\n## 3. Repair and release (observed)\n\nFix `4b695edf967ce179cdf4009fe8cddd184b7511ee` (\"fix: escape double quotes in log fields\",\nauthor/committer Ulises Gascón <ulisesgascongonzalez@gmail.com>) adds `\"` to the class and\n`case '\"'\\\\\\\"': return '\\\\\\\\\\\"'\"'`, plus two tests; it is the first mechanism-closing change on the\ndefault branch and lands in released tag `1.12.1`\n(`b1272e70812dbc504321eeb5a43d14b0822c150d`, whose parent is 4b695edf). `fix_granularity`\nATOMIC, `fix_sha`/`direct_fix_sha` = 4b695edf, no other landings. The advisory'\"'s patched\nrange \"'`< 1.12.1 -> 1.12.1` is consistent with the tag content: HISTORY.md 1.12.1 names\nCVE-2026-87859. The residual (the unescaped quote) is closed by 4b695edf; the phrase\n\"incomplete fix\" in the advisory names the historical 1.11.0/1.12.0 state, not an open\nsurface, so `residual_triage` = NOT-RESIDUAL. Evidence:\n`evidence/receipt-fix-commit.txt`, `evidence/receipt-releases.txt`.\n\n## 4. AI participation (observed; this is the decisive question)\n\nThe causal content (the `escapeLogField` regex and the `token()` wrapper) was inspected\nacross **all** local objects, not just ref-reachable commits:\n`git cat-file --batch-all-objects --batch-check` yields 428 commit objects in a\nnon-shallow clone, and each message was read. No agent/bot author, AI co-author trailer or\nfirst-person AI disclosure appears on b3f5d9b, fbf9383 or 4b695edf, nor on any other local\ncommit carrying that content. The only AI-looking trailer in the whole history is\n`Co-authored-by: EvoX <evox@evomap.ai>` on 286b000228cacba362bfa89791c6268663f86610\n(\"test: run CI on Windows and macOS (#379)\") — an unrelated CI commit, not the causal\nchange, so it is repository-level context and is **not admissible** to the BIC. The 1.12.0\ncommit'\"'s only trailer, \"'`Co-authored-by: M. Fazri Nizar <anon6372098.id@gmail.com>`, is a\nnamed human, not an AI marker. Authors/committers are named humans: b3f5d9b Jon Church\n<me@jonchurch.com> (committer `GitHub <noreply@github.com>`), fbf9383 Sebastian Beltran\n<bjohansebas@gmail.com> (committer Ulises Gascón), 4b695edf Ulises Gascón.\n\nVerdict **NOT_AI**: the BIC object (fbf9383) has a recovered named-human identity\n(`identity_class: human`), no object-local AI marker, and the repo'\"'s disclosure convention\nis present (AI co-authors *are* credited by trailer, e.g. EvoX) yet unused on the causal\nobject (\"'`CONVENTION_PRESENT_UNUSED`, observed at the 2026-08/09 date). No `ai_on_bic`\nattribution. Evidence: `evidence/receipt-ai-marker-scan.txt`,\n`evidence/receipt-object-enumeration.txt`.\n\n## 5. Version scope\n\nVulnerable `< 1.12.1`; first patched `1.12.1`. Source-release finding; not extended to\nuninspected binaries/platforms. Evidence: `evidence/00-github.json`,\n`evidence/receipt-releases.txt`.\n\n## 6. Boundaries, failures, flip condition\n\n- The 