Sencha / 2011 TJ Holowaychuk). The advisory's own words make this an *incomplete
remediation* of CVE-2026-5078 and CVE-2026-15603, so the smallest logically atomic change
that carries the defect *as the advisory describes it* is an escaping implementation that
omits the delimiter:

- b3f5d9bdb388690dfae9c06ab966328f49b7982b (1.11.0) first added `escapeLogField` with the
  incomplete class, but applied it only to `:remote-user`.
- fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe (1.12.0) extended the class and — decisively —
  wrapped **all** string tokens, so the incomplete escaping now covers the quoted fields
  the advisory names (`:user-agent`, `:referrer`, `:url`). Its immediate parent
  03383991f55ec5d5e2c0cbdeb783a252f27196a5 still carries `[\u0000-\u001f\u007f\\]` and no
  token wrapper.

I bind **introducer_sha = fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe**, ATOMIC,
