ame `except ValueError` pattern\n+  and was normalized to `(ValueError, RecursionError)` later, on 2026-09-22 in\n+  `5fde08a` (first released in `2.15.0`). That path parses the payload only\n+  after signature verification, so it is a distinct exposure, not an unclosed\n+  part of the unauthenticated header mechanism. Recorded as related hardening\n+  for the adjudicator; it does not move the verdict.\n+\n+## Step 4 - AI participation (NOT_AI)\n+\n+- BIC object `ab8821f` (2011) carries no AI marker; author and committer are the\n+  named human Jeff Lindsay `<progrium@gmail.com>` with a resolvable identity\n+  (`identity_class = HUMAN`).\n+- All other causal carriers (`0e8dcb3`, `5f255f9`, `a3f2ec3`, ...) and the fix\n+  `0657369` are human-authored with no `Co-authored-by`/`Generated-by` AI\n+  trailer (full metadata retained in `evidence/`; fix commit body is only the\n+  subject line, `evidence/fix_0657369_catfile.txt`).\n+- The repository does have an AI disclosure practice from 2026 (Claude-authored\n+  commit `74961f1` 2026-02-03, and `Co-authored-by: Claude` trailers on other\n+  2026 commits; `evidence/ai_commit_scan.txt`,\n+  `evidence/claude_commit_74961f1.txt`), but none of it touches the 2011 BIC or\n+  its carriers. That repo-level AI activity is **inadmissible** as\n+  attribution to this BIC (`ai_admissibility`).\n+- `disclosure_convention = CONVENTION_NOT_OBSERVED` scoped to the BIC date\n+  (2011): no AI disclosure convention existed to be used or omitted.\n+\n+## Step 5 - evidence, residual and flip condition\n+\n+- Decisive receipts are the raw files under `evidence/` (clone history,\n+  pickaxe, fix diff/cat-file, root commit, tag set, and the three isolated\n+  regression runs) with SHA-256 hashes recorded in `research.json`.\n+- **Residual / versions:** no code surface of the reported header mechanism\n+  remains open. The one qualified boundary is advisory scope: the published\n+  range `>= 2.13.0` understates the affected set (2.10.1 / 2.12.1 also escape).\n+  This is a version-range metadata cue, adjudicated NOT-RESIDUAL for the code\n+  defect; no additional closing commit is needed because the single 2.14.0 fix\n+  closes all of them once released.\n+- **flip_condition:** the verdict would change if the BIC object or a causal\n+  carrier were shown to carry a first-party AI disclosure bound to the flawed\n+  hunk (e.g. an AI co-author/bot identity on `ab8821f` or on a commit that\n+  changed the header `except` clause), or if a later exposure point were\n+  introduced by an AI-assisted change. Ordinal dates do not.\n+- Not run / limits: the strict `--repo` local-object check was run against the\n+  scratch clone (see Submission). No exploit was executed; the regression check\n+  is a bounded ordinary call at the public `jwt.decode` boundary in owned\n+  scratch. No live target was contacted.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/incremental-causal-20261004-case-050/auditor2/workspace/output/alias-360123c1550c32ce5077e4bc/REPORT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /home/hanqing/agents/ai-slop/research/incremental-causal-20261004-case-050/auditor2/workspace/output/alias-360123c1550c32ce5077e4bc/record.json\n+{\n+  \\\"class_id\\\": \\\"alias-360123c1550c32ce5077e4bc\\\",\n+  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"NOT_AI\\\",\n+  \\\"advisory_ids\\\": [\\\"GHSA-8WJV-2P76-3863\\\", \\\"CVE-2026-102265\\\"],\n+  \\\"advisory_disposition\\\": \\\"ACTIVE\\\",\n+  \\\"advisory_aliases\\\": [\n+    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"GHSA-8WJV-2P76-3863\\\", \\\"state\\\": \\\"ACTIVE\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"GitHub Advisory API inputs/00-github.json: type=reviewed, withdrawn_at=null, published 2026-09-29T23:43:06Z\\\"},\n+    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"CVE-2026-102265\\\", \\\"state\\\": \\\"ACTIVE\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"NVD inputs/01-nvd.json: vulnStatus=Awaiting Analysis, not rejected or withdrawn\\\"}\n+  ],\n+  \\\"cause\\\": \\\"Untrusted compact-token header reaches json.loads() in PyJWS._load() before signature verification, and the surrounding handler catches ValueError but not RecursionError, so deeply nested JSON raises a RecursionError (RuntimeError subclass) that escapes the documented PyJWTError hierarchy and turns an unauthenticated request into an HTTP 500 with a logged traceback.\\\",\n+  \\\"mechanism\\\": \\\"PyJWS._load() base64url-decodes the header segment and calls json.loads(header_data) wrapped in except ValueError as e: raise DecodeError(...). CPython's JSON decoder raises RecursionError once array nesting crosses the native stack guard (~65,000 levels). RecursionError is not a ValueError, so it leaves _load() and jwt.decode(), matching no jwt.PyJWTError handler. The header is parsed first, so no key and no valid signature are required. Depth (not size) is the trigger; a header that large cannot ride in Authorization, so body transport (RFC 7662 introspection style) is the practical path. Effect is a repeatable authentication-path denial of service (no crash, no data exposure).\\\",\n+  \\\"bug_semantics\\\": \\\"Exception-type translation gap: the parser guards only against ValueError/TypeError, omitting RuntimeError/RecursionError, at a revision whose documented contract is that jwt.decode on untrusted input raises only PyJWTError.\\\",\n+  \\\"flaw_origin\\\": \\\"Present at the repository root. Root commit ab8821fefa1c481ece410305d03a1f21c0b4a207 (2011-02-24, Jeff Lindsay <progrium@gmail.com>) parses the untrusted header with json.loads() inside except (ValueError, TypeError), which also excludes RecursionError. The 2013-05-15 commit 0e8dcb32ef115676cd7b6a2402a221fad4820553 gave the header parse its own except ValueError as e, but its immediate parent had identical RecursionError behavior, so 0e8dcb3 is an error-granularity refactor, not the introducer. 5f255f94a6d8763cb7ae504348429f770f69be6e (2015-01-18) and a3f2ec37f8660e3c445635ed417ae1100753309d (2015-04-19) only moved the code into jwt/api.py and then jwt/api_jws.py.\\\",\n+  \\\"introducer_sha\\\": \\\"ab8821fefa1c481ece410305d03a1f21c0b4a207\\\",\n+  \\\"introducer_parent\\\": null,\n+  \\\"bic_granularity\\\": \\\"ATOMIC\\\",\n+  \\\"bic_note\\\": \\\"Root-boundary atomic change: the minimal causal hunk is the untrusted header json.loads() inside decode()'s narrow except in the root commit jwt/__init__.py. No behavior-changing predecessor is observable, and no later commit changed the RecursionError behavior until the fix.\\\",\n+  \\\"landing_commit\\\": null,\n+  \\\"landing_basis\\\": \\\"NO_LANDING_NAMED\\\",\n+  \\\"landing_note\\\": \\\"The BIC is the repository root commit, which has no separate merge/squash carrier; introducing change and landing coincide at the earliest observable boundary, so landing_commit is null rather than duplicating introducer_sha. Pre-root origin and authorship are not inferred.\\\",\n+  \\\"decomposed_shas\\\": null,\n+  \\\"decomposition_probe\\\": \\\"git -C scratch/pyjwt log --all --oneline -S \\\\\\\"except ValueError as e\\\\\\\" -- jwt/api_jws.py jwt/api.py jwt/__init__.py -> content carriers ab8821f, 0e8dcb3, 5f255f9, a3f2ec3 (plus typing/traceback commits); retarget/materialize probes retained in evidence/pickaxe_except_valueerror.txt.\\\",\n+  \\\"fix_sha\\\": \\\"06573692ebcdec8831c3927513b3e87c31fbbb62\\\",\n+  \\\"fix_granularity\\\": \\\"ATOMIC\\\",\n+  \\\"fix_note\\\": \\\"Single one-line hunk in jwt/api_jws.py::_load changing 'except ValueError as e:' to 'except (ValueError, RecursionError) as e:', plus one regression test. First mechanism-closing change on the default branch (parent e6f48401001609a8f99e71fcaf355fb895d508a8), ancestor of origin/HEAD, contained in tags 2.14.0, 2.15.0 and 2.15.1.\\\",\n+  \\\"ai_on_bic\\\": false,\n+  \\\"ai_marker\\\": {\\\"state\\\": \\\"ABSENT\\\", \\\"sha\\\": \\\"ab8821fefa1c481ece410305d03a1f21c0b4a207\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"commit\\\", \\\"note\\\": \\\"Root commit author and committer: Jeff Lindsay <progrium@gmail.com>; message 'initial commit'; no Co-authored-by/Generated-by/bot trailer.\\\"},\n+  \\\"identity_class\\\": \\\"HUMAN\\\",\n+  \\\"disclosure_convention\\\": \\\"CONVENTION_NOT_OBSERVED\\\",\n+  \\\"disclosure_convention_evidence\\\": \\\"Scoped to the 2011 BIC date, no AI disclosure convention existed to be used or omitted. For context, the repository later acquires one: Claude-authored commit 74961f165765300dc6b366c6c2b3dc0d11b92bde (2026-02-03, author 'Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>') and 'Co-authored-by: Claude' trailers on 2026 commits (evidence/ai_commit_scan.txt, evidence/claude_commit_74961f1.txt). None of it touches the BIC object or its causal carriers.\\\",\n+  \\\"ai_admissibility\\\": \\\"Repo-level AI activity (the 2026 Claude-authored commit and Claude co-author trailers) is not bound to the 2011 BIC object or to any commit that changed the header except clause, so it is inadmissible as BIC or exposure attribution and does not move the verdict.\\\",\n+  \\\"ai_evidence\\\": \\\"BIC object ab8821f and every causal carrier on the header path (0e8dcb3, 5f255f9, a3f2ec3) are human-authored with no AI marker, and the fix 0657369 is human-authored and SSH-signed with no AI trailer. The repository's AI disclosures are confined to unrelated 2026 commits.\\\",\n+  \\\"fix_ai_marker\\\": {\\\"state\\\": \\\"ABSENT\\\", \\\"note\\\": \\\"Fix commit 0657369 has author and committer Jose Padilla <jpadilla@users.noreply.github.com>, an SSH signature and a subject-only message with no AI trailer.\\\"},\n+  \\\"evidence\\\": [\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/bic_ab8821f_catfile.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"7b2249f5e040a7059b73d4988db508bcab5c40198ef7f6716365d6c94df7ff19\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt cat-file -p ab8821fefa1c481ece410305d03a1f21c0b4a207\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Root commit, no parent, author and committer Jeff Lindsay <progrium@gmail.com>, 2011-02-24.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/bic_ab8821f_jwt_init.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"7d2eae24c3a943c40ba5a269bb3feff211010381ee71672e828ae31a38422877\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt show ab8821f:jwt/__init__.py\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Root decode() parses untrusted header with json.loads inside except (ValueError, TypeError); RecursionError escapes.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/0e8dcb3_diff.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"cb3a141a43255b95ce49ff27bd0541d784812bc83179def7379f2e1e8c9d7129\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt show 0e8dcb32ef115676cd7b6a2402a221fad4820553 -- jwt/__init__.py\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"2013 refactor splitting the error handling; parent already excluded RecursionError, so not the introducer.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/pickaxe_except_valueerror.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"84dbcb9fe53d988d64383a2fc6e3346b559081133d72802d9bf3951804fcb46b\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt log --all --oneline -S \\\\\\\"except ValueError as e\\\\\\\" -- jwt/api_jws.py jwt/api.py jwt/__init__.py\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Content carriers of the flawed except clause: ab8821f, 0e8dcb3, 5f255f9, a3f2ec3, 8556a15, 3b14696, 0657369.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/fix_0657369_diff.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"d2766f571047e92cde893fab3b7681ace25f4a6caefb5bba6714d2d54cd15e34\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt show 06573692ebcdec8831c3927513b3e87c31fbbb62\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Fix hunk except (ValueError, RecursionError) plus regression test.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/fix_0657369_catfile.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"aec489e497c3c7edff498b31a4769de649149440f150161aafb49a5243bc2f20\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt cat-file -p 06573692ebcdec8831c3927513b3e87c31fbbb62\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Fix metadata: human author/committer, SSH signature, subject-only message, no AI trailer.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/tags_containing_fix.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"f95d36da0d5ff9f73494a59f1ee239fae842a42512b55bd92ff680740715a16f\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt tag --contains 06573692ebcdec8831c3927513b3e87c31fbbb62\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"2.14.0, 2.15.0, 2.15.1 contain the fix.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/regression_2.13.0.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"6a9bbbea87e52aa855c47f20998b48dc3997a78d880f40037fd10e037ab78ceb\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"python3 scratch/check_rec.py scratch/v2130\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"RecursionError escapes 2.13.0 at the public jwt.decode boundary.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/regression_2.14.0.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"68031b673582e38fb9cf863bc6da46bd9705d3c473076feb206c355aa5144451\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"python3 scratch/check_rec.py scratch/v2140\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"2.14.0 raises DecodeError (PyJWTError); mechanism closed.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/regression_2.10.1.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"dbe0805d068054989bbeb2393ac24fd2d69d61911d473c501f5b8bbe38c15a31\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"python3 scratch/check_rec.py scratch/v2101\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"2.10.1 also escapes RecursionError: published range understates affected set.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/ai_commit_scan.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"d24205bc279a70269466afabbb6b2ec5e3dba04069e4f1aeccff3d0d2a9f677a\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt log --all --format=... | grep -iE \\\\\\\"claude|copilot\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"AI-authored/co-authored commits are 2026-only and unrelated to the header path.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/claude_commit_74961f1.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"d7555457973944308ddde73869824600b02eea865342e5511d78cfb805942d5f\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt show -s --format=... 74961f165765300dc6b366c6c2b3dc0d11b92bde\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Repo AI disclosure practice exists in 2026, far from the 2011 BIC.\\\"},\n+    {\\\"path\\\": \\\"evidence/clone_head.txt\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"3c5b1ab5cf4705784996efbf452a63a91ce0d4ff6e2d4a1840ecf90d316b6310\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"git -C jpadilla/pyjwt rev-parse HEAD\\\", \\\"observation\\\": \\\"Clone HEAD b5bd6fe6d7ac0370ba90557c7a1e3d50a9414572.\\\"}\n+  ],\n+  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Step 0: GHSA reviewed and CVE live => ACTIVE. Step 1: traced the real caller (jwt.decode -> PyJWS._load), the untrusted input (header segment), the operation (json.loads before signature verification) and the missing translation (RecursionError not caught), and reproduced the escape and the fix empirically at the public decode boundary. Step 2: immediate-parent/child comparison excludes 0e8dcb3 (refactor) and the moves; the earliest observable boundary is the root commit, which already excluded RecursionError, giving an atomic root-boundary BIC. Step 3: fix 0657369 is the first default-branch mechanism-closing change and ships in 2.14.0. Step 4: BIC and all carriers are named-human with no marker; repo AI activity is 2026-only and inadmissible. Therefore NOT