## Repair and shipment

On main, parent **`0c170ca13f70aafa8ade685406c913591900e1f4`** still has the shared pointer and direct invocation. Child **`d66ebd121c5a621ab0b03569fc75bd1cf829e52a`** removes the pointer, callback factory, callback binding and pointer assignments, and wires internal-router `onBadUrl`/`onMaxParamLength` to `options.routerOptions`. It is directly on the default branch's first-parent history, not a side-branch member whose later ancestry is being confused with integration. The implementation change and its tests are one coherent repair, so `fix_granularity: ATOMIC`.

`processOptions()`/`buildRouterOptions()` establish the router callbacks before both main and 404 routers are constructed. Defaults in `fastify.js` send a 400 FST_ERR_BAD_URL response and 414 FST_ERR_MAX_PARAM_LENGTH response respectively. They do not invoke an application not-found handler. A user-supplied `routerOptions.onBadUrl` or `frameworkErrors` handler is still deliberately invoked; its application-defined behavior is outside the claim that built-in dispatch now fails closed. The scoped fix claim is removal of the cross-prefix application-not-found dispatch under normal/default callbacks, and honoring explicitly configured error callbacks.

The advisory-linked **`93c239a380f3f2778bb7565fcdf777e91cfe1fbc`** is on 5.x, with parent **`7de6e81697778f9f41bd327a3b1c5c9a0d9637b4`**. It is not an ancestor of main. Its repaired 404 blob equals main's repaired blob, **`d994fd4309c64d5c391a9a853f186020d0b1c836`**. It belongs in `fix_shas` as another landing of the same repair, not as the default-branch `fix_sha`.

