{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 sh -c 'sed -n \\\"222,270p\\\" contract/scripts/README.md; sed -n \\\"285,329p\\\" contract/docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md; sed -n \\\"1,142p\\\" contract/scripts/audit_reduction_gate.py; python3 -c '\\\\''import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"inputs/00-github.json\\\")); print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k not in (\\\"description\\\",\\\"credits\\\",\\\"cvss\\\",\\\"cvss_severities\\\")},indent=2)); print(d[\\\"description\\\"][d[\\\"description\\\"].index(\\\"## Maintainer update — 2026-09-11\\\"):]); d=json.load(open(\\\"inputs/01-nvd.json\\\")); print(json.dumps(d,indent=2))'\\\\'''\"","aggregated_output":"## Submission\n\nSave the independent report and primary receipts before cross-reading. Receipts can be\nplain text: command/URL, repository, full object SHA/version, capture time, exit/HTTP\nresult and raw output. Preserve failed probes. Hash the receipts and keep original\noutputs immutable; corrections are new attempts linked to their originals.\n\nWrite report text and structured records with file patches or a script that serializes\ndata from files. Do not interpolate source quotations or whole JSON documents into\nnested shell command strings. After a quoting/write failure, inspect the actual files\nand diagnostics before continuing; a later successful check does not erase that failure.\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict <case.json>\npython3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict --repo <clone-dir> <case.json>\n```\n\nUse the frozen gate code and retain both outputs. The first checks structure; the second\nchecks commit quotes and parent links without fetching. Neither proves causal truth,\natomicity, absent AI use or web disclosure scope. Retain a failed local check with its\nalternative primary evidence or explicit research gap; never invent a value for `ok`.\nPrefer local Git and patch/raw/PR sources; avoid API calls while rate-limited.\n\nReject duplicate JSON keys and unfinished drafts. A crash, timeout, rate limit or empty\nresponse belongs in execution errors; resume within the assigned limits. Do not turn\nit into a researched gap or completed independent audit. An actual EVIDENCE_GAP names\nthe evidence sought, bounded probes/results and the next decisive question.\nSubmission, research acceptance and publication are separate states in the batch index.\n\nFor new batches adopting the research-work sidecar introduced in `2026-09-25.1`, bind the schema's\n[research-work contract](../docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md#research-work-contract) and invoke the\nreduction gate with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`. Its `research_work.worklist`\nincludes unfinished qualified conclusions as well as unresolved ones. Review\n`unassessed_cases` and the actual findings before treating an empty list as a handoff.\nBefore sealing an auditor sidecar, validate it with the frozen `check_research_work`\nand verify its receipt hashes. The leader checks each supplied sidecar before relying\non its work states; an invalid sidecar remains unassessed. Keep the independent\nsidecars with their sealed reports; the reduction gate validates the adjudicator's\nrecorded work, not the completeness of source discovery. Frozen old\nbatches continue using their pinned commands and contracts.\n\nComparison/reduction lane and accepted arguments accept exact record files or\nrecords-only directories. Use the original `record.json` for a one-case task; for a\nbatch, bind a complete view whose record bytes match the sealed originals. The directory\nloader recursively parses JSON, so source-response arrays, receipts and scratch checkouts\nbelong outside that view. Keep every manifest case and assigned lane, and retain the\noriginal reports and evidence for research and decision pins. A packaging retry preserves\nthe failed invocation and is not a fresh independent research attempt.\n\nthe code actually used. Historical batches retain their original contract; adoption of\nthis format must be explicit, not a retroactive claim that old runs followed it.\n\n### Research-work contract\n\nNew batches adopting the current contract retain the sidecar introduced in\n`2026-09-25.1`: set `reduction.research_contract` to\n`causal-work-v1` and freeze the gate invocation with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`.\nThe option rejects an omitted or different declaration; older frozen batches retain\ntheir existing contract. This is local coordination data, never ledger or site data.\n\nEach decision has a `research` object with `advisory`, `mechanism`, `bic`, `ai`, `fix`\nand `versions` entries. Auditors keep the same object in their owned research sidecar,\nlinked from the sealed report; adjudicators write their own synthesis in the decision.\nThe existing `basis`, `residual` resolution and per-dimension `missing_fact` describe\nthe remaining uncertainty. A single entry has this shape (not a prewritten finding):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"evidence_grade\": \"QUALIFIED_BOUNDARY\",\n  \"work_state\": \"UNFINISHED\",\n  \"finding\": \"State the supported causal conclusion, conditions and counterevidence.\",\n  \"evidence\": [{\"path\": \"evidence/source.txt\", \"sha256\": \"<64 hex>\"}],\n  \"missing_fact\": \"State the decisive fact still unknown.\",\n  \"next_permitted_route\": \"original-member\",\n  \"routes\": [{\n    \"id\": \"original-member\",\n    \"question\": \"Which parent/child change first introduced the relevant behavior?\",\n    \"source\": \"upstream repository history\",\n    \"evidence_type\": \"parent/child source comparison\",\n    \"status\": \"PENDING\"\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n`evidence_grade` is `BOUND`, `QUALIFIED_BOUNDARY` or `UNRESOLVED`. It describes the\nsupported conclusion, independently of work remaining. `BOUND` need not assert a\nvulnerability or an existing fix: an affirmative refutation or the keyed advisory's\ndocumented exclusion of further work can support a scoped conclusion. State that scope;\ndo not invent code findings for a rejected advisory or extend an absence claim.\nA `BOUND` finding has no decisive `missing_fact`: represent it with JSON null, not an\nempty string. Genuine remaining gaps use the other evidence grades and a named fact.\n\n`work_state` is `UNFINISHED` while an identified, permitted, decisive investigation\nremains, regardless of the grade or case verdict. `next_permitted_route` names a\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Check a reducer's evidence-backed decisions against exact input/output bytes.\n\nThis checks delivery integrity, not the truth of a causal judgment. See\ndocs/ADJUDICATION-PROTOCOL.md. It never assembles records or writes the ledger.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom audit_record_gates import AI_VERDICTS, check_record, check_record_strict, load_record, review_signals\nfrom compare_slots import RESEARCH_FIELDS, lane_paths, load_snapshot, research_differences_many\n\nPIN_ROLES = ('manifest', 'audit_protocol', 'reducer_protocol', 'schema', 'brief',\n             'record_gate', 'comparison', 'reduction_gate')\nRESEARCH_CONTRACT = 'causal-work-v1'\nWORK_DIMENSIONS = tuple(name for name in RESEARCH_FIELDS if name != 'residual')\nTERMINAL_ROUTES = {'ANSWERED', 'UNAVAILABLE', 'EXHAUSTED', 'PROHIBITED'}\n\n\ndef text(value) -> bool:\n    return isinstance(value, str) and bool(value.strip())\n\n\ndef check_research_work(research, label, receipt):\n    \"\"\"Validate recorded work, not the completeness of source discovery or causal truth.\"\"\"\n    problems, worklist, boundaries = [], [], []\n    counts = collections.Counter()\n    if not isinstance(research, dict):\n        return [f'{label}: research needs an object'], counts, worklist, boundaries\n    if set(research) != set(WORK_DIMENSIONS):\n        problems.append(f'{label}: research needs exactly {list(WORK_DIMENSIONS)}')\n\n    def evidence(value, where):\n        if not isinstance(value, list) or not value:\n            problems.append(f'{where}: needs retained evidence receipts')\n        else:\n            for item in value:\n                receipt(item, where)\n\n    for dimension in WORK_DIMENSIONS:\n        if dimension not in research:\n            continue\n        detail = research[dimension]\n        where = f'{label} research {dimension}'\n        if not isinstance(detail, dict):\n            problems.append(f'{where}: needs an object')\n            continue\n        grade, state = detail.get('evidence_grade'), detail.get('work_state')\n        if grade not in ('BOUND', 'QUALIFIED_BOUNDARY', 'UNRESOLVED'):\n            problems.append(f'{where}: invalid evidence_grade')\n        if state not in ('COMPLETE', 'UNFINISHED'):\n            problems.append(f'{where}: invalid work_state')\n        if not text(detail.get('finding')):\n            problems.append(f'{where}: needs the supported finding and its scope')\n        evidence(detail.get('evidence'), where)\n        if grade != 'BOUND' and not text(detail.get('missing_fact')):\n            problems.append(f'{where}: an unbound conclusion needs missing_fact')\n        if grade == 'BOUND' and detail.get('missing_fact') is not None:\n            problems.append(f'{where}: BOUND cannot retain a decisive missing_fact')\n        routes = detail.get('routes')\n        if not isinstance(routes, list):\n            problems.append(f'{where}: routes must be a list')\n            routes = []\n        route_ids, identities, pending = set(), set(), set()\n        for route in routes:\n            if not isinstance(route, dict):\n                problems.append(f'{where}: each route must be an object')\n                continue\n            route_id = route.get('id')\n            if not text(route_id) or route_id in route_ids:\n                problems.append(f'{where}: route IDs must be nonempty and unique')\n                continue\n            route_ids.add(route_id)\n            identity = tuple(route.get(key) for key in ('question', 'source', 'evidence_type'))\n            if not all(text(part) for part in identity):\n                problems.append(f'{where} route {route_id}: needs question, source and evidence_type')\n            else:\n                identity = tuple(part.strip() for part in identity)\n                if identity in identities:\n                    problems.append(f'{where}: duplicate evidence route {route_id}')\n                identities.add(identity)\n            outcome = route.get('status')\n            if outcome in ('PENDING', 'FAILED'):\n                pending.add(route_id)\n            elif not text(outcome) or outcome not in TERMINAL_ROUTES:\n                problems.append(f'{where} route {route_id}: invalid status')\n            if outcome != 'PENDING':\n                if not text(route.get('observation')):\n                    problems.append(f'{where} route {route_id}: needs its actual observation')\n                evidence(route.get('evidence'), f'{where} route {route_id}')\n        next_route = detail.get('next_permitted_route')\n        if state == 'COMPLETE':\n            counts['COMPLETE'] += 1\n            if pending or 'next_permitted_route' not in detail or next_route is not None:\n                problems.append(f'{where}: COMPLETE contradicts unfinished routes or a next route')\n            if grade != 'BOUND':\n                boundaries.append(dimension)\n                if not routes:\n                    problems.append(f'{where}: an unbound COMPLETE finding needs a recorded evidence frontier')\n        elif state == 'UNFINISHED':\n            counts['UNFINISHED'] += 1\n            if not text(next_route) or next_route not in pending:\n                problems.append(f'{where}: UNFINISHED needs a next_permitted_route naming a PENDING or FAILED route')\n            worklist.append({'dimension': dimension, 'next_permitted_route': next_route})\n    return problems, counts, worklist, boundaries\n\n\ndef digest(path: Path) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef manifest_ids(path: Path) -> set[str]:\n    ids = []\n    for line in path.read_text().splitlines():\n        if not line.strip():\n            continue\n        value = load_record(line).get('class_id') if line.lstrip().startswith('{') else line.strip()\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError('manifest: each row needs a class_id')\n        ids.append(value)\n    if not ids or len(ids) != len(set(ids)):\n        raise ValueError('manifest: empty or duplicate case IDs')\n    return set(ids)\n\n\ndef check_delivery(manifest: Path, accepted: Path, decisions: Path,\n                   a: Path | None = None, b: Path | None = None,\n                   lanes: dict[str, Path] | None = None,\n                   research_contract: str | None = None) -> dict:\n    paths = lane_paths([f'{name}={path}' for name, path in lanes.items()] if lanes else None, a, b)\n    if accepted.resolve() in {path.resolve() for path in paths.values()}:\n        raise ValueError('accepted output must be separate from independent inputs')\n    problems, observed = [], {manifest.resolve(): digest(manifest)}\n    expected = manifest_ids(manifest)\n    decision_bytes = decisions.read_bytes()\n    document = load_record(decision_bytes.decode('utf-8'))\n    index = document.get('reduction', document)\n{\n  \"ghsa_id\": \"GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n  \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-102265\",\n  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n  \"summary\": \"PyJWT: Uncaught RecursionError in jwt.decode() on deeply nested token header\",\n  \"type\": \"reviewed\",\n  \"severity\": \"medium\",\n  \"repository_advisory_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/jpadilla/pyjwt/security-advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n  \"source_code_location\": \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt\",\n  \"identifiers\": [\n    {\n      \"value\": \"GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n      \"type\": \"GHSA\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"value\": \"CVE-2026-102265\",\n      \"type\": \"CVE\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n    \"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-102265\",\n    \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/06573692ebcdec8831c3927513b3e87c31fbbb62\",\n    \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases/tag/2.14.0\",\n    \"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\"\n  ],\n  \"published_at\": \"2026-09-29T23:43:06Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-29T23:43:07Z\",\n  \"github_reviewed_at\": \"2026-09-29T23:43:06Z\",\n  \"nvd_published_at\": \"2026-09-28T21:17:14Z\",\n  \"withdrawn_at\": null,\n  \"vulnerabilities\": [\n    {\n      \"package\": {\n        \"ecosystem\": \"pip\",\n        \"name\": \"pyJWT\"\n      },\n      \"vulnerable_version_range\": \">= 2.13.0, < 2.14.0\",\n      \"first_patched_version\": \"2.14.0\",\n      \"vulnerable_functions\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cwes\": [\n    {\n      \"cwe_id\": \"CWE-674\",\n      \"name\": \"Uncontrolled Recursion\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": 2,\n  \"epss\": {\n    \"percentage\": 0.00291,\n    \"percentile\": 0.19505\n  }\n}\n## Maintainer update — 2026-09-11\n\nThe verified fix for this advisory is included in PyJWT 2.14.0, released on 2026-09-11 and available on PyPI. PyJWT 2.14.0 is the first release containing the fix. This advisory is now published with 2.14.0 recorded as the patched version.\n{\n  \"id\": \"CVE-2026-102265\",\n  \"sourceIdentifier\": \"security-advisories@github.com\",\n  \"published\": \"2026-09-28T21:17:14.077\",\n  \"lastModified\": \"2026-10-01T15:17:25.207\",\n  \"vulnStatus\": \"Awaiting Analysis\",\n  \"cveTags\": [],\n  \"descriptions\": [\n    {\n      \"lang\": \"en\",\n      \"value\": \"PyJWT is a Python implementation of JSON Web Token standards. From 2.13.0 until 2.14.0, PyJWS._load in jwt/api_jws.py is affected because parser catches ValueError but not RecursionError. This occurs when a deeply nested token header reaches json.loads. As a result, RecursionError escapes the documented PyJWT error hierarchy. Consequently, an unauthenticated malformed token can cause a request-level failure and HTTP 500. This issue is fixed in version 2.14.0.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"affected\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"security-advisories@github.com\",\n      \"affectedData\": [\n        {\n          \"vendor\": \"jpadilla\",\n          \"product\": \"pyjwt\",\n          \"versions\": [\n            {\n              \"version\": \">= 2.13.0, < 2.14.0\",\n              \"status\": \"affected\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"cvssMetricV31\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"security-advisories@github.com\",\n        \"type\": \"Secondary\",\n        \"cvssData\": {\n          \"version\": \"3.1\",\n          \"vectorString\": \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L\",\n          \"baseScore\": 5.3,\n          \"baseSeverity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n          \"attackVector\": \"NETWORK\",\n          \"attackComplexity\": \"LOW\",\n          \"privilegesRequired\": \"NONE\",\n          \"userInteraction\": \"NONE\",\n          \"scope\": \"UNCHANGED\",\n          \"confidentialityImpact\": \"NONE\",\n          \"integrityImpact\": \"NONE\",\n          \"availabilityImpact\": \"LOW\"\n        },\n        \"exploitabilityScore\": 3.9,\n        \"impactScore\": 1.4\n      }\n    ],\n    \"ssvcV203\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0\",\n        \"ssvcData\": {\n          \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:00:55.850520Z\",\n          \"id\": \"CVE-2026-102265\",\n          \"options\": [\n            {\n              \"exploitation\": \"poc\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"automatable\": \"yes\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"technicalImpact\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"role\": \"CISA Coordinator\",\n          \"version\": \"2.0.3\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"weaknesses\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"security-advisories@github.com\",\n      \"type\": \"Secondary\",\n      \"description\": [\n        {\n          \"lang\": \"en\",\n          \"value\": \"CWE-674\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/06573692ebcdec8831c3927513b3e87c31fbbb62\",\n      \"source\": \"security-advisories@github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases/tag/2.14.0\",\n      \"source\": \"security-advisories@github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n      \"source\": \"security-advisories@github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-8wjv-2p76-3863\",\n      \"source\": \"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
