   }\n  ],\n  \"raw_metadata\": \"tree 7244edac61ea44652de03c1ded8dec3439eab343\\nparent 6b1194c9093e768f778ede56b29fa363fe5912b4\\nauthor Florian Lefebvre <contact@florian-lefebvre.dev> 1788341824 +0200\\ncommitter Florian Lefebvre <contact@florian-lefebvre.dev> 1788341824 +0200\\n\\nfeat(actions): validate JSON actions with Standard Schema\\n\\nThe `input` of a JSON action now accepts any Standard Schema validator \\u2014 Zod,\\nValibot, ArkType, and others \\u2014 instead of only Zod, and the actions runtime no\\nlonger pulls Zod in to validate them.\\n\\nForm actions keep their Zod schema, since turning `FormData` into the value a\\nschema expects needs more introspection than the spec describes. That `input` is\\nnow deprecated and delegates to `@standard-community/standard-form`, a new\\nplaceholder package expected to move to the standard-community org, structured\\nafter its sibling `standard-json`: handlers are resolved from `~standard.vendor`\\nand imported lazily, with only Zod implemented.\\n\\n`ActionInputError#issues` stays typed as Zod issues for backwards compatibility.\\nIssues from another validator are normalized to Zod's `custom` code, and `fields`\\nis built from the spec's shape either way. It becomes `StandardSchemaV1.Issue[]`\\nin Astro 8.\\n\\n`defineAction` now rejects an `input` that is not a Standard Schema validator, or\\nthat is not a Zod schema on a form action, the way collection schemas are checked.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Cla\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
