'path': 'packages/integrations/netlify/src/index.ts', 'blob': 'e42f52f6eb79f202ae46248279a66659fe5c1027'}] tree 707f7ece4fdfdac21e43bd3e3434bc1574901448\nparent cf9ffc72258b23211eb07f4f38176756812b373d\nauthor Fred K. Schott <622227+FredKSchott@users.noreply.github.com> 1784609620 -0700\ncommitter Fred K. Schott <622227+FredKSchott@users.noreply.github.com> 1784609620 -0700\n\nFix dual React instances after mid-session SSR dep re-optimization in @astrojs/cloudflare dev\n\nWhen Vite's SSR dep optimizer discovered a new dependency mid-session\n(e.g. a newly added island importing a package outside the pre-optimized\nset), the re-optimization renamed optimized dep URLs. Modules already\nevaluated in the workerd module runner kept the old React copy while new\nmodules loaded the new one, so hooks failed with \"Invalid hook call\" /\n\"Cannot read properties of null\" in every island.\n\n`@cloudflare/vite-plugin` defaults `optimizeDeps.ignoreOutdatedRequests`\nto `true` in the workerd environment, which suppresses the\nERR_OUTDATED_OPTIMIZED_DEP error Vite relies on for recovery. Override\nit to `false` for server environments so a request racing the\nre-optimization fails fast and the next render sees a single React.\n\nFixes #17364\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nd4f266de4af009876baa554708705e5ac36572bb [{'path': 'packages/integrations/netlify/src/index.ts', 'blob': 'e42f52f6eb79f202ae46248279a66659fe5c1027'}] tree 7e7791f885f00febb89a20e99ee1e0ec99a464ad\nparent 2e83040aefe733006b89d608ab4c6817f8b6d676\nauthor emerson lopes <24904209+emerson-d-lopes@users.noreply.github.com> 1785007719 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785007719 -0400\ngpgsig -----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n \n wsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZQ5nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhusQABvWzLwdUCIejcTaG0HPOVle\n 0Sle1ttK1rIQ4hFFG9HN66aDB/960kiOY6cN/C5TBqLGm27BsMHLVC2xy+ZoREfB\n 21IoIr/T1dZt2mMQ3MzNLezh3cywgsDZbL5zxumwuoWh2OPsTOPjaUJ6e1qDKcCh\n BWx5y6VwdxhywiYwVF9u/vJWcMYEouxp9CeQ8hxIau6+BwyhDopa8YGYoAiwNpqe\n hRKZXWlFiO3H+0HmR9mOrFmZOZBqQT5BSjrt8Jz0L2aOYUrpHNMV4xvNTcvhD1Y9\n lZvCuc9L2NDcEYap2qaINlMVHTBeSxBrlr16Y0RsAsKQKo5nWAP2kDgQTr//IsmM\n q2Ie1BIlV9/CBJ4VZV73Rdp4UIKvDumAkTedJJnCZDXdTCIeYBI4g1EMmbk9lVtx\n aYfwD+Rx6c4WY1TToP5AJpBsLlhTEGMgSniDQur0QrZR8HkNrK9a2E/OjsEjjtzJ\n ZX0IUhnWdEh5goqE+/nU4X6p3K0xkW77sOSLuOtlWiYcDIX2xvUPRU8GKTjisCIs\n 6Y2ZXNKu0gFUbFQtIfBbQS2tKNpfNE2PZxWQmERXQQX0BOTJGM8y2FwNfBTFwgGF\n bxOhbBQokYy9tNZRq5UnDnz/pa1vcfsPIPv5sNvclmjYC4QMqIPGiiexahQqP1/s\n VvOoS3OEqwRynaF6Ol52\n =yYcX\n -----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n \n\nfix(build): deduplicate CSS assets between prerender and SSR environments (#17488)\n\n* fix(build): deduplicate CSS assets between prerender and SSR environments\n\nIn server output, the prerender and SSR environments each bundle shared\nlayouts separately, emitting one CSS asset per environment for the same\nCSS source modules (e.g. `index.X.css` and `_..Y.css`). The prerender\nbuild now records its CSS asset filenames keyed by each chunk's CSS\nmodule set, and the SSR build renames its matching assets to the\nprerender filenames, so moving assets to the client directory yields a\nsingle file referenced by both page types.\n\nKeyed by module identity rather than content hash because plugins that\nscan the environment module graph (e.g. Tailwind) can produce slightly\ndifferent content for the same CSS source in each environment.\n\nThe rename mutates `asset.fileName` in place instead of re-keying the\nbundle object: the bundle is a Rolldown proxy that ignores direct key\nassignment, and the writer emits files based on `fileName`.\n\nFixes #17298\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U5TQ1y3yBEDx73tYTHoUBj\n\n* test: cover multi-page and unique-CSS cases for prerender/SSR dedup\n\nExtends the fixture with a second prerendered page, and a server-only\npage with its own stylesheet, asserting that all pages share one\ndeduplicated file while CSS unique to a server-rendered page is still\nemitted and linked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U5TQ1y3yBEDx73tYTHoUBj\n\n* chore: retrigger CI\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U5TQ1y3yBEDx73tYTHoUBj\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
