pation, not dismissed because the earlier origin was human.\n+\n+Sources: `origin-parent-history.txt`, `origin-parent.ts`, `origin-member.ts`, `origin-landing.ts`, `adapters-pr187*.json`, `causal-identity.txt`, `june-hardening.txt`, `june-member-details.txt`, `hardening-members.txt`, and bounded ref-fetch receipts. The owned clone is non-shallow and non-promisor. No shared Git clone was modified.\n+\n+## Contribution-specific AI evidence\n+\n+The original member names **Matt Kane <matt.kane@netlify.com>**. June/July/repair members name **Matthew Phillips** with recovered addresses. No examined causal member or relevant PR disclosure supplies an AI marker. At the original member'\"'s parent the actual \"'`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` asks for changes, testing and docs without AI disclosure; a 30-commit contemporary sample shows ordinary human/coauthor/automation metadata without an observed AI convention. The initial lowercase template probe failed and was corrected to the actual uppercase path; both observations are retained.\n+\n+After the bounded PR/source-history recoveries, a `cat-file --batch-all-objects` inventory covers **19,357** local commit objects, including any objects unreachable from refs. Both historical paths were checked in every commit. Seven target blobs locate **543** exact-content carriers, whose complete metadata is retained. The broader function-content scan covers **4,596** carriers and **97** distinct index.ts blobs, retaining full metadata and checking AI-marked commits against their first-parent source diff. It found zero AI-marked source-changing commits in that universe. Some descendants retain the Netlify blob while their AI trailers refer to unrelated content/Cloudflare/build changes; unchanged carriage is not code authorship or new Netlify exposure. This is a bounded local/public attribution finding, not proof of private non-use of AI.\n+\n+Sources: `final-carrier-path-universe.txt`, `final-carrier-metadata.json`, `final-hunk-car