{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 sh -c 'cat sealed-auditors/auditor2/REPORT.md; cat additional-primary/README.md; ls additional-primary; ls inputs; ls contract/scripts; ls retained-git/auditor1 retained-git/auditor2'\"","aggregated_output":"# Independent audit report — alias-348fd55a42f6b70e3521be0e\n\nTask 53e64c109ea403aa5ba7ce4a3f8e26914e8744355c5fa1eadffedc3a1bb40a53\nBatch incremental-causal-20261004-case-048, role auditor2, attempt 1.\nContract: audit protocol 2026-09-27.3, research contract causal-work-v1.\nCoverage cutoff 2026-10-04T08:13:00Z. Repository: expressjs/morgan (npm `morgan`).\nAll Git commands ran as `numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1` with\n`GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in an owned full clone\n`/tmp/morgan-scratch/morgan`. Receipts: `evidence/`.\n\n## 0. Advisory status and identity\n\nThe keyed advisory GHSA-9F6G-J8CH-79G4 (CVE-2026-87859) is reachable as an official\nGitHub global advisory: `ghsa_id` matches, `published_at` valid (2026-09-28T21:33:08Z),\n`withdrawn_at` explicitly `null` => disposition ACTIVE. The advisory is `reviewed`,\nseverity medium, CVSS 3.1 5.3 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N), CWE-117, and it\ndeclares itself an incomplete fix of CVE-2026-5078 and CVE-2026-15603. Its own text does\nnot contradict its live state, so it is not dead. Both prior advisories were consulted\nand are also ACTIVE (GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m/CVE-2026-5078, 1.11.0;\nGHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m/CVE-2026-15603, 1.12.0). Evidence: `evidence/00-github.json`,\n`evidence/prior-GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m.json`, `evidence/prior-GHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m.json`,\n`evidence/receipt-prior-advisories.txt`.\n\n## 1. Reported behavior and mechanism (observed)\n\n`morgan` writes request-derived token values into one-line access-log records. The\n`combined`, `common` and `default` formats wrap several tokens in literal double quotes\n(`\":user-agent\"`, `:referrer`/`\":referrer\"`, `:url`, `\":remote-user\"`). From 1.11.0 the\nhelper `escapeLogField` neutralizes control characters; from 1.12.0 it also neutralizes\n`U+007F-U+009F`, `U+2028`, `U+2029` and backslash, and the `token()` wrapper routes every\nstring token through it. The character class never contained `\"` (0x22), the field\ndelimiter of the emitted format. An attacker who controls a quoted field (User-Agent,\nReferer, request URL, Basic-auth username) can therefore emit a raw `\"` that closes the\nfield early and forges additional fields in the log record (log injection / forging,\nCWE-117). Receipts: `evidence/receipt-remediation-diffs.txt`,\n`evidence/receipt-parent-and-regex.txt`: the escaping regex reads\n`[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f\\\\]` at b3f5d9b (1.11.0), `[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\u2028\\u2029\\\\]`\nat fbf9383 (1.12.0), and `[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\u2028\\u2029\"\\\\]` after the fix\n4b695edf (1.12.1). This is genuine, not a wrong-product report; no counterevidence refutes\nthe mechanism, so FALSE_POSITIVE does not apply.\n\n## 2. Introduction and exposure; BIC (observed + inference)\n\nThe vulnerable behavior — a quoted log field whose delimiter is not escaped — long\npredates the mitigations: a full non-shallow clone shows the `:user-agent`/combined\nformat already present in the root/import commit 79622119370961349101f676965987320013835b\n(2014-02-08, \"asdf\", an import of the older Connect logger whose header credits 2010\nSencha / 2011 TJ Holowaychuk). The advisory's own words make this an *incomplete\nremediation* of CVE-2026-5078 and CVE-2026-15603, so the smallest logically atomic change\nthat carries the defect *as the advisory describes it* is an escaping implementation that\nomits the delimiter:\n\n- b3f5d9bdb388690dfae9c06ab966328f49b7982b (1.11.0) first added `escapeLogField` with the\n  incomplete class, but applied it only to `:remote-user`.\n- fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe (1.12.0) extended the class and — decisively —\n  wrapped **all** string tokens, so the incomplete escaping now covers the quoted fields\n  the advisory names (`:user-agent`, `:referrer`, `:url`). Its immediate parent\n  03383991f55ec5d5e2c0cbdeb783a252f27196a5 still carries `[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f\\\\]` and no\n  token wrapper.\n\nI bind **introducer_sha = fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe**, ATOMIC,\n`landing_basis INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT` (it is a normal single-parent commit directly on the\ndefault branch; `git tag --contains` reaches 1.12.0/1.12.1, and the 1.12.0 release commit\n063f084a8de1fe02e52333f0b5df2533ced85e42 has fbf9383 as its only-parent descent). Competing\nexplanation retained: b3f5d9b is the origin of the escaping helper and the first incomplete\nfix; the pre-1.11.0 origin is a pre-VCS/import boundary (NON_GIT_BOUNDARY-like). The choice\nbetween these candidates does **not** change the AI verdict, because all three carry named\nhuman identities and no AI marker (see §4). Evidence:\n`evidence/receipt-parent-and-regex.txt`, `evidence/receipt-remediation-diffs.txt`,\n`evidence/receipt-object-enumeration.txt`.\n\n## 3. Repair and release (observed)\n\nFix `4b695edf967ce179cdf4009fe8cddd184b7511ee` (\"fix: escape double quotes in log fields\",\nauthor/committer Ulises Gascón <ulisesgascongonzalez@gmail.com>) adds `\"` to the class and\n`case '\\\"': return '\\\\\"'`, plus two tests; it is the first mechanism-closing change on the\ndefault branch and lands in released tag `1.12.1`\n(`b1272e70812dbc504321eeb5a43d14b0822c150d`, whose parent is 4b695edf). `fix_granularity`\nATOMIC, `fix_sha`/`direct_fix_sha` = 4b695edf, no other landings. The advisory's patched\nrange `< 1.12.1 -> 1.12.1` is consistent with the tag content: HISTORY.md 1.12.1 names\nCVE-2026-87859. The residual (the unescaped quote) is closed by 4b695edf; the phrase\n\"incomplete fix\" in the advisory names the historical 1.11.0/1.12.0 state, not an open\nsurface, so `residual_triage` = NOT-RESIDUAL. Evidence:\n`evidence/receipt-fix-commit.txt`, `evidence/receipt-releases.txt`.\n\n## 4. AI participation (observed; this is the decisive question)\n\nThe causal content (the `escapeLogField` regex and the `token()` wrapper) was inspected\nacross **all** local objects, not just ref-reachable commits:\n`git cat-file --batch-all-objects --batch-check` yields 428 commit objects in a\nnon-shallow clone, and each message was read. No agent/bot author, AI co-author trailer or\nfirst-person AI disclosure appears on b3f5d9b, fbf9383 or 4b695edf, nor on any other local\ncommit carrying that content. The only AI-looking trailer in the whole history is\n`Co-authored-by: EvoX <evox@evomap.ai>` on 286b000228cacba362bfa89791c6268663f86610\n(\"test: run CI on Windows and macOS (#379)\") — an unrelated CI commit, not the causal\nchange, so it is repository-level context and is **not admissible** to the BIC. The 1.12.0\ncommit's only trailer, `Co-authored-by: M. Fazri Nizar <anon6372098.id@gmail.com>`, is a\nnamed human, not an AI marker. Authors/committers are named humans: b3f5d9b Jon Church\n<me@jonchurch.com> (committer `GitHub <noreply@github.com>`), fbf9383 Sebastian Beltran\n<bjohansebas@gmail.com> (committer Ulises Gascón), 4b695edf Ulises Gascón.\n\nVerdict **NOT_AI**: the BIC object (fbf9383) has a recovered named-human identity\n(`identity_class: human`), no object-local AI marker, and the repo's disclosure convention\nis present (AI co-authors *are* credited by trailer, e.g. EvoX) yet unused on the causal\nobject (`CONVENTION_PRESENT_UNUSED`, observed at the 2026-08/09 date). No `ai_on_bic`\nattribution. Evidence: `evidence/receipt-ai-marker-scan.txt`,\n`evidence/receipt-object-enumeration.txt`.\n\n## 5. Version scope\n\nVulnerable `< 1.12.1`; first patched `1.12.1`. Source-release finding; not extended to\nuninspected binaries/platforms. Evidence: `evidence/00-github.json`,\n`evidence/receipt-releases.txt`.\n\n## 6. Boundaries, failures, flip condition\n\n- The BIC could alternatively be placed at b3f5d9b (first incomplete fix) or at the\n  pre-VCS import boundary. These are recorded as competing candidates; none carries AI\n  evidence, so the verdict is stable under all three.\n- No execution failures: clone, all Git reads, gates and API fetches exited 0 (receipts).\n- `flip_condition`: an object-local AI marker (agent/bot author, AI co-author trailer, or\n  a first-person AI disclosure) on the escaping content — or a first-party disclosure bound\n  to that change — would move the verdict to AI_CODE_FLAWED.\ncat: additional-primary/README.md: No such file or directory\nSOURCE-QUESTIONS.txt\n00-github.json\nREADME.md\nSOURCES.json\nREADME.md\naudit_dispatch.py\naudit_record_gates.py\naudit_reduction_gate.py\nclaims.py\ncompare_slots.py\nledger_store.py\nretained-git/auditor1:\n01.git\n02.git\nSOURCES.json\n\nretained-git/auditor2:\nSOURCES.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
