r releases the lock. An expired foreign claim also blocks ledger writes.\n\nHistorical logs stay append-only and readable; no bulk rewrite or cleanup is needed.\nOld slot holders remain occupied until individually released, so a new leader cannot\nclaim that case prematurely. `release --slot <old-slot>` targets such a holder; legacy\nrecords may close without a receipt ID, and old `done` calls remain a release-only alias.\nNew claims always require their receipt ID for release; `--result` stores no verdict.\nNew per-lane claims, `pick` and `sweep` are disabled. Update old dispatchers/TSV readers\nbefore reuse; `list` now emits JSONL. Never run frozen old claim tools against new claims.\n\n## Submission\n\nSave the independent report and primary receipts before cross-reading. Receipts can be\nplain text: command/URL, repository, full object SHA/version, capture time, exit/HTTP\nresult and raw output. Preserve failed probes. Hash the receipts and keep original\noutputs immutable; corrections are new attempts linked to their originals.\n\nWrite report text and structured records with file patches or a script that serializes\ndata from files. Do not interpolate source quotations or whole JSON documents into\nnested shell command strings. After a quoting/write failure, inspect the actual files\nand diagnostics before continuing; a later successful check does not erase that failure.\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict <case.json>\npython3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict --repo <clone-dir> <case.json>\n```\n\nUse the frozen gate code and retain both outputs. The first checks structure; the second\nchecks commit quotes and parent links without fetching. Neither proves causal truth,\natomicity, absent AI use or web disclosure scope. Retain a failed local check with its\nalternative primary evidence or explicit research gap; never invent a value for `ok`.\nPrefer local Git and patch/raw/PR sources; avoid API calls while rate-limited.\n\nReject duplicate JSON keys and unfinished drafts. A crash, timeout, rate limit or empty\nresponse belongs in execution errors; resume within the assigned limits. Do not turn\nit into a researched gap or completed independent audit. An actual EVIDENCE_GAP names\nthe evidence sought, bounded probes/results and the next decisive question.\nSubmission, research acceptance and publication are separate states in the batch index.\n\nFor new batches adopting the research-work sidecar introduced in `2026-09-25.1`, bind the schema's\n[research-work contract](../docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md#research-work-contract) and invoke the\nreduction gate with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`. Its `research_work.worklist`\nincludes unfinished qualified conclusions as well as unresolved ones. Review\n`unassessed_cases` and the actual findings before treating an empty list as a handoff.\nsupported, qualified, contradicted or unresolved, and which missing observation would\nchange each decision. Keep an unknown AI attribution separate from an established\nmechanism or repair. A missing platform artifact need not block a supported source-release\nresult; an unresolved part of the advisory cannot be excluded merely to obtain closure.\nApply the frozen acceptance threshold to the stated claim. Preserve legitimate-operation\ncontrasts and state/configuration qualifications. Report newly established facts and\nchanged decisions; repeated prose, hashes and passing checks are not research progress.\n\nA demonstrated partial repair can settle the repair question while leaving the defect\nopen. Do not wait for a future vendor fix to explain that state. Likewise, affirmative\nrefutation of the keyed mechanism is a finding; apply its frozen verdict requirements\nwithout inventing an introduction for behavior that the evidence contradicts. Keep a\nfuture condition that would change a finding separate from an available unanswered\nquestion. Neither conditional scope nor a terminal route label closes unread work.\nIf the frozen schema cannot represent a supported finding, retain it in the report and\nidentify the representation conflict for the leader. Do not invent causal roles or turn\nthat contract limitation into uncertainty about an already answered mechanism.\nFor current-contract false positives, use its explicit not-applicable nulls and\naffirmative grounds. Check the keyed advisory's status against its aliases; a\nwithdrawn alias does not dispose of an otherwise live vulnerability cluster.\n\n## Deliver a coherent synthesis\n\nWrite the final account, records and decisions together. Use the frozen schema's causal\nroles and unknown representations: metadata alone cannot establish atomicity, a missing\nmarker cannot establish no AI, and an unproved repair is not an unreadable or nonexistent\nfix. Preserve observed objects in evidence without inventing their roles.\n\nRead the completed files back and reconcile their material qualifications. Replace\nsuperseded assertions and answered next-question fields throughout the current synthesis,\nrecords and worklist, preserving original auditor artifacts unchanged. A contradictory\naddendum is not a correction. Verify execution claims against raw results or the original\ntrace. A successful process exit, an older valid skeleton or a failed wait does not prove\nthe completed research was written. Preserve original failures, reject duplicate JSON\nkeys and keep execution, input completeness and causal uncertainty distinct.\nKeep release qualifications in the structured fields as well as the report. A source-tag\ncomparison and a registry upload timestamp do not establish the contents of that uploaded\npackage; verify its bytes or retain the narrower source-release finding throughout.\n\nRun the frozen record checks and reduction gate on the final bytes with the original\nmanifest and every assigned lane. Keep raw results and hashes outside the checked files;\n{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-348fd55a42f6b70e3521be0e\",\n  \"task_id\": \"