{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc 'numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 cat sealed-auditors/auditor2/record.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"class_id\": \"alias-348fd55a42f6b70e3521be0e\",\n  \"advisory_ids\": [\n    \"GHSA-9F6G-J8CH-79G4\",\n    \"CVE-2026-87859\"\n  ],\n  \"advisory_disposition\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"advisory_aliases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GHSA-9F6G-J8CH-79G4\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CVE-2026-87859\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GHSA-4VJ7-5MJ6-JM8M\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CVE-2026-5078\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"GHSA-JXFW-X594-9X9M\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CVE-2026-15603\",\n      \"state\": \"ACTIVE\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verdict\": \"NOT_AI\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"morgan emits one-line access logs; the combined/common/default formats wrap :user-agent, :referrer, :url and :remote-user in literal double quotes. escapeLogField (1.11.0) and the token() wrapper (1.12.0) neutralize control characters, U+007F-U+009F, U+2028/U+2029 and backslash but never the double quote 0x22, the field delimiter, so a request field containing a raw quote can close the field early and forge extra log fields (CWE-117).\",\n  \"bug_semantics\": \"Improper output neutralization for logs: the escaping character class omits the field delimiter used by the emitted Apache-combined-style format.\",\n  \"introducer_sha\": \"fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe\",\n  \"introducer_parent\": \"03383991f55ec5d5e2c0cbdeb783a252f27196a5\",\n  \"bic_granularity\": \"ATOMIC\",\n  \"decomposed_shas\": [],\n  \"decomposition_probe\": null,\n  \"landing_commit\": null,\n  \"landing_basis\": \"INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT\",\n  \"landing_note\": \"fbf9383 is a normal single-parent commit directly on the default branch (parent 0338399); the 1.12.0 release commit 063f084 has fbf9383 as its first parent, and git tag --contains reaches 1.12.0/1.12.1. No separate carrier object exists, so landing_commit is null per INTRODUCER_ON_DEFAULT.\",\n  \"bic_note\": \"The advisory frames this as an incomplete remediation, so the BIC is the change that made the incomplete escaping cover the quoted fields it names: fbf9383 (1.12.0) wrapped every string token and extended the class, while its parent 0338399 still had [\\\\u0000-\\\\u001f\\\\u007f\\\\\\\\] applied only to :remote-user. b3f5d9b (1.11.0) is the retained earlier incomplete hardening; the pre-1.11.0 raw-token origin is a pre-VCS/import boundary at root 7962211. All carry named humans, so the choice does not affect the verdict.\",\n  \"fix_sha\": \"4b695edf967ce179cdf4009fe8cddd184b7511ee\",\n  \"direct_fix_sha\": \"4b695edf967ce179cdf4009fe8cddd184b7511ee\",\n  \"fix_granularity\": \"ATOMIC\",\n  \"atomic_repair_sha\": null,\n  \"fix_note\": \"4b695edf adds 0x22 to the escape class and case '\\\"' -> '\\\\\\\"' plus two regression tests; it is the first mechanism-closing change on the default branch and lands in 1.12.1 (b1272e7, whose parent is 4b695edf). HISTORY.md 1.12.1 names CVE-2026-87859; the <1.12.1 -> 1.12.1 range is consistent.\",\n  \"ai_on_bic\": false,\n  \"ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"ABSENT\"\n  },\n  \"fix_ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"ABSENT\"\n  },\n  \"ai_evidence\": \"All 428 local commit objects were enumerated (git cat-file --batch-all-objects) in a non-shallow clone and each message read. No agent/bot author, AI co-author trailer or first-person AI disclosure appears on fbf9383, b3f5d9b or 4b695edf, nor on any local commit carrying the escaping content. The single AI-looking trailer in the history is a Co-authored-by trailer from EvoX <evox@evomap.ai> on 286b000 (an unrelated CI commit), which is not admissible to the BIC. The trailer on fbf9383, M. Fazri Nizar <anon6372098.id@gmail.com>, is a named human. Authors are named humans: Jon Church (b3f5d9b), Sebastian Beltran (fbf9383), Ulises Gascon (4b695edf).\",\n  \"ai_admissibility\": \"The only AI-looking evidence (EvoX <evox@evomap.ai> on 286b000, a CI commit) is repository-level context; it does not carry the escapeLogField content and is not admitted as BIC attribution. The BIC-side marker is therefore ABSENT within the fully inspected carrier set, and no first-party disclosure bound to the causal change exists in the inspected sources.\",\n  \"identity_class\": \"human\",\n  \"disclosure_convention\": \"CONVENTION_PRESENT_UNUSED\",\n  \"flaw_origin\": {\n    \"sha\": \"79622119370961349101f676965987320013835b\",\n    \"note\": \"Root/import commit (2014-02-08, Jonathan Ong) of the Connect logger into morgan; it already emits quoted, unescaped token fields, i.e. the pre-mitigation origin of the vulnerable behavior. Pre-VCS boundary (header credits 2010 Sencha / 2011 TJ Holowaychuk); treated as context, not as the AI question.\"\n  },\n  \"remaining_gap\": \"None for the AI question: no AI marker exists on any inspected carrier of the escaping logic, so NOT_AI is bound. The only open point is a judgment on BIC placement among fbf9383 (chosen), b3f5d9b and the pre-1.11.0 import boundary; it is recorded as a competing candidate and does not change the verdict.\",\n  \"flip_condition\": \"An object-local AI marker (an agent/bot author, an AI co-author trailer, or a first-person AI disclosure) on the escaping content of fbf9383/b3f5d9b, or a first-party disclosure bound to that causal change, would move the verdict to AI_CODE_FLAWED. Discovering a later, non-Anthropic carrier of the same escaping blob with an AI marker would do the same.\",\n  \"residual_triage\": {\n    \"decision\": \"NOT-RESIDUAL\",\n    \"basis\": \"The advisory phrase 'incomplete fix' / 'incomplete remediation' names the historical 1.11.0 and 1.12.0 escaping states, not an open surface: the residual unescaped double quote is closed by 4b695edf, which is released in 1.12.1.\"\n  },\n  \"verdict_basis\": \"The defect is a real human-origin incomplete mitigation. The escaping content carries a named human identity on every candidate BIC object and no AI marker in the fully enumerated local object set, so the causal change is NOT_AI, not AI_ROOT_CAUSE and not AI_CODE_FLAWED.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/00-github.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"4d0d2e2dca4a528495a84f270645604082343149993fb27cb3214d62e56b3a87\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/prior-GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"32bbe452087dfe994e32398caac8b2378a374dae97bb335129ec2196b129a88e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/prior-GHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"dc09f724480afcc034a500f88b014d79b94a3e5cce570fb4782352bfe7de5249\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-fix-commit.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"69d69fe25c12125e7cd13d1f090db8662746234d1dbe0c1c07270cdd7d917ff0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-remediation-diffs.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"5adf7e4d926d5252ef3c9fb175361a0985ccbb4b281ccf4836ad26ce2cfb1667\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-parent-and-regex.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"a1aefccb79aa156aadfc214a6dd44ef18d3dbf451fd5922cda204a0e7a85d3aa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-object-enumeration.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"18de70730af6f403e439a3e52e0609230060b35acc90f1d2081e2ba1f1b5e015\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-ai-marker-scan.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"a2a5a6e9f3cdeb1554709751446d29094a458276aef686473919256f6f5d662d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-releases.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"8bfe9fac9a7598b5c7823e10cb392e47f8470d6998e1b70a7a41008b0989bb3d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"evidence/receipt-prior-advisories.txt\",\n      \"sha256\": \"926b5a729574ec0c31f67c965f28c0eec635d16cc042eba643ee0f912cbc6c6c\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
