itative non-shallow clone of senchalabs/connect, followed through logger path moves and exact blob history, reaches parentless root b29880dc05eaa8fd72aff20e741dde5cdf98ccc6. No preceding atomic logger member or identified PR is supplied by that bounded history route. See origin-boundary and connect-history receipts.\",\n  \"flaw_origin\": {\n    \"sha\": \"b29880dc05eaa8fd72aff20e741dde5cdf98ccc6\",\n    \"repo\": \"senchalabs/connect\",\n    \"role\": \"earliest observed aggregate boundary, not proven atomic BIC\",\n    \"path\": \"filters/log.js\",\n    \"finding\": \"Direct concatenation of unescaped referer/user-agent inside quoted log fields.\"\n  },\n  \"candidate_set\": [\n    \"b29880dc05eaa8fd72aff20e741dde5cdf98ccc6\",\n    \"79622119370961349101f676965987320013835b\",\n    \"b3f5d9bdb388690dfae9c06ab966328f49b7982b\",\n    \"fbf93833186920cc39bb19b247e4a86b61bef4fe\"\n  ],\n  \"ai_marker\": {\n    \"state\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n222:## Submission\n249:Submission, research acceptance and publication are separate states in the batch index.\nrefutation of the keyed mechanism is a finding; apply its frozen verdict requirements\nwithout inventing an introduction for behavior that the evidence contradicts. Keep a\nfuture condition that would change a finding separate from an available unanswered\nquestion. Neither conditional scope nor a terminal route label closes unread work.\nIf the frozen schema cannot represent a supported finding, retain it in the report and\nidentify the representation conflict for the leader. Do not invent causal roles or turn\nthat contract limitation into uncertainty about an already answered mechanism.\nFor current-contract false positives, use its explicit not-applicable nulls and\naffirmative grounds. Check the keyed advisory's status against its aliases; a\nwithdrawn alias does not dispose of an otherwise live vulnerability cluster.\n\n## Deliver a coherent synthesis\n\nWrite the final account, records and decisions together. Use the frozen schema's causal\nroles and unknown representations: metadata alone cannot establish atomicity, a missing\nmarker cannot establish no AI, and an unproved repair is not an unreadable or nonexistent\nfix. Preserve observed objects in evidence without inventing their roles.\n\nRead the completed files back and reconcile their material qualifications. Replace\nsuperseded assertions and answered next-question fields throughout the current synthesis,\nrecords and worklist, preserving original auditor artifacts unchanged. A contradictory\naddendum is not a correction. Verify execution claims against raw results or the original\ntrace. A successful process exit, an older valid skeleton or a failed wait does not prove\nthe completed research was written. Preserve original failures, reject duplicate JSON\nkeys and keep execution, input completeness and causal uncertainty distinct.\nKeep release qualifications in the structured fields as well as the report. A source-tag\ncomparison and a registry upload timestamp do not establish the contents of that uploaded\npackage; verify its bytes or retain the narrower source-release finding throughout.\n\nRun the frozen record checks and reduction gate on the final bytes with the original\nmanifest and every assigned lane. Keep raw results and hashes outside the checked files;\nretain failed runs and label corrected runs. Never choose a smaller successful subset to\nclaim whole-batch acceptance. Changed findings require renewed review of the affected\ndecisions, not merely refreshed hashes.\n\nHand the leader the final case/task identity, report/record/decision paths, decisive\n{\n  \"ghsa_id\": \"GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-87859\",\n  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"summary\": \"morgan vulnerable to Log Injection via unescaped double quote in quoted log fields\",\n  \"description\": \"### Impact\\n\\nMorgan writes attacker-controlled request data to the access log. Its escaping (added in 1.11.0 and 1.12.0) neutralizes control characters, the Unicode line separators, and backslash, but not the double quote (`0x22`), which is the field delimiter of the Apache combined log format morgan emits. An attacker who controls a quoted field (`:user-agent`, `:referrer`, the request URL, or the Basic auth `:remote-user`) can inject a double quote to close the field early and forge additional fields in the log record. The `combined`, `common`, and `default` formats, and any custom format that quotes a token, are affected. This is an incomplete fix of CVE-2026-5078 and CVE-2026-15603.\\n\\n### Patches\\n\\nUsers should upgrade to version 1.12.1.\\n\\n### Workarounds\\n\\nUpdate to version 1.12.1.\",\n  \"type\": \"reviewed\",\n  \"severity\": \"medium\",\n  \"repository_advisory_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/expressjs/morgan/security-advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n  \"source_code_location\": \"https://github.com/expressjs/morgan\",\n  \"identifiers\": [\n    {\n      \"value\": \"GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n      \"type\": \"GHSA\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"value\": \"CVE-2026-87859\",\n      \"type\": \"CVE\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    \"https://github.com/expressjs/morgan/security/advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\",\n    \"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-87859\",\n    \"https://github.com/expressjs/morgan/commit/4b695edf967ce179cdf4009fe8cddd184b7511ee\",\n    \"https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\",\n    \"https://github.com/expressjs/morgan/releases/tag/1.12.1\",\n    \"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4\"\n  ],\n  \"published_at\": \"2026-09-28T21:33:08Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-28T21:33:10Z\",\n  \"github_reviewed_at\": \"2026-09-28T21:33:08Z\",\n  \"nvd_published_at\": \"2026-09-11T10:16:53Z\",\n  \"withdrawn_at\": null,\n  \"vulnerabilities\": [\n    {\n      \"package\": {\n        \"ecosystem\": \"npm\",\n        \"name\": \"morgan\"\n      },\n      \"vulnerable_version_range\": \"< 1.12.1\",\n      \"first_patched_version\": \"1.12.1\",\n      \"vulnerable_functions\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cvss_severities\": {\n    \"cvss_v3\": {\n      \"vector_string\": \"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N\",\n      \"score\": 5.3\n    },\n    \"cvss_v4\": {\n      \"vector_string\": null,\n      \"score\": 0.0\n    }\n  },\n  \"cwes\": [\n    {\n      \"cwe_id\": \"CWE-117\",\n      \"name\": \"Improper Output Neutralization for Logs\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"credits\": [\n    {\n      \"user\": {\n        \"login\": \"iRevivalx\",\n        \"id\": 55530196,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NTMwMTk2\",\n        \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55530196?v=4\",\n        \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx\",\n        \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/iRevivalx\",\n        \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/followers\",\n        \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/following{/other_user}\",\n        \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/gists{/gist_id}\",\n        \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n        \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/subscriptions\",\n        \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/orgs\",\n        \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/repos\",\n        \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/events{/privacy}\",\n        \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/iRevivalx/received_events\",\n        \"type\": \"User\",\n        \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n        \"site_admin\": false\n      },\n      \"type\": \"finder\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"user\": {\n        \"login\": \"UlisesGascon\",\n        \"id\": 5110813,\n        \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTA4MTM=