gned limits. Do not turn\nit into a researched gap or completed independent audit. An actual EVIDENCE_GAP names\nthe evidence sought, bounded probes/results and the next decisive question.\nSubmission, research acceptance and publication are separate states in the batch index.\n\nFor new batches adopting the research-work sidecar introduced in `2026-09-25.1`, bind the schema's\n[research-work contract](../docs/DATA-SCHEMA.md#research-work-contract) and invoke the\nreduction gate with `--research-contract causal-work-v1`. Its `research_work.worklist`\nincludes unfinished qualified conclusions as well as unresolved ones. Review\n2:\"\"\"Check a reducer's evidence-backed decisions against exact input/output bytes.\n16:from compare_slots import RESEARCH_FIELDS, lane_paths, load_snapshot, research_differences_many\n25:def text(value) -> bool:\n29:def check_research_work(research, label, receipt):\n33:    if not isinstance(research, dict):\n34:        return [f'{label}: research needs an object'], counts, worklist, boundaries\n35:    if set(research) != set(WORK_DIMENSIONS):\n36:        problems.append(f'{label}: research needs exactly {list(WORK_DIMENSIONS)}')\n38:    def evidence(value, where):\n40:            problems.append(f'{where}: needs retained evidence receipts')\n46:        if dimension not in research:\n48:        detail = research[dimension]\n49:        where = f'{label} research {dimension}'\n53:        grade, state = detail.get('evidence_grade'), detail.get('work_state')\n55:            problems.append(f'{where}: invalid evidence_grade')\n60:        evidence(detail.get('evidence'), where)\n79:            identity = tuple(route.get(key) for key in ('question', 'source', 'evidence_type'))\n81:                problems.append(f'{where} route {route_id}: needs question, source and evidence_type')\n85:                    problems.append(f'{where}: duplicate evidence route {route_id}')\n95:                evidence(route.get('evidence'), f'{where} route {route_id}')\n104:                    problems.append(f'{where}: an unbound COMPLETE finding needs a recorded evidence frontier')\n113:def digest(path: Path) -> str:\n117:def manifest_ids(path: Path) -> set[str]:\n131:def check_delivery(manifest: Path, accepted: Path, decisions: Path,\n134:                   research_contract: str | None = None) -> dict:\n146:    def receipt(value, label):\n170:    pins = index.get('pins')\n171:    if not isinstance(pins, dict):\n172:        pins = {}\n173:    for role in sorted(set(PIN_ROLES) | set(pins)):\n174:        receipt(pins.get(role), f'pin {role}')\n179:        pin = pins.get(role)\n192:    contract = index.get('research_contract')\n196:        problems.append('decisions: keep frozen research decisions separate from the mutable dispatch index')\n197:    if research_contract is not None and contract != research_contract:\n198:        problems.append('research_contract: missing or different from the explicitly required contract')\n200:        problems.append(f'research_contract: unsupported version {contract!r}')\n201:    if research_contract is not None and research_contract != RESEARCH_CONTRACT:\n202:        problems.append(f'research_contract: unsupported required version {research_contract!r}')\n203:    if contract is None and any(isinstance(case, dict) and 'research' in case for case in cases.values()):\n204:        problems.append('research_contract: research objects require explicit contract adoption')\n217:            errors, dimension_counts, pending, limited = check_research_work(\n218:                decision.get('research') if isinstance(decision, dict) else None, cid, receipt)\n226:                problems.append(f'{cid}: ACCEPTED contradicts unfinished research')\n249:            problems.append(f'{cid}: research remains BLOCKED')\n253:            problems.append(f'{cid}: an open verdict cannot be research ACCEPTED')\n256:        reviewed = decision.get('reviewed_dimensions')\n258:            problems.append(f'{cid}: explicitly review every research dimension')\n259:        required = set(research_differences_many({**inputs, 'accepted': final}))\n261:        # Agreement does not waive primary-evidence scrutiny on publication-sensitive claims.\n268:        resolutions = decision.get('resolutions')\n269:        if not isinstance(resolutions, dict):\n270:            resolutions = {}\n272:            required.update(resolutions)\n274:            resolution = resolutions.get(dimension)\n285:                if not isinstance(resolution.get('evidence'), list) or not resolution['evidence']:\n288:                    for item in resolution['evidence']:\n289:                        receipt(item, f'{cid} {dimension} resolution evidence')\n291:                problems.append(f'{cid}: unresolved {dimension}; explain the competing readings and evidence')\n292:        evidence = decision.get('evidence')\n293:        if not isinstance(evidence, list) or not evidence:\n294:            problems.append(f'{cid}: retain primary evidence receipts')\n296:            for item in evidence:\n297:                receipt(item, f'{cid} evidence')\n311:    return {'cases': len(expected), 'auditors': list(paths), 'research_status': dict(counts),\n312:            'research_work': {'contract': contract, 'checked': contract == RESEARCH_CONTRACT,\n314:                              'worklist': worklist, 'evidence_boundaries': boundaries,\n322:def main() -> int:\n329:    parser.add_argument('--research-contract', choices=[RESEARCH_CONTRACT],\n330:                        help='require the explicitly adopted research-work contract')\n335:                                research_contract=args.research_contract)\n18:  python3 scripts/audit_record_gates.py --strict --repo /path/to/clone RECORD.json\n20:--repo checks quoted commit markers and recorded parent links against local Git\n35:CLOSED = {\"NOT_AI\", \"FALSE_POSITIVE\"} | AI_VERDICTS\n36:OPEN = {\"EVIDENCE_GAP\", \"BLOCKED\"}\n69:# The step-4 NOT_AI threshold: a recovered named human or organization identity\n70:# on the BIC object. Everything else there is EVIDENCE_GAP.\n82:# stays EVIDENCE_GAP under step 4 rather than carrying a NOT_AI verdict.\n129:def judgment_text(record: dict) -> str:\n140:def denied_around(text: str, start: int, end: int) -> bool:\n148:def claimed_disclosure(text: str) -> str:\n157:def residual_denied(record: dict) -> bool:\n180:def official_ids(record: dict) -> list[str]:\n189:def sha_list(value) -> list[str]:\n201:def check_record(record: dict) -> list[str]:\n231:    intro = record.get(\"introducer_sha\")\n236:        verdict == \"NOT_AI\"\n238:        and record.get(\"introducer_parent\") is None\n239:        and record.get(\"introducer_parent_absent\") is True\n244:            f\"{cid}: closed {verdict} requires a 40-hex introducer_sha \"\n270:def check_jsonl(path: Path) -> list[str]:\n274:def check_record_strict(record: dict) -> list[str]:\n284:    def need(key: str) -> str:\n307:            open_gap and record.get(\"introducer_sha\") is None\n330:            if record.get(\"introducer_sha\") is not None:\n332:                    f\"{cid}: strict: NON_GIT_BOUNDARY requires introducer_sha null\"\n336:            intro = str(record.get(\"introducer_sha\") or \"\").lower()\n339:                    f\"{cid}: strict: introducer_sha is its own landing commit, \"\n429:            \"introducer_sha (the AI-attributed change is the BIC; record the human \"\n430:            \"origin in flaw_origin, not as introducer_sha)\"\n432:    if verdict == \"NOT_AI\" and ai_on_bic is True:\n433:        problems.append(f\"{cid}: strict: NOT_AI contradicts ai_on_bic true\")\n435:    if verdict == \"NOT_AI\":\n441:                f\"{cid}: strict: NOT_AI requires identity_class one of \"\n446:                f\"{cid}: strict: NOT_AI needs a recovered named identity on the BIC \"\n447:                f\"object; {identity} is EVIDENCE_GAP (step 4)\"\n452:                f\"{cid}: strict: NOT_AI requires the repo's disclosure convention at \"\n473:        # A refuted or excluded allegation has no causal introducer or repair.\n475:        for key in (\"introducer_sha\", \"bic_granularity\", \"fix_sha\", \"fix_granularity\"):\n478:        for key in (\"introducer_parent\", \"landing_commit\", \"decomposed_shas\", \"direct_fix_sha\", \"atomic_repair_sha\", \"fix_shas\", \"minimum_fix_set\"):\n552:def review_signals(record: dict) -> list[str]:\n592:def load_record(text: str) -> dict:\n594:    def unique_pairs(pairs):\n608:def check_git_evidence(record: dict, repo: Path) -> list[str]:\n615:    def read_commit(sha):\n623:                [\"git\", \"--no-replace-objects\", \"-C\", str(repo), \"cat-file\", \"--batch\"],\n633:            problems.append(f\"{cid}: git: commit {sha} unavailable in {repo}; recover evidence or record the gap\")\n642:    intro = record.get(\"introducer_sha\")\n645:        parent = record.get(\"introducer_parent\")\n649:                problems.append(f\"{cid}: git: introducer_parent is not a parent of {intro}\")\n688:def check_text(text: str, strict: bool = False, repo: Path | None = None) -> list[str]:\n696:    if repo is not None:\n697:        problems += check_git_evidence(record, repo)\n701:def check_path(path: Path, strict: bool = False, repo: Path | None = None) -> list[str]:\n713:        problems.extend(f\"{source}: {item}\" for item in check_text(text, strict, repo))\n717:def main() -> int:\n721:    parser.add_argument(\"--repo\", type=Path, help=\"verify commit marker quotes and parent links in this local clone (no fetch)\")\n732:        problems.extend(check_text(sys.stdin.read(), args.strict, args.repo))\n734:        problems.extend(check_path(path, args.strict, args.repo))\nAI marker scan over ALL local commit objects (428 commits):\n$ git cat-file --batch-all-objects --batch-check | awk '$2==\"commit\"' | while read h; do git cat-file commit $h | grep -iE 'claude|copilot|cursor|codex|chatgpt|gpt-?[45]|gemini|devin|aider|windsurf|evomap|generated with|co-authored-by'; done\n== 286b000228cacba362bfa89791c6268663f86610\nCo-authored-by: EvoX <evox@evomap.ai>\nvar logger;\n\nmodule.exports = {\n    \n    // Default to sys.debug, but allow it to be overridden\n    setup: function (env, customLogger) {\n        logger = customLogger || require('sys').debug;\n    },\n\n    handle: function (req, res, next) {\n    \n        // Proxy writeHead to get the status Code out of it\n        var writeHead = res.writeHead;\n        var statusCode;\n        var resHeaders;\n        res.writeHead = function (code, headers) {\n            statusCode = code;\n            resHeaders = headers;\n            return writeHead.call(res, code, headers);\n        };\n\n        // Proxy end to output a line to the provided logger\n        var end = res.end;\n        res.end = function () {\n            // Common Log Format (mostly)\n            logger((req.socket && req.socket.remoteAddress)\n             + \" - - [\" + (new Date).toUTCString() + \"]\" \n             + \" \\\"\" + req.method + \" \" + req.url.pathname\n             + \" HTTP/\" + req.httpVersionMajor + \".\" + req.httpVersionMinor + \"\\\" \"\n             + statusCode + \" \" + (resHeaders[\"Content-Length\"] || \"-\") + \" \\\"\"\n             + (req.headers['referer'] || \"\") + \"\\\" \\\"\" \n             + (req.headers[\"user-agent\"] ? req.headers[\"user-agent\"] : '') + \"\\\"\");\n\n            return end.apply(res, arguments);\n        };\n    \n        // Punt to the next item in the chain\n        next(req, res);\n    }\n\n};\ntree 04a1d2477ac7a9747a76bdadefbbfb4cfaa50925\nauthor Tim Caswell <tim@creationix.com> 1274901258 -0700\ncommitter Tim Caswell <tim@creationix.com> 1274901258 -0700\n\nInitial commit\nafa25934e9d5c1ee04f8613909c40cd9954d1e4e 16a4aa43749a72e0e1f64eb8ad5122bd040c20a8 Added log filter tests\n5241490a82b5a52567d1d1e809a8c4219fba7757 a9415688e4195dea39ce6c0e39592700220c864b Nest framework within lib/connect\nb5dae604f686f0e97efb284999be6149f3341a05 b2