{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1 apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: output/alias-348fd55a42f6b70e3521be0e/REPORT.md\n+# Adjudication: alias-348fd55a42f6b70e3521be0e\n+\n+Task: incremental-causal-20261004-case-048-adjudicator, independent attempt 1.\n+Binding: 1a07e9835ff1f19eb0af2b80252a59cfc3e1d4af4e85e5d3767719d425308e1a.\n+Recipient: incremental-causal-20261004T081300Z-lead; research handoff only.\n+Frozen protocol 2026-09-27.3 and causal-work-v1. Original N=2 is retained.\n+Manifest SHA256: ddc825b20aa5c55daad781b13219699cfd7752df9dea0cca9a867dae806e2a6b.\n+\n+## Finding\n+\n+The vulnerability and shipped correction are supported. Contribution-level classification is EVIDENCE_GAP and the decision is BLOCKED. The quote-delimiter defect is already present in Connect's 2010 multi-subsystem root, and Morgan's 2014 import exactly copies older Connect logger bytes. The available source history does not recover the original atomic logger contribution or its immediate predecessor/provenance. Neither later human hardening nor named authors of aggregate carriers closes that gap. No admissible contribution-specific AI participation was established in the inspected sources.\n+\n+Auditor1's open classification is better supported than auditor2's NOT_AI. This is an independently checked causal synthesis, not acceptance by vote. Auditor2 misplaces the BIC at a later hardening, conflates an import with pre-VCS origin, overstates built-in format coverage, treats prior distinct advisories as aliases, and promotes an ambiguous later CI coauthor trailer into a disclosure convention. The successful fix and release findings survive those corrections.\n+\n+## Input integrity and observation scope\n+\n+Both complete reports, records, sidecars and their decisive receipts were examined. The copies' sealed inventories validate: auditor1 117 files, auditor2 14 files. Retained Connect and Morgan Git inventories each validate all 27 listed files. The full local Git object stores pass fsck and are non-shallow. Original record paths are used for the comparison and reduction gate; their exact hashes, reports, sidecars and seals are pinned in decisions.json. Auditor2's temporary clone is not retained; this is not evidence that its past observations failed. Independent checks use retained auditor1 primary Git bytes, without adopting that auditor's judgments.\n+\n+Receipt: receipts/input-integrity.json; receipts/original-inputs.json; receipts/morgan-fsck.* and connect-fsck.*; copied original source receipts under primary/auditor1 and primary/auditor2. All shared Git reads have GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 and GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0. Commands inherit node-1 affinity; shell entry commands use numactl --cpunodebind=1 --membind=1.\n+\n+The fixed coverage cutoff is 2026-10-04T08:13:00Z. The retained GHSA is the starting in-window evidence, extracted later with its source identity recorded in inputs/SOURCES.json. Auditor fetches and this adjudicator's additional retrievals occur after cutoff. Source dates for the mechanism, repair and release precede cutoff; later retrieval does not expand the original coverage window. No later-dated causal change is needed for this conclusion. Current empty public API associations/comments do not prove they were empty at the cutoff.\n+\n+## Advisory identity\n+\n+The accepted record is keyed to CVE-2026-87859. The retained CVE response matches that identifier and has cveMetadata.state PUBLISHED, dated 2026-09-11. Matching global GHSA-9f6g-j8ch-79g4 has published_at 2026-09-28T21:33:08Z and explicit withdrawn_at null. Both normalize to ACTIVE. Reviewed status and publication state are separate. Neither is rejected or withdrawn.\n+\n+The earlier GHSA-4vj7-5mj6-jm8m/CVE-2026-5078 and GHSA-jxfw-x594-9x9m/CVE-2026-15603 describe prior line-oriented escaping problems. They are historical related consultations, not aliases of this quote-delimiter advisory; their lifecycle cannot establish this keyed CVE's lifecycle. Auditor2's six-entry alias list is corrected to the two actual aliases.\n+\n+The CVE explicitly limits impact to within-record field interpretation. It describes changed built-in recorded values and status forgery in a custom format putting attacker-controlled quoted text before a server-controlled field; no newline is injected and record separation remains intact. Receipts: primary/advisory-retained.json, primary/auditor1/receipts/cve.out and its URL/capture/exit receipt, primary/auditor2/evidence/prior-*.json.\n+\n+## Actual caller, authority, representation and recipient\n+\n+At repair parent 0f74eca337508e006052a0ae48fb2754c076ec76, middleware selects a built-in/string format via getFormatFunction/compile or accepts an application format function. logRequest executes immediately or after onFinished, may be suppressed by skip, and writes the result plus newline to configured stream/stdout. Object-mode custom output is a separate path. The protected asset is downstream access-log interpretation, not template execution.\n+\n+User-Agent and Referer/referrer callbacks return request headers directly. URL returns originalUrl or url without percent decoding. Basic-auth's credentials.name supplies remote-user without Morgan authenticating that identity. Registered callbacks pass through tokenValue; string results are escaped. compile JSON-escapes the application's format to construct JavaScript, then concatenates runtime token values. That template escaping does not neutralize log delimiters in those values.\n+\n+The parent helper neutralizes C0, DEL/C1, U+2028/U+2029 and backslash; it preserves double quote. combined/default quote the request field, referrer and user-agent. common has the quoted request field but no User-Agent/referrer. Built-in remote-user is unquoted. A quote-delimiter remote-user example requires a custom quoted format. URL exposure requires an actual quote